gy_sidebar" title="Template talk:History of technology sidebar"><abbr title="Discuss this template">t</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-edit"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Template:History_of_technology_sidebar" title="Special:EditPage/Template:History of technology sidebar"><abbr title="Edit this template">e</abbr></a></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwEg" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwEw" aria-labelledby="Paleolithic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Paleolithic">Paleolithic</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Paleolithic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt12" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwFA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Outline of prehistoric technology"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1368532237" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt13" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt12" id="mwFQ">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_prehistoric_technology" title="Outline of prehistoric technology">Outline of prehistoric technology</a></div>
<p id="mwFg">The dates listed in this section refer to the earliest evidence of an invention found and dated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaeology" title="Archaeology" id="mwFw">archaeologists</a> (or in a few cases, suggested by indirect evidence). Dates are often approximate and change as more research is done, reported and seen. Older examples of any given technology are often found. The locations listed are where the earliest solid evidence has been found, but for earlier inventions, there is little certainty about how close that is to where the invention took place.</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwGA" aria-labelledby="Lower_Paleolithic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Lower_Paleolithic">Lower Paleolithic</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Lower Paleolithic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwGQ">The Lower Palaeolithic period lasted over 3 million years, during which many human-like species <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_evolution" title="Human evolution" id="mwGg">evolved</a>, including, toward the end of this period, <i id="mwGw">Homo sapiens</i>. The original divergence between humans and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chimpanzee" title="Chimpanzee" id="mwHA">chimpanzees</a> occurred 13 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Year#SI_prefix_multipliers" title="Year" id="mwHQ">Mya</a>; however, interbreeding continued until as recently as 4 Mya, with the first species clearly belonging to the human (and not chimpanzee) lineage being <i id="mwHg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australopithecus_anamensis" title="Australopithecus anamensis" id="mwHw">Australopithecus anamensis</a></i>.  Some species are controversial among paleoanthropologists, who disagree on whether they are species on their own or not. Here <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_ergaster" title="Homo ergaster" id="mwIA">Homo ergaster</a> is included under <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_erectus" title="Homo erectus" id="mwIQ">Homo erectus</a>, while <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_rhodesiensis" title="Homo rhodesiensis" id="mwIg">Homo rhodesiensis</a> is included under <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_heidelbergensis" title="Homo heidelbergensis" id="mwIw">Homo heidelbergensis</a>.</p>

<p id="mwJA">During this period, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quaternary_glaciation" title="Quaternary glaciation" id="mwJQ">Quaternary glaciation</a> began (about 2.58 million years ago) and continues to today. It has been an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_age" title="Ice age" id="mwJg">ice age</a>, with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_glaciation" title="Timeline of glaciation" id="mwJw">cycles of 40–100,000 years</a> alternating between long, cold, more glaciated periods, and shorter, warmer periods – <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interglacial" title="Interglacial" id="mwKA">interglacial</a> episodes.</p>

<ul id="mwKQ"><li id="mwKg"><b id="mwKw">3.3 Mya – 2.6 Mya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_tool" title="Stone tool" id="mwLA">Stone tools</a> - found in modern-day <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenya" title="Kenya" id="mwLQ">Kenya</a> are older and only found on the archetype road. Ancient stone tools from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopia" title="Ethiopia" id="mwLg">Ethiopia</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oldowan" title="Oldowan" id="mwLw">Oldowan</a>) were hand-crafted by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australopithecus" title="Australopithecus" id="mwMA">Australopithecus</a> or related people.<sup about="#mwt17" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-de_Heinzelin_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"de Heinzelin"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-de_Heinzelin-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-de_Heinzelin-2" id="mwMQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt20" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Wikipedia_articles_needing_clarification_from_October_2023" about="#mwt14" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwOQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"explain","href":"./Template:Explain"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"October 2023"}},"i":0}}]}'/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template " style="margin-left:0.1em; white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt14" id="mwOg"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Please_clarify" title="Wikipedia:Please clarify"><span title="The text near this tag needs further explanation. (October 2023)">further explanation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></li>
<li id="mwOw"><b id="mwPA">1.76 Mya:</b> Advanced (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acheulean" title="Acheulean" id="mwPQ">Acheulean</a>) stone tools in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenya" title="Kenya" id="mwPg">Kenya</a> by <i id="mwPw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_erectus" title="Homo erectus" id="mwQA">Homo erectus</a></i><sup about="#mwt21" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwRQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRw">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwSQ"><b id="mwSg">1.75 Mya – 150 kya:</b> Varying estimates for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Origin_of_language" title="Origin of language" id="mwSw">origin of language</a><sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Uomini_e72693_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Uomini e72693"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Uomini_e72693-6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Uomini_e72693-6" id="mwTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Perreault_2012_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Perreault 2012"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Perreault_2012-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Perreault_2012-7" id="mwUA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUg">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwVA"><b id="mwVQ">1.5 Mya:</b> Earliest likely <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Control_of_fire_by_early_humans" title="Control of fire by early humans" id="mwVg">control of fire</a> by <i id="mwVw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_erectus" title="Homo erectus" id="mwWA">Homo Erectus</a></i><sup about="#mwt33" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-8" id="mwWQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt36" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Miller_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Miller"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Miller-9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Miller-9" id="mwXQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt39" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-James_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"James"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-James-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-James-10" id="mwYQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYw">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwZQ"><b id="mwZg">1.5 Mya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_tool" title="Bone tool" id="mwZw">Bone tools</a> in Africa by <i id="mwaA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_erectus" title="Homo erectus" id="mwaQ">Homo erectus</a></i> and/or <i id="mwag"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paranthropus_boisei" title="Paranthropus boisei" id="mwaw">Paranthropus boisei</a></i><sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbg">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt45" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}'><a href="#cite_note-12" id="mwcA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt48" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-13"}}'><a href="#cite_note-13" id="mwdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdg">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mweA"><b id="mweQ">1 Mya-780 Kya:</b>  <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooking" title="Cooking" id="mweg">Cooking</a> in Middle East by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_erectus" title="Homo erectus" id="mwew">Homo erectus</a> <sup about="#mwt51" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"}}'><a href="#cite_note-14" id="mwfA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfg">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-15"}}'><a href="#cite_note-15" id="mwgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgg">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwhA"><b id="mwhQ">900 kya – 40 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raft" title="Raft" id="mwhg">Rafts</a><sup about="#mwt57" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Plakias2010_16-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Plakias2010"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Plakias2010-16"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Plakias2010-16" id="mwhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwiA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiQ">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwig">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt60" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17"}}'><a href="#cite_note-17" id="mwiw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjQ">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwjw"><b id="mwkA">500 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hafting" title="Hafting" id="mwkQ">Hafting</a> in South Africa by <i id="mwkg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_heidelbergensis" title="Homo heidelbergensis" id="mwkw">Homo heidelbergensis</a></i><sup about="#mwt63" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-18" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-18"}}'><a href="#cite_note-18" id="mwlA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlg">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwmA"><b id="mwmQ">500 kya – 450 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodworking" title="Woodworking" id="mwmg">Woodworking</a> construction in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zambia" title="Zambia" id="mwmw">Zambia</a> by <i id="mwnA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_heidelbergensis" title="Homo heidelbergensis" id="mwnQ">Homo heidelbergensis</a></i><sup about="#mwt66" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-19" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-19"}}'><a href="#cite_note-19" id="mwng"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoA">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoQ">]</span></span></a></sup> (The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_oldest_extant_buildings" title="List of oldest extant buildings" id="mwog">oldest known surviving buildings</a> are made from stone and date back no more than 9,500 years.<sup about="#mwt69" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-20"}}'><a href="#cite_note-20" id="mwow"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwpA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpQ">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpg">]</span></span></a></sup>)</li>
<li id="mwpw"><b id="mwqA">420 – 200 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_storage" title="Food storage" id="mwqQ">Food storage</a> in the form of uncracked bones saved for their marrow in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qesem_cave" title="Qesem cave" class="mw-redirect" id="mwqg">Qesem cave</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel" title="Israel" id="mwqw">Israel</a>.<sup about="#mwt72" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-21" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-21"}}'><a href="#cite_note-21" id="mwrA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrg">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwsA"><b id="mwsQ">400 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_hide_materials" title="History of hide materials" id="mwsg">Hide and leather</a>  clothing, footwear and shelter.<sup about="#mwt75" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-22" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-22"}}'><a href="#cite_note-22" id="mwsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtQ">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt78" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-23" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-23"}}'><a href="#cite_note-23" id="mwtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwuA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuQ">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwug">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwuw"><b id="mwvA">400 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pigment" title="Pigment" id="mwvQ">Pigments</a> in Zambia by <i id="mwvg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_heidelbergensis" title="Homo heidelbergensis" id="mwvw">Homo heidelbergensis</a></i><sup about="#mwt81" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-24" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-24" id="mwwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwg">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwww">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwxA"><b id="mwxQ">337 kya – 300 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schöningen_spears" title="Schöningen spears" id="mwxg">Schöningen</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spear" title="Spear" id="mwxw">Spears</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany" title="Germany" id="mwyA">Germany</a><sup about="#mwt82" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-25" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-25"}}'><a href="#cite_note-25" id="mwyQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyw">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt85" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-26" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26"}}'><a href="#cite_note-26" id="mwzQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzw">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt88" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-27" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-27"}}'><a href="#cite_note-27" id="mw0Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0w">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt91" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-28" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-28"}}'><a href="#cite_note-28" id="mw1Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1w">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt94" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-29" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-29"}}'><a href="#cite_note-29" id="mw2Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw2g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2w">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3A">]</span></span></a></sup> likely by <i id="mw3Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homo_heidelbergensis" title="Homo heidelbergensis" id="mw3g">Homo heidelbergensis</a></i> or early Neandarthals.<sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-30" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-30"}}'><a href="#cite_note-30" id="mw3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4Q">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-31"}}'><a href="#cite_note-31" id="mw4w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5Q">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5g">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mw5w"><b id="mw6A">320 kya:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade" title="Trade" id="mw6Q">trade</a> and long-distance (up to 50 miles) <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transportation" title="Transportation" class="mw-redirect" id="mw6g">transportation</a> of resources (e.g. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obsidian" title="Obsidian" id="mw6w">obsidian</a>), use of pigments, and possible making of projectile points in Kenya<sup about="#mwt103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NPR-593591796_32-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NPR-593591796"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NPR-593591796-32"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NPR-593591796-32" id="mw7A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw7Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7g">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-The_Atlantic-555674_33-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"The Atlantic-555674"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-The_Atlantic-555674-33"}}'><a href="#cite_note-The_Atlantic-555674-33" id="mw8A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8g">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt109" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Brooks_34-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Brooks"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Brooks-34"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Brooks-34" id="mw9A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9g">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9w">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mw-A" aria-labelledby="Middle_Paleolithic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Middle_Paleolithic">Middle Paleolithic</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Middle Paleolithic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw-Q">The evolution of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Early_modern_humans" title="Early modern humans" class="mw-redirect" id="mw-g">early modern humans</a> around 300 kya coincides with the start of the Middle Paleolithic period. During this 250,000-year period, our related <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archaic_humans" title="Archaic humans" class="mw-redirect" id="mw-w">archaic humans</a> such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neanderthals" title="Neanderthals" class="mw-redirect" id="mw_A">Neanderthals</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denisovans" title="Denisovans" class="mw-redirect" id="mw_Q">Denisovans</a> began to spread out of Africa, joined later by <i id="mw_g">Homo sapiens</i>. Over the course of the period we see evidence of increasingly long-distance trade, religious rites, and other behavior associated with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Behavioral_modernity" title="Behavioral modernity" id="mw_w">Behavioral modernity</a>.</p>
<ul id="mwAQA"><li id="mwAQE"><b id="mwAQI">279 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hafting" title="Hafting" id="mwAQM">Hafting</a> and early stone-tipped projectile weapons in Ethiopia<sup about="#mwt112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SahlePLOS1_35-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"SahlePLOS1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-SahlePLOS1-35"}}'><a href="#cite_note-SahlePLOS1-35" id="mwAQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQY">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAQg"><b id="mwAQk">200 kya:</b> Simple glue (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adhesive" title="Adhesive" id="mwAQo">adhesive</a>) made of one kind of material, birch tar, in Central Italy by Neanderthals.<sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mwAQs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ0">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAQ8"><b id="mwARA">200 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bed" title="Bed" id="mwARE">Beds</a> in South Africa.<sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-37" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-37" id="mwARI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARQ">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt121" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38"}}'><a href="#cite_note-38" id="mwARY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARg">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt124" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-39" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-39"}}'><a href="#cite_note-39" id="mwARo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARw">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAR4"><b id="mwAR8">170 kya – 90 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_clothing_and_textiles" title="History of clothing and textiles" id="mwASA">Clothing</a>, among anatomically modern humans in Africa. Genetic evidence from body lice suggests a range of dates centering over 100 thousand years ago.<sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-40" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-40"}}'><a href="#cite_note-40" id="mwASE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASM">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_tool" title="Bone tool" id="mwASU">bone scrapers</a> appropriate for scraping hides to make supple leather were found in Morocco dating to 90–120,000 years ago.<sup about="#mwt130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-41" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-41"}}'><a href="#cite_note-41" id="mwASY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASg">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TG-20210916_42-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TG-20210916"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TG-20210916-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TG-20210916-42" id="mwASo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASw">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAS4"><b id="mwAS8">164 kya – 47 kya:</b> Heat treating of stone blades in South Africa.<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-43" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-43" id="mwATA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATI">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwATQ"><b id="mwATU">135 kya – 100 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bead" title="Bead" id="mwATY">Beads</a> in Israel and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algeria" title="Algeria" id="mwATc">Algeria</a><sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwATg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATo">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATs">]</span></span></a></sup> — implying string or thread</li>
<li id="mwATw"><b id="mwAT0">100 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blombos_Cave#Ochre_processing_workshop" title="Blombos Cave" id="mwAT4">Ochre processed</a>, and compound <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paint" title="Paint" id="mwAT8">paints</a> made in South Africa<sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bbc.com-15257259_45-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bbc.com-15257259"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-bbc.com-15257259-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bbc.com-15257259-45" id="mwAUA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUI">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Washington_Post-2011/10/12/gIQApyHrhL_46-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Washington Post-2011/10/12/gIQApyHrhL"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Washington_Post-2011/10/12/gIQApyHrhL-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Washington_Post-2011/10/12/gIQApyHrhL-46" id="mwAUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUY">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Henshilwood_et_al._2011_47-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Henshilwood et al. 2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Henshilwood_et_al._2011-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Henshilwood_et_al._2011-47" id="mwAUg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUo">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAUw"><b id="mwAU0">100 kya:</b> Funerals (in the form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burial" title="Burial" id="mwAU4">burial</a>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skhul_Cave" title="Skhul Cave" id="mwAU8">Skhul Cave</a>, Israel<sup about="#mwt151" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-lieberman2_48-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"lieberman2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-lieberman2-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-lieberman2-48" id="mwAVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVI">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAVQ"><b id="mwAVU">90 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harpoon" title="Harpoon" id="mwAVY">Harpoons</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo" title="Democratic Republic of the Congo" id="mwAVc">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a>.<sup about="#mwt154" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAVg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVo">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAVw"><b id="mwAV0">70 kya – 60 kya</b> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sibudu_Cave" title="Sibudu Cave" id="mwAV4">Sibudu Cave</a> in South Africa by <i id="mwAV8">Homo sapiens</i>:
<ul id="mwAWA"><li id="mwAWE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adhesive" title="Adhesive" id="mwAWI">Compound adhesives</a><sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wadley_50-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wadley"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Wadley-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Wadley-50" id="mwAWM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWU">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAWc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWk">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAWs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrow" title="Arrow" id="mwAWw">Arrows</a> and other evidence of bow-and-arrow technology<sup about="#mwt163" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Lombard_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Lombard"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lombard-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Lombard-52" id="mwAW0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAW4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW8">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt166" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Lombard_M_53-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Lombard M"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lombard_M-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Lombard_M-53" id="mwAXE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXM">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt169" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Backwell2018_54-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Backwell2018"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Backwell2018-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Backwell2018-54" id="mwAXU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXc">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAXk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sewing_needle" title="Sewing needle" id="mwAXo">Sewing needle</a><sup about="#mwt172" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Backwell_55-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Backwell"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Backwell-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Backwell-55" id="mwAXs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX0">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt175" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAX8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYE">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYI">]</span></span></a></sup> (implying thread of some kind)</li></ul></li>
<li id="mwAYM"><b id="mwAYQ">62 kya – 61 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_painting" title="Cave painting" id="mwAYU">Cave painting</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spain" title="Spain" id="mwAYY">Spain</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neanderthal" title="Neanderthal" id="mwAYc">Neanderthal</a><sup about="#mwt178" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hoffmann2018_57-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hoffmann2018"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hoffmann2018-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hoffmann2018-57" id="mwAYg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYo">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAYw"><b id="mwAY0">59–49 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dentistry" title="Dentistry" id="mwAY4">Dentistry</a> in southwestern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberia" title="Siberia" id="mwAY8">Siberia</a>, by Neanderthals<sup about="#mwt181" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-58" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-58" id="mwAZA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZI">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt184" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwAZQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZY">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAZg"><b id="mwAZk">55.8–51.2 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Representation_(arts)" title="Representation (arts)" id="mwAZo">Representational</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narrative_art" title="Narrative art" id="mwAZs">Narrative art</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indonesia" title="Indonesia" id="mwAZw">Indonesia</a> by <i id="mwAZ0">Homo sapiens</i><sup about="#mwt187" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-60" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-60"}}'><a href="#cite_note-60" id="mwAZ4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZ8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaA">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaE">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwAaI" aria-labelledby="Upper_Paleolithic_to_Early_Mesolithic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Upper_Paleolithic_to_Early_Mesolithic">Upper Paleolithic to Early Mesolithic</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Upper Paleolithic to Early Mesolithic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAaM">50 kya was long regarded as the beginning of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Behavioral_modernity" title="Behavioral modernity" id="mwAaQ">behavioral modernity</a>, which defined the Upper Paleolithic period. The Upper Paleolithic lasted nearly 40,000 years, while research continues to push the beginnings of behavioral modernity earlier into the Middle Paleolithic. Behavioral modernity is characterized by the widespread observation of religious rites, artistic expression and the appearance of tools made for purely intellectual or artistic pursuits.</p>
<ul id="mwAaU"><li id="mwAaY"><b id="mwAac">49 kya – 30 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ground_stone" title="Ground stone" id="mwAag">Ground stone</a> tools – fragments of an axe in Australia date to 49–45 ka, more appear in Japan closer to 30 ka, and elsewhere closer to the Neolithic.<sup about="#mwt190" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwAak"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAao"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAas">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt193" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwAa0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAa4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAa8">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAbE"><b id="mwAbI">47 kya:</b> The oldest-known mines in the world are from Eswatini, and extracted hematite for the production of the red pigment <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ochre" title="Ochre" id="mwAbM">ochre</a>.<sup about="#mwt196" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwAbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbY">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt199" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwAbg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbo">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAbw"><b id="mwAb0">45 kya – 9 kya:</b> Earliest evidence of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoe" title="Shoe" id="mwAb4">shoes</a>, suggested by changes in foot bone morphology in China by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tianyuan_man" title="Tianyuan man" id="mwAb8">Tianyuan man</a>.<sup about="#mwt202" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-65" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-65"}}'><a href="#cite_note-65" id="mwAcA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcI">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcM">]</span></span></a></sup> The earliest physical shoes found so far are bark <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandal" title="Sandal" id="mwAcQ">sandals</a> dated to 10 to 9 kya in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Rock_Cave" title="Fort Rock Cave" id="mwAcU">Fort Rock Cave</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" id="mwAcY">United States</a>.<sup about="#mwt205" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Connolly_Tom_66-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Connolly_Tom"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Connolly_Tom-66"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Connolly_Tom-66" id="mwAcc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAck">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAco">]</span></span></a></sup> The oldest known leather shoe dated to 5.5 kya was found in excellent condition in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Areni-1_cave" title="Areni-1 cave" id="mwAcs">Areni-1 cave</a> located in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vayots_Dzor" title="Vayots Dzor" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAcw">Vayots Dzor</a> province of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenia" title="Armenia" id="mwAc0">Armenia</a>.<sup about="#mwt208" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-National_Geographic_67-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"National Geographic"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-National_Geographic-67"}}'><a href="#cite_note-National_Geographic-67" id="mwAc4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAc8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdA">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAdI"><b id="mwAdM">44 kya – 42 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tally_stick" title="Tally stick" id="mwAdQ">Tally sticks</a> (see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lebombo_bone" title="Lebombo bone" id="mwAdU">Lebombo bone</a>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eswatini" title="Eswatini" id="mwAdY">Eswatini</a><sup about="#mwt211" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-68"}}'><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwAdc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdk">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAds"><b id="mwAdw">42 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flute" title="Flute" id="mwAd0">Flute</a> in Germany<sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-69"}}'><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwAd4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAd8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeA">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-70" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-70"}}'><a href="#cite_note-70" id="mwAeI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeQ">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAeY"><b id="mwAec">42-17.5 kya:</b> The oldest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spear-thrower" title="Spear-thrower" id="mwAeg">spear-thrower</a> (aka atlatl, woomera) found so far was in France, dated to 17.5 thousand years ago.<sup about="#mwt220" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-71" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-71"}}'><a href="#cite_note-71" id="mwAek"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAes">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAew">]</span></span></a></sup> Indirect evidence suggests 42 thousand years ago or longer, from study of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Mungo_remains" title="Lake Mungo remains" id="mwAe0">Mungo Man's</a> arthritis<sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-72"}}'><a href="#cite_note-72" id="mwAe4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAe8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfA">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAfI"><b id="mwAfM">37 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortar_and_pestle" title="Mortar and pestle" id="mwAfQ">Mortar and pestle</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwest_Asia" title="Southwest Asia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAfU">Southwest Asia</a><sup about="#mwt226" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-73" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-73"}}'><a href="#cite_note-73" id="mwAfY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfg">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAfo"><b id="mwAfs">32-28 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rope" title="Rope" id="mwAfw">Rope</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String_(structure)" title="String (structure)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAf0">Cords</a> for "hafting stone tools, weaving <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baskets" title="Baskets" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAf4">baskets</a>, or sewing garments," according to Elis Kvavadze et al.<sup about="#mwt229" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-74" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-74"}}'><a href="#cite_note-74" id="mwAf8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgE">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt232" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-75" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-75"}}'><a href="#cite_note-75" id="mwAgM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgU">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAgc"><b id="mwAgg">31 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amputation" title="Amputation" id="mwAgk">Amputation</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surgery" title="Surgery" id="mwAgo">surgery</a>.<sup about="#mwt235" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-76" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-76"}}'><a href="#cite_note-76" id="mwAgs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg0">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg4">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medicine" title="Medicine" id="mwAg8">Medicine</a> in a meaningful sense likely predates the human-chimpanzee split, as, for example, herbal medicine has been observed in other primates.<sup about="#mwt238" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-77" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-77"}}'><a href="#cite_note-77" id="mwAhA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhI">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAhQ"><b id="mwAhU">28 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceramics" title="Ceramics" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAhY">Ceramics</a> (direct evidence) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weaving" title="Weaving" id="mwAhc">weaving</a> (impressions left in the ceramics) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moravia" title="Moravia" id="mwAhg">Moravia</a><sup about="#mwt241" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-78" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-78"}}'><a href="#cite_note-78" id="mwAhk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAho"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhs">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt244" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-79"}}'><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwAh0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAh4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh8">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiA">]</span></span></a></sup> (Czech Republic) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgia_(country)" title="Georgia (country)" id="mwAiE">Georgia</a>. (The oldest piece of woven cloth found so far was in Çatalhöyük, Turkey and dated to about 9,000 years ago.<sup about="#mwt247" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-80" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-80"}}'><a href="#cite_note-80" id="mwAiI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiQ">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiU">]</span></span></a></sup>)</li>
<li id="mwAiY"><b id="mwAic">24 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus_of_Dolní_Věstonice" title="Venus of Dolní Věstonice" id="mwAig">Oldest known ceramic sculpture</a><sup about="#mwt250" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-81" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-81"}}'><a href="#cite_note-81" id="mwAik"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAio"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAis">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAi0"><b id="mwAi4">23 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestication_of_the_dog" title="Domestication of the dog" id="mwAi8">Domestication of the dog</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberia" title="Siberia" id="mwAjA">Siberia</a>.<sup about="#mwt253" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Perri2021_82-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Perri2021"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Perri2021-82"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Perri2021-82" id="mwAjE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjM">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAjU"><b id="mwAjY">22 – 17 kya</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bullroarer" title="Bullroarer" id="mwAjc">Bullroarer</a><sup about="#mwt256" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-83" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-83"}}'><a href="#cite_note-83" id="mwAjg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjo">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt259" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-84" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-84"}}'><a href="#cite_note-84" id="mwAjw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAj0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj4">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt260" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-85" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-85"}}'><a href="#cite_note-85" id="mwAkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkI">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAkQ"><b id="mwAkU">22 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish_hook" title="Fish hook" id="mwAkY">Fish hook</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okinawa_Island" title="Okinawa Island" id="mwAkc">Okinawa Island</a>, modern day Japan.<sup about="#mwt263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Price2016_86-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Price2016"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Price2016-86"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Price2016-86" id="mwAkg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAko">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAks">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt266" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-87" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-87"}}'><a href="#cite_note-87" id="mwAkw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAk0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk4">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAlA"><b id="mwAlE">21 – 3.7 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_chart" title="Star chart" id="mwAlI">Star chart</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France" title="France" id="mwAlM">France</a>,<sup about="#mwt270" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-88" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-88"}}'><a href="#cite_note-88" id="mwAlQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlY">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt273" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-89" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-89"}}'><a href="#cite_note-89" id="mwAlg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlo">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAls">]</span></span></a></sup> and later <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spain" title="Spain" id="mwAlw">Spain</a>,<sup about="#mwt276" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-90" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-90"}}'><a href="#cite_note-90" id="mwAl0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAl4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAl8">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmA">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_lacking_reliable_references" about="#mwt267" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAmE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Irrelevant citation","href":"./Template:Irrelevant_citation"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"September 2026"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_lacking_reliable_references_from_September_2026" about="#mwt267"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template " style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt267" id="mwAmI"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability" title="Wikipedia:Verifiability"><span title="Verification of this source citation failed to find it supporting or even relevant to the material that cites it (September 2026)">irrelevant citation</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kashmir" title="Kashmir" id="mwAmM">Kashmir</a>,<sup about="#mwt279" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-91" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-91"}}'><a href="#cite_note-91" id="mwAmQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmY">[</span>90<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmc">]</span></span></a></sup> Germany,<sup about="#mwt282" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-92" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-92"}}'><a href="#cite_note-92" id="mwAmg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmo">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAms">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt285" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-93" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-93"}}'><a href="#cite_note-93" id="mwAmw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAm0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm4">[</span>92<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm8">]</span></span></a></sup> and Egypt.<sup about="#mwt288" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-94" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-94"}}'><a href="#cite_note-94" id="mwAnA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnI">[</span>93<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAnQ"><b id="mwAnU">20 – 16 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pottery" title="Pottery" id="mwAnY">Pottery</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwAnc">China</a><sup about="#mwt291" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-95" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-95"}}'><a href="#cite_note-95" id="mwAng"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAno">[</span>94<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAns">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt294" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Science_96-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Science"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Science-96"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Science-96" id="mwAnw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAn0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn4">[</span>95<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt295" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-97" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-97"}}'><a href="#cite_note-97" id="mwAoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoI">[</span>96<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAoQ"><b id="mwAoU">14.5 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bread" title="Bread" id="mwAoY">Bread</a> in Jordan<sup about="#mwt298" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Briggs2018_98-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Briggs2018"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Briggs2018-98"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Briggs2018-98" id="mwAoc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAog"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAok">[</span>97<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt301" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Arranz-Otaegui_Gonzalez_Carretero_Ramsey_Fuller_p=201801071_99-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Arranz-Otaegui Gonzalez Carretero Ramsey Fuller p=201801071"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Arranz-Otaegui_Gonzalez_Carretero_Ramsey_Fuller_p=201801071-99"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Arranz-Otaegui_Gonzalez_Carretero_Ramsey_Fuller_p=201801071-99" id="mwAos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo0">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAo8"><b id="mwApA">12 kya:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spindle_whorl" title="Spindle whorl" id="mwApE">Spindle whorl</a>, also the oldest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheel" title="Wheel" id="mwApI">wheel</a>-like tool, at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nahal_Ein_Gev_II" title="Nahal Ein Gev II" id="mwApM">Nahal Ein Gev II</a>, Israel<sup about="#mwt304" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-100" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-100"}}'><a href="#cite_note-100" id="mwApQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApY">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt307" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-101" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-101"}}'><a href="#cite_note-101" id="mwApg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApo">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAps">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwApw" aria-labelledby="Agricultural_and_proto-agricultural_eras"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Agricultural_and_proto-agricultural_eras">Agricultural and proto-agricultural eras</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Agricultural and proto-agricultural eras"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAp0">The end of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Last_Glacial_Period" title="Last Glacial Period" id="mwAp4">Last Glacial Period</a> ("ice age") and the beginning of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holocene" title="Holocene" id="mwAp8">Holocene</a> around 11.7 ka coincide with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neolithic_Revolution" title="Neolithic Revolution" id="mwAqA">Agricultural Revolution</a>, marking the beginning of the agricultural era, which persisted there until the industrial revolution.<sup about="#mwt310" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-102" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-102"}}'><a href="#cite_note-102" id="mwAqE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqM">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwAqU" aria-labelledby="Neolithic_and_Late_Mesolithic"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Neolithic_and_Late_Mesolithic">Neolithic and Late Mesolithic</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Neolithic and Late Mesolithic"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt311" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAqY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Outline of prehistoric technology"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt312" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt311" id="mwAqc">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_prehistoric_technology" title="Outline of prehistoric technology">Outline of prehistoric technology</a></div>
<p id="mwAqg">During the Neolithic period, lasting 8400 years, stone began to be used for construction, and remained a predominant hard material for toolmaking. Copper and arsenic bronze were developed towards the end of this period, and of course the use of many softer materials such as wood, bone, and fibers continued. Domestication spread both in the sense of how many species were domesticated, and how widespread the practice became.</p>
<ul id="mwAqk"><li id="mwAqo"><b id="mwAqs">10,000 BC – 9000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agriculture" title="Agriculture" id="mwAqw">Agriculture</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fertile_Crescent" title="Fertile Crescent" id="mwAq0">Fertile Crescent</a><sup about="#mwt315" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-103" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-103"}}'><a href="#cite_note-103" id="mwAq4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArA">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt318" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-104" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-104"}}'><a href="#cite_note-104" id="mwArI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwArY"><b id="mwArc">10,000 BC – 9000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestication_of_the_sheep" title="Domestication of the sheep" id="mwArg">Domestication of sheep</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwest_Asia" title="Southwest Asia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwArk">Southwest Asia</a><sup about="#mwt321" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-105" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-105"}}'><a href="#cite_note-105" id="mwAro"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArw">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAr0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt324" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-storey_106-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"storey"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-storey-106"}}'><a href="#cite_note-storey-106" id="mwAr4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAr8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsA">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsE">]</span></span></a></sup> (followed shortly by pigs, goats and cattle)</li>
<li id="mwAsI"><b id="mwAsM">10,000 - 9000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethanol_fermentation#Alcoholic_beverages" title="Ethanol fermentation" id="mwAsQ">Alcohol fermentation</a> – specifically <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mead" title="Mead" id="mwAsU">mead</a>, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwest_Asia" title="Southwest Asia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAsY">Southwest Asia</a><sup about="#mwt327" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-107" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-107"}}'><a href="#cite_note-107" id="mwAsc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsk">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAso">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAss"><b id="mwAsw">9500 BC – 9000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_oldest_extant_buildings" title="List of oldest extant buildings" id="mwAs0">Oldest known surviving building</a> – <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Göbekli_Tepe" title="Göbekli Tepe" id="mwAs4">Göbekli Tepe</a>, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey" title="Turkey" id="mwAs8">Turkey</a><sup about="#mwt330" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-108" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-108"}}'><a href="#cite_note-108" id="mwAtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtI">[</span>107<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt333" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-109" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-109"}}'><a href="#cite_note-109" id="mwAtQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtY">[</span>108<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAtg"><b id="mwAtk">9000 BC – 6000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestication_of_rice" title="Domestication of rice" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAto">Domestication of rice</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwAts">China</a><sup about="#mwt336" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-110" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-110"}}'><a href="#cite_note-110" id="mwAtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAt0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt4">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAt8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAuA"><b id="mwAuE">9000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mudbrick" title="Mudbrick" id="mwAuI">Mudbricks</a> (unfired bricks), and clay <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortar_(masonry)" title="Mortar (masonry)" id="mwAuM">mortar</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jericho" title="Jericho" id="mwAuQ">Jericho</a>.<sup about="#mwt339" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-111" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-111"}}'><a href="#cite_note-111" id="mwAuU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuc">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAug">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt342" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_112-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-112"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-112" id="mwAuk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAus">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt345" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-113" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-113"}}'><a href="#cite_note-113" id="mwAu0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAu4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu8">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAvE"><b id="mwAvI">8400 BC:</b> Oldest known water <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Well" title="Well" id="mwAvM">well</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyprus" title="Cyprus" id="mwAvQ">Cyprus</a>.<sup about="#mwt348" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated2_114-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-autogenerated2-114"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated2-114" id="mwAvU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvc">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAvk"><b id="mwAvo">8040–7510 BC:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pesse_canoe" title="Pesse canoe" id="mwAvs">Pesse canoe</a> is the oldest boat we have found,<sup about="#mwt351" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-115" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-115"}}'><a href="#cite_note-115" id="mwAvw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAv0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAv4">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAv8">]</span></span></a></sup> while early human habitation of Crete and Australia make clear human seafaring goes back tens or hundreds of thousands of years. (see above)</li>
<li id="mwAwA"><b id="mwAwE">8000–7500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-city" title="Proto-city" id="mwAwI">Proto-city</a> – large permanent settlements, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tell_es-Sultan" title="Tell es-Sultan" id="mwAwM">Tell es-Sultan (Jericho)</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Çatalhöyük" title="Çatalhöyük" id="mwAwQ">Çatalhöyük</a>, Turkey.<sup about="#mwt354" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-116" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-116"}}'><a href="#cite_note-116" id="mwAwU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwc">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAwk"><b id="mwAwo">8000–5000 BC:</b> Domestication of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potatoes" title="Potatoes" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAws">potatoes</a>, in southern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peru" title="Peru" id="mwAww">Peru</a> and northwestern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolivia" title="Bolivia" id="mwAw0">Bolivia</a> by pre-Columbian farmers, around <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Titicaca" title="Lake Titicaca" id="mwAw4">Lake Titicaca</a>.<sup about="#mwt357" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-117" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-117"}}'><a href="#cite_note-117" id="mwAw8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxE">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt360" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-118" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-118"}}'><a href="#cite_note-118" id="mwAxM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxU">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt363" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-119" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-119"}}'><a href="#cite_note-119" id="mwAxc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxk">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAxs"><b id="mwAxw">7500–6500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalcolithic" title="Chalcolithic" id="mwAx0">Copper tools</a>, by the people of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Copper_Complex" title="Old Copper Complex" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAx4">Old Copper Complex</a> from the Great Lakes region of North America.<sup about="#mwt366" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-120" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-120"}}'><a href="#cite_note-120" id="mwAx8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyE">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt369" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-121" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-121"}}'><a href="#cite_note-121" id="mwAyM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyU">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt372" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-122" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-122"}}'><a href="#cite_note-122" id="mwAyc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyk">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAys"><b id="mwAyw">7000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sled_dog" title="Sled dog" id="mwAy0">Sled dog</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dog_sled" title="Dog sled" id="mwAy4">Dog sled</a>, in Siberia.<sup about="#mwt375" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-123"}}'><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwAy8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzE">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAzM"><b id="mwAzQ">6500 BC:</b> Evidence of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lead_smelting" title="Lead smelting" id="mwAzU">lead smelting</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Çatalhöyük" title="Çatalhöyük" id="mwAzY">Çatalhöyük</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turkey" title="Turkey" id="mwAzc">Turkey</a><sup about="#mwt378" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-124" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124"}}'><a href="#cite_note-124" id="mwAzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzo">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwAzw"><b id="mwAz0">6000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiln" title="Kiln" id="mwAz4">Kiln</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwAz8">Mesopotamia</a> (Iraq)<sup about="#mwt381" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bienkowski_125-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bienkowski"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bienkowski-125"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bienkowski-125" id="mwA0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0I">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA0Q"><b id="mwA0U">6th millennium BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irrigation" title="Irrigation" id="mwA0Y">Irrigation</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khuzestan_Province" title="Khuzestan Province" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA0c">Khuzistan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran" title="Iran" id="mwA0g">Iran</a><sup about="#mwt384" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-126" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-126"}}'><a href="#cite_note-126" id="mwA0k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0s">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt387" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-127" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-127"}}'><a href="#cite_note-127" id="mwA00"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA04"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA08">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA1E"><b id="mwA1I">6000 BC – 3200 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-writing" title="Proto-writing" id="mwA1M">Proto-writing</a> in present-day Egypt, Iraq, Romania, China, India and Pakistan.<sup about="#mwt390" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-128" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-128"}}'><a href="#cite_note-128" id="mwA1Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA1U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1Y">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA1c">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA1g"><b id="mwA1k">5900 – 5600 BC:</b> Oldest evidence of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_production" title="Salt production" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA1o">salt production</a> found in Southeastern Europe, in the countries of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moldova" title="Moldova" id="mwA1s">Moldova</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romania" title="Romania" id="mwA1w">Romania</a>.<sup about="#mwt393" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-129" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-129"}}'><a href="#cite_note-129" id="mwA10"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA14"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA18">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA2E"><b id="mwA2I">5500 – 5200 BC:</b> Oldest evidence of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese" title="Cheese" id="mwA2M">cheese</a> found, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poland" title="Poland" id="mwA2Q">Poland</a> and on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalmatia" title="Dalmatia" id="mwA2U">Dalmatian coast</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croatia" title="Croatia" id="mwA2Y">Croatia</a>.<sup about="#mwt397" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-130" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-130"}}'><a href="#cite_note-130" id="mwA2c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2k">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA2o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt400" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-131" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-131"}}'><a href="#cite_note-131" id="mwA2s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA2w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA20">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA24">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA28"><b id="mwA3A">5500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sailing" title="Sailing" id="mwA3E">Sailing</a> - pottery depictions of sail boats, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwA3I">Mesopotamia</a>,<sup about="#mwt403" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-132"}}'><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwA3M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3U">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3Y">]</span></span></a></sup> and later <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egypt" title="Ancient Egypt" id="mwA3c">ancient Egypt</a><sup about="#mwt406" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-133" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-133"}}'><a href="#cite_note-133" id="mwA3g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA3k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3o">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA3s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt407" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-johnstone_134-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"johnstone"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-johnstone-134"}}'><a href="#cite_note-johnstone-134" id="mwA3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA30"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA34">[</span>133<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA38">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA4A"><b id="mwA4E">5000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smelting#Copper_and_bronze" title="Smelting" id="mwA4I">Copper smelting</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbia" title="Serbia" id="mwA4M">Serbia</a>.<sup about="#mwt410" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-135" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-135"}}'><a href="#cite_note-135" id="mwA4Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA4U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4Y">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4c">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt413" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-136" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-136"}}'><a href="#cite_note-136" id="mwA4g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA4k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4o">[</span>135<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA4s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA4w"><b id="mwA40">5000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seawall" title="Seawall" id="mwA44">Seawall</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tel_Hreiz?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Tel Hreiz (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwA48" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Tel Hreiz"]}}'>Tel Hareiz</a>, near Haifa, Israel.<sup about="#mwt416" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-137" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-137"}}'><a href="#cite_note-137" id="mwA5A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5I">[</span>136<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA5Q"><b id="mwA5U">5th millennium BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lacquer" title="Lacquer" id="mwA5Y">Lacquer</a> in China<sup about="#mwt419" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-138" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138"}}'><a href="#cite_note-138" id="mwA5c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5k">[</span>137<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt420" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-139" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139"}}'><a href="#cite_note-139" id="mwA5s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA50">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA54">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA58"><b id="mwA6A">5000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton" title="Cotton" id="mwA6E">Cotton</a> thread, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mehrgarh" title="Mehrgarh" id="mwA6I">Mehrgarh</a>, Indus Valley, connecting the copper beads of a bracelet.<sup about="#mwt423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Mithen2006_140-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Mithen2006"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mithen2006-140"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Mithen2006-140" id="mwA6M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6U">[</span>139<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt426" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-141" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-141"}}'><a href="#cite_note-141" id="mwA6c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6k">[</span>140<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt429" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-JIAPAN2018_142-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"JIAPAN2018"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-JIAPAN2018-142"}}'><a href="#cite_note-JIAPAN2018-142" id="mwA6s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA60">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA64">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA68"><b id="mwA7A">5000 BC – 4500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oar" title="Oar" id="mwA7E">Rowing oars</a> in China<sup about="#mwt432" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-143" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-143"}}'><a href="#cite_note-143" id="mwA7I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA7M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7Q">[</span>142<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7U">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt435" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Stark_144-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Stark"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Stark-144"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Stark-144" id="mwA7Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA7c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7g">[</span>143<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7k">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA7o"><b id="mwA7s">4500 BC – 3500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost-wax_casting" title="Lost-wax casting" id="mwA7w">Lost-wax casting</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestine" title="Palestine" id="mwA70">Palestine</a><sup about="#mwt439" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Muhly_145-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Muhly"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Muhly-145"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Muhly-145" id="mwA74"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA78"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8A">[</span>144<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8E">]</span></span></a></sup> or the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indus_Valley" title="Indus Valley" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA8I">Indus Valley</a><sup about="#mwt442" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-146" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-146"}}'><a href="#cite_note-146" id="mwA8M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8U">[</span>145<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA8c"><b id="mwA8g">4400 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick#Fired_brick" title="Brick" id="mwA8k">Fired bricks</a> in China.<sup about="#mwt445" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-147" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-147"}}'><a href="#cite_note-147" id="mwA8o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA8s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA8w">[</span>146<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA80">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA84"><b id="mwA88">4000 BC:</b> Probable time period of the first diamond-mines in the world, in Southern India.<sup about="#mwt449" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-hershey_148-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"hershey"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-hershey-148"}}'><a href="#cite_note-hershey-148" id="mwA9A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA9E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9I">[</span>147<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA9Q"><b id="mwA9U">4000 BC:</b> Paved <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roads" title="Roads" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA9Y">roads</a>, in and around the Mesopotamian city of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ur" title="Ur" id="mwA9c">Ur</a>, Iraq.<sup about="#mwt452" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-149" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-149"}}'><a href="#cite_note-149" id="mwA9g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA9k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9o">[</span>148<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA9s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA9w"><b id="mwA90">4000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plumbing" title="Plumbing" id="mwA94">Plumbing</a>. The earliest pipes were made of clay, and are found at the Temple of Bel at Nippur in Babylonia.<sup about="#mwt472" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-150" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-150"}}'><a href="#cite_note-150" id="mwA98"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-E">[</span>149<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-I">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt453" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-153" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-153"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Earthen pipes were later used in the Indus Valley c. 2700 BC for a city-scale urban drainage system,&lt;ref>{{cite book| last1 = Teresi| first1 = Dick| author-link = Dick Teresi| title = Lost Discoveries: The Ancient Roots of Modern Science--from the Babylonians to the Maya| publisher = Simon &amp; Schuster| year = 2002| location = New York| pages = [https://archive.org/details/lostdiscoveriesa00tere/page/351 351–352]| isbn = 0-684-83718-8| url-access = registration| url = https://archive.org/details/lostdiscoveriesa00tere/page/351}}&lt;/ref> and more durable copper drainage pipes appeared in Egypt, by the time of the construction of the [[Pyramid of Sahure#Drainage system|Pyramid of Sahure]] at [[Abusir]], c.2400 BCE.&lt;ref name=\"Bunson 6\">{{Cite book|last=Bunson|first=Margaret|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=-6EJ0G-4jyoC&amp;q=Abusir+copper+pipe+ancient+egypt&amp;pg=PA6|title=Encyclopedia of Ancient Egypt|date=14 May 2014|publisher=Infobase Publishing|isbn=978-1-4381-0997-8|page=6|language=en}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-153" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwA-M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-U">[</span>b<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA-c"><b id="mwA-g">4000 BC:</b> Oldest evidence of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lock_and_key" title="Lock and key" id="mwA-k">locks</a>, the earliest example discovered in the ruins of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nineveh" title="Nineveh" id="mwA-o">Nineveh</a>, the capital of ancient <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assyria" title="Assyria" id="mwA-s">Assyria</a>.<sup about="#mwt475" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-154" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-154"}}'><a href="#cite_note-154" id="mwA-w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-4">[</span>152<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA_A"><b id="mwA_E">4000 BC – 3400 BC:</b> Oldest evidence of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheel" title="Wheel" id="mwA_I">wheels</a>, found in the countries of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukraine" title="Ukraine" id="mwA_M">Ukraine</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poland" title="Poland" id="mwA_Q">Poland</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany" title="Germany" id="mwA_U">Germany</a>.<sup about="#mwt478" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-155" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-155"}}'><a href="#cite_note-155" id="mwA_Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA_c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_g">[</span>153<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_k">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt481" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_156-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:4-156"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:4-156" id="mwA_o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA_s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_w">[</span>154<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA_0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwA_4"><b id="mwA_8">3630 BC:</b> Silk garments (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sericulture" title="Sericulture" id="mwBAA">sericulture</a>) in China<sup about="#mwt484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Schoeser_157-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Schoeser"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Schoeser-157"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Schoeser-157" id="mwBAE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBAI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAM">[</span>155<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBAU"><b id="mwBAY">3500 BC:</b> Probable first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestication_of_the_horse" title="Domestication of the horse" id="mwBAc">domestication of the horse</a> in the Eurasian Steppes.<sup about="#mwt485" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-158" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-158"}}'><a href="#cite_note-158" id="mwBAg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBAk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAo">[</span>156<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBAs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt488" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-159" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-159"}}'><a href="#cite_note-159" id="mwBAw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBA0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBA4">[</span>157<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBA8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt491" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cbc.ca_160-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cbc.ca"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-cbc.ca-160"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cbc.ca-160" id="mwBBA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBBE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBI">[</span>158<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBBQ"><b id="mwBBU">3500 BC:</b> Wine as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_anaesthesia" title="General anaesthesia" id="mwBBY">general anaesthesia</a> in Sumer.<sup about="#mwt494" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Powell1996_161-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Powell1996"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Powell1996-161"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Powell1996-161" id="mwBBc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBBg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBk">[</span>159<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBBo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBBs"><b id="mwBBw">3500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seal_(emblem)" title="Seal (emblem)" id="mwBB0">Seal (emblem)</a> invented around in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Near_East" title="Near East" id="mwBB4">Near East</a>, at the contemporary sites of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uruk" title="Uruk" id="mwBB8">Uruk</a> in southern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwBCA">Mesopotamia</a> and slightly later at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Susa" title="Susa" id="mwBCE">Susa</a> in south-western <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran" title="Iran" id="mwBCI">Iran</a> during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Elamite_(period)" title="Proto-Elamite (period)" id="mwBCM">Proto-Elamite period</a>, and they follow the development of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stamp_seal" title="Stamp seal" id="mwBCQ">stamp seals</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halaf_culture" title="Halaf culture" id="mwBCU">Halaf culture</a> or slightly earlier.<sup about="#mwt497" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-162" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-162"}}'><a href="#cite_note-162" id="mwBCY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBCc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCg">[</span>160<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBCo"><b id="mwBCs">3500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ploughing" title="Ploughing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBCw">Ploughing</a>, on a site in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubeneč" title="Bubeneč" id="mwBC0">Bubeneč</a>, Czech Republic.<sup about="#mwt500" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-163" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-163"}}'><a href="#cite_note-163" id="mwBC4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBC8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDA">[</span>161<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDE">]</span></span></a></sup> Evidence, c. 2800 BC, has also been found at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalibangan" title="Kalibangan" id="mwBDI">Kalibangan</a>, Indus Valley (modern-day India).<sup about="#mwt501" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-lal-ivc_164-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"lal-ivc"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-lal-ivc-164"}}'><a href="#cite_note-lal-ivc-164" id="mwBDM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDU">[</span>162<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBDc"><b id="mwBDg">3400 BC – 3100 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tattoo" title="Tattoo" id="mwBDk">Tattoos</a> in southern Europe<sup about="#mwt504" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-165" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-165"}}'><a href="#cite_note-165" id="mwBDo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBDs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBDw">[</span>163<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBD0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt507" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-166" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-166"}}'><a href="#cite_note-166" id="mwBD4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBD8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEA">[</span>164<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBEE">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwBEI" aria-labelledby="Bronze_Age"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Bronze_Age">Bronze Age</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Bronze Age"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBEM"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nippur_cubit.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBEQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nippur_cubit.JPG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Nippur_cubit.JPG/500px-Nippur_cubit.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Nippur_cubit.JPG/960px-Nippur_cubit.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1024" data-file-height="446" data-file-type="bitmap" height="166" width="380" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1.5" id="mwBEU"/></a><figcaption id="mwBEY">The Nippur cubit-rod, <abbr title="circa" about="#mwt508" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBEc" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"c.","href":"./Template:C."},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2650 BCE"}},"i":0}}]}'>c.</abbr><span style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt508" id="mwBEg"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>2650 BCE</span>, in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Istanbul_Archaeology_Museums" title="Istanbul Archaeology Museums" id="mwBEk">Archeological Museum</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Istanbul" title="Istanbul" id="mwBEo">Istanbul</a>, Turkey</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwBEs">The beginning of bronze-smelting coincides with the emergence of the first cities and of writing in the Ancient Near East and the Indus Valley. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_Age" title="Bronze Age" id="mwBEw">Bronze Age</a> starting in Eurasia in the 4th millennia BC and ended, in Eurasia, c.1200 BC.</p>
<ul id="mwBE0"><li id="mwBE4"><b id="mwBE8">Late 4th millennium BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Writing" title="Writing" id="mwBFA">Writing</a> – in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumer" title="Sumer" id="mwBFE">Sumer</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt" title="Egypt" id="mwBFI">Egypt</a>.<sup about="#mwt511" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Radner_167-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Radner"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Radner-167"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Radner-167" id="mwBFM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFU">[</span>165<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt514" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-168" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-168"}}'><a href="#cite_note-168" id="mwBFc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFk">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBFo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt517" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-169" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-169"}}'><a href="#cite_note-169" id="mwBFs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBFw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBF0">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBF4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt520" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-170" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-170"}}'><a href="#cite_note-170" id="mwBF8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGE">[</span>168<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBGM"><b id="mwBGQ">3300 BC:</b> The first documented <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sword" title="Sword" id="mwBGU">swords</a>. They have been found in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arslantepe" title="Arslantepe" id="mwBGY">Arslantepe</a>, Turkey, are made from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arsenical_bronze" title="Arsenical bronze" id="mwBGc">arsenical bronze</a>, and are about <span about="#mwt521" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwBGg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"60"},"2":{"wt":"cm"},"3":{"wt":"in"},"abbr":{"wt":"on"}},"i":0}}]}'>60</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt521"> </span><span about="#mwt521">cm (24</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt521"> </span><span about="#mwt521">in)</span> long.<sup about="#mwt522" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-171" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-171"}}'><a href="#cite_note-171" id="mwBGk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBGo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGs">[</span>169<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBGw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt525" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-KAY_172-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"KAY"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-KAY-172"}}'><a href="#cite_note-KAY-172" id="mwBG0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBG4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBG8">[</span>170<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHA">]</span></span></a></sup> Some of them are inlaid with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver" title="Silver" id="mwBHE">silver</a>.<sup about="#mwt526" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-KAY_172-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"KAY"}}'><a href="#cite_note-KAY-172" id="mwBHI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBHM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHQ">[</span>170<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBHU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBHY"><b id="mwBHc">3300 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City" title="City" id="mwBHg">City</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uruk" title="Uruk" id="mwBHk">Uruk</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumer" title="Sumer" id="mwBHo">Sumer</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwBHs">Mesopotamia</a> (modern-day Iraq).<sup about="#mwt529" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-173" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-173"}}'><a href="#cite_note-173" id="mwBHw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBH0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBH4">[</span>171<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBH8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBIA"><b id="mwBIE">3250 BC: </b>One of the earliest documented <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hat" title="Hat" id="mwBII">hats</a> was worn by a man (nicknamed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ötzi" title="Ötzi" id="mwBIM">Ötzi</a>) whose body and hat  found frozen in a mountain between Austria and Italy. He was found wearing a bearskin cap with a chin strap, made of several hides stitched together, resembling a Russian fur hat without the flaps.<sup about="#mwt532" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-174" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-174"}}'><a href="#cite_note-174" id="mwBIQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIY">[</span>172<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-175" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-175"}}'><a href="#cite_note-175" id="mwBIg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBIk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIo">[</span>173<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-176" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-176"}}'><a href="#cite_note-176" id="mwBIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBI0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI4">[</span>174<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBI8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBJA"><b id="mwBJE">3200 BC:</b> Dry <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latrine" title="Latrine" id="mwBJI">Latrines</a> in the city of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uruk" title="Uruk" id="mwBJM">Uruk</a>, Iraq, with later dry squat <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toilet" title="Toilet" id="mwBJQ">Toilets</a>, that added raised fired brick foot platforms, and pedestal toilets, all over clay pipe constructed drains.<sup about="#mwt541" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-177" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-177"}}'><a href="#cite_note-177" id="mwBJU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJc">[</span>175<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt544" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-178" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-178"}}'><a href="#cite_note-178" id="mwBJk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJs">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt547" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-179" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-179"}}'><a href="#cite_note-179" id="mwBJ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBJ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBJ8">[</span>177<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBKE"><b id="mwBKI">3200 BC:</b> Earliest actual wheel ever found, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ljubljana_Marshes_Wheel" title="Ljubljana Marshes Wheel" id="mwBKM">Ljubljana Marshes Wheel</a>, made of wood, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovenia" title="Slovenia" id="mwBKQ">Slovenia</a>.<sup about="#mwt548" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_156-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:4-156" id="mwBKU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBKY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKc">[</span>154<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBKg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBKk"><b id="mwBKo">3000 BC:</b> Devices functionally equivalent to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dice" title="Dice" id="mwBKs">dice</a>, in the form of flat two-sided throwsticks, are seen in the Egyptian game of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senet" title="Senet" id="mwBKw">Senet</a>.<sup about="#mwt551" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Aruz_180-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Aruz"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Aruz-180"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Aruz-180" id="mwBK0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBK4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBK8">[</span>178<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLA">]</span></span></a></sup> Perhaps the oldest known dice, resembling modern ones, were excavated as part of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backgammon" title="Backgammon" id="mwBLE">backgammon</a>-like game set at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnt_City" title="Burnt City" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBLI">Burnt City</a>, an archeological site in south-eastern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran" title="Iran" id="mwBLM">Iran</a>, estimated to be from between 2800 and 2500 BC.<sup about="#mwt554" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-181" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-181"}}'><a href="#cite_note-181" id="mwBLQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLY">[</span>179<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt557" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-182" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-182"}}'><a href="#cite_note-182" id="mwBLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBLk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLo">[</span>180<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBLs">]</span></span></a></sup> Later, terracotta dice were used at the Indus Valley site of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohenjo-daro" title="Mohenjo-daro" id="mwBLw">Mohenjo-daro</a> (modern-day Pakistan).<sup about="#mwt558" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-183" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-183"}}'><a href="#cite_note-183" id="mwBL0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBL4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBL8">[</span>181<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBME"><b id="mwBMI">3000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin" title="Tin" id="mwBMM">Tin</a> extraction in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Asia" title="Central Asia" id="mwBMQ">Central Asia</a><sup about="#mwt561" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-184" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-184"}}'><a href="#cite_note-184" id="mwBMU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBMY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMc">[</span>182<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBMg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBMk"><b id="mwBMo">3000 BC – 2560 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papyrus" title="Papyrus" id="mwBMs">Papyrus</a> in Egypt<sup about="#mwt564" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Fischer_185-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Fischer"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Fischer-185"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Fischer-185" id="mwBMw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBM0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBM4">[</span>183<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBM8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt567" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-186" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-186"}}'><a href="#cite_note-186" id="mwBNA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNI">[</span>184<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt570" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Johnson_187-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Johnson"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Johnson-187"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Johnson-187" id="mwBNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNY">[</span>185<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt573" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_188-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-188"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-188" id="mwBNg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBNk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNo">[</span>186<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBNs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBNw"><b id="mwBN0">3000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reservoir" title="Reservoir" id="mwBN4">Reservoir</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girnar" title="Girnar" id="mwBN8">Girnar</a>, Indus Valley.<sup about="#mwt576" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rodda_189-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Rodda"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rodda-189"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Rodda-189" id="mwBOA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOI">[</span>187<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBOQ"><b id="mwBOU">3000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receipt" title="Receipt" id="mwBOY">Receipt</a> in Ancient <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwBOc">Mesopotamia</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq" title="Iraq" id="mwBOg">Iraq</a>)<sup about="#mwt579" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-190" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-190"}}'><a href="#cite_note-190" id="mwBOk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBOo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOs">[</span>188<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBOw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBO0"><b id="mwBO4">3000 BC – 2800 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prosthesis" title="Prosthesis" id="mwBO8">Prosthesis</a> first documented in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Near_East" title="Ancient Near East" id="mwBPA">Ancient Near East</a>, in ancient Egypt and Iran, specifically for an eye prosthetics, the eye found in Iran was likely made of bitumen paste that was covered with a thin layer of gold.<sup about="#mwt582" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-191" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-191"}}'><a href="#cite_note-191" id="mwBPE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBPI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPM">[</span>189<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBPU"><b id="mwBPY">3000 BC – 2500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinoplasty" title="Rhinoplasty" id="mwBPc">Rhinoplasty</a> in Egypt.<sup about="#mwt585" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cossurg_192-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"cossurg"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-cossurg-192"}}'><a href="#cite_note-cossurg-192" id="mwBPg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBPk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPo">[</span>190<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBPs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt588" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-plsurgery_193-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"plsurgery"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-plsurgery-193"}}'><a href="#cite_note-plsurgery-193" id="mwBPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBP4">[</span>191<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBP8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBQA"><b id="mwBQE">2650 BC:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruler" title="Ruler" id="mwBQI">Ruler</a>, or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Measuring_rod" title="Measuring rod" id="mwBQM">Measuring rod</a>, in the subdivided <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nippur" title="Nippur" id="mwBQQ">Nippur</a>, copper rod, of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumer" title="Sumer" id="mwBQU">Sumerian Civilisation</a> (modern-day Iraq).<sup about="#mwt589" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-195" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-195"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Shell, Terracotta, Copper, and Ivory rulers were in use by the [[Indus Valley civilisation]] in what today is Pakistan, and North West India, prior to 1500 BCE.&lt;ref>{{Cite book|last=McIntosh|first=Jane|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=1AJO2A-CbccC&amp;q=ivory+ruler+lothal+indus+valley&amp;pg=PA345|title=The Ancient Indus Valley: New Perspectives|date=2008|publisher=ABC-CLIO|isbn=978-1-57607-907-2|language=en}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-195" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwBQY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQg">[</span>c<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBQo"><b id="mwBQs">2600 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planned_city" title="Planned city" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBQw">Planned city</a> in Indus Valley.<sup about="#mwt601" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Davreu1_196-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Davreu1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Davreu1-196"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Davreu1-196" id="mwBQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBQ8">[</span>193<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt604" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Kipfer229_197-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Kipfer229"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Kipfer229-197"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Kipfer229-197" id="mwBRE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRM">[</span>194<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBRU"><b id="mwBRY">2600 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanitation_of_the_Indus_Valley_Civilisation" title="Sanitation of the Indus Valley Civilisation" id="mwBRc">Public sewage and sanitation systems in Indus Valley</a> sites such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohenjo-daro" title="Mohenjo-daro" id="mwBRg">Mohenjo-daro</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rakhigarhi" title="Rakhigarhi" id="mwBRk">Rakhigarhi</a>.<sup about="#mwt607" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-198" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-198"}}'><a href="#cite_note-198" id="mwBRo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBRs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBRw">[</span>195<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBR0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBR4"><b id="mwBR8">2600 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Bath,_Mohenjo-daro" title="Great Bath, Mohenjo-daro" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBSA">Public bath</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohenjo-daro" title="Mohenjo-daro" id="mwBSE">Mohenjo-daro</a>, Indus Valley (modern-day <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistan" title="Pakistan" id="mwBSI">Pakistan</a>).<sup about="#mwt610" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Kenoyer_199-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Kenoyer"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Kenoyer-199"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Kenoyer-199" id="mwBSM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSU">[</span>196<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBSc"><b id="mwBSg">2600 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levee" title="Levee" id="mwBSk">Levee</a> in Indus Valley.<sup about="#mwt613" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-200" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-200"}}'><a href="#cite_note-200" id="mwBSo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBSs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBSw">[</span>197<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBS0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBS4"><b id="mwBS8">2600 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weighing_scale" title="Weighing scale" id="mwBTA">Balance weights and scales</a>, from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourth_Dynasty_of_Egypt" title="Fourth Dynasty of Egypt" id="mwBTE">Fourth Dynasty of Egypt</a>; examples of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deben_(unit)" title="Deben (unit)" id="mwBTI">Deben (unit)</a> balance weights, from reign of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sneferu" title="Sneferu" id="mwBTM">Sneferu</a> (c. 2600 BC) have been attributed.<sup about="#mwt616" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-201" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-201"}}'><a href="#cite_note-201" id="mwBTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTY">[</span>198<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBTc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBTg"><b id="mwBTk">2556 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dock_(maritime)" title="Dock (maritime)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBTo">Docks</a> structure in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wadi_al-Jarf" title="Wadi al-Jarf" id="mwBTs">Wadi al-Jarf</a>, Egypt, which was developed by the reign of the Pharaoh <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khufu" title="Khufu" id="mwBTw">Khufu</a>.<sup about="#mwt660" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Global_202-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Global"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Global-202"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Global-202" id="mwBT0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBT4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT8">[</span>199<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt661" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_188-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-188" id="mwBUE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUM">[</span>186<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt617" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-209" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-209"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"A competing claim is from [[Lothal]] dockyard in India,&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/27667625 |title=Foraminifera as an additional tool for archaeologists - Examples from the Arabian Sea |date=25 September 2015 }}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{Cite web|title=ARCHAEOASTRONOMICAL SURVEYS IN LOTHAL (INDIA)|url=http://www.archaeoastronomy.it/Lothal.htm|last=Codebò|first=Mario|date=2013|website=www.archaeoastronomy.it|access-date=10 May 2020}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{Cite book|last=Frenez|first=D.|title=Lothal re-visitation Project, a fine thread connecting Intis to contemporary Raveena (Via Oman)|publisher=BAR|year=2014|isbn=978-1-4073-1326-9|location=UK|pages=263–267}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref name=\"RaoQ\">Rao, pages 27–28&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{cite web |title=Archaeological remains of a Harappa Port-Town, Lothal |url=https://whc.unesco.org/en/tentativelists/5918/ |website=UNESCO |publisher=UN |access-date=10 May 2020}}&lt;/ref> constructed at some point between 2400-2000 BC;&lt;ref name=\"RaoY\">{{cite book | title = Lothal | publisher = [[Archaeological Survey of India]] | author = [[S. R. Rao]] | pages = 11–17 | year = 1985}}&lt;/ref> however, more precise dating does not exist."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-209" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwBUU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBUY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUc">[</span>d<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBUg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBUk"><b id="mwBUo">2500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puppetry" title="Puppetry" id="mwBUs">Puppetry</a> in the Indus Valley.<sup about="#mwt664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-210" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-210"}}'><a href="#cite_note-210" id="mwBUw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBU0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBU4">[</span>206<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBU8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt667" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-211" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-211"}}'><a href="#cite_note-211" id="mwBVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVI">[</span>207<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBVQ"><b id="mwBVU">2400 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fork" title="Fork" id="mwBVY">Fork</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_Age" title="Bronze Age" id="mwBVc">Bronze Age</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qijia_culture" title="Qijia culture" id="mwBVg">Qijia culture</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwBVk">China</a><sup about="#mwt670" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-212" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-212"}}'><a href="#cite_note-212" id="mwBVo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBVs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBVw">[</span>208<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBV0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBV4"><b id="mwBV8">2400 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_water_supply_and_sanitation#Ancient_Egypt" title="History of water supply and sanitation" id="mwBWA">Copper pipes</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyramid_of_Sahure#Drainage_system" title="Pyramid of Sahure" id="mwBWE">Pyramid of Sahure</a>, an adjoining temple complex at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abusir" title="Abusir" id="mwBWI">Abusir</a>, was discovered to have a network of copper drainage pipes.<sup about="#mwt671" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bunson_6_152-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bunson 6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bunson_6-152" id="mwBWM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBWQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWU">[</span>151<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBWY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBWc"><b id="mwBWg">2400 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touchstone_(assaying_tool)" title="Touchstone (assaying tool)" id="mwBWk">Touchstone</a> in the Indus Valley site of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banawali" title="Banawali" id="mwBWo">Banawali</a> (modern-day India).<sup about="#mwt674" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-213" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-213"}}'><a href="#cite_note-213" id="mwBWs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBW0">[</span>209<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBW4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBW8"><b id="mwBXA">2300 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dictionary" title="Dictionary" id="mwBXE">Dictionary</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwBXI">Mesopotamia</a>.<sup about="#mwt677" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-214" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-214"}}'><a href="#cite_note-214" id="mwBXM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXU">[</span>210<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBXY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBXc"><b id="mwBXg">2200 BC – 2000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_smelting" title="Iron smelting" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBXk">Iron smelting</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaman-Kalehöyük" title="Kaman-Kalehöyük" id="mwBXo">Kaman-Kalehöyük</a>.<sup about="#mwt680" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-215" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-215"}}'><a href="#cite_note-215" id="mwBXs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBX0">[</span>211<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBX4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBX8"><b id="mwBYA">2200 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protractor" title="Protractor" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBYE">Protractor</a>, Phase IV, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lothal" title="Lothal" id="mwBYI">Lothal</a>, Indus Valley (modern-day India), a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turbinella_pyrum" title="Turbinella pyrum" id="mwBYM">Xancus</a> shell cylinder with sawn grooves, at right angles, in its top and bottom surfaces, has been proposed as an angle marking tool.<sup about="#mwt683" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rao401_216-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Rao401"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rao401-216"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Rao401-216" id="mwBYQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYY">[</span>212<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt686" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-217" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-217"}}'><a href="#cite_note-217" id="mwBYg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBYk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYo">[</span>213<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBYs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBYw"><b id="mwBY0">2000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_clock" title="Water clock" id="mwBY4">Water clock</a> by at least the old Babylonian period (c. 2000 – c. 1600 BC),<sup about="#mwt689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-218" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-218"}}'><a href="#cite_note-218" id="mwBY8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZE">[</span>214<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZI">]</span></span></a></sup> but possibly earlier from Mohenjo-Daro in the Indus Valley.<sup about="#mwt692" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-219" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-219"}}'><a href="#cite_note-219" id="mwBZM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZU">[</span>215<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBZc"><b id="mwBZg">2000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chariot" title="Chariot" id="mwBZk">Chariot</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia" title="Russia" id="mwBZo">Russia</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kazakhstan" title="Kazakhstan" id="mwBZs">Kazakhstan</a><sup about="#mwt693" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-220" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-220"}}'><a href="#cite_note-220" id="mwBZw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBZ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZ4">[</span>216<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBZ8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBaA"><b id="mwBaE">2000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scissors" title="Scissors" id="mwBaI">Scissors</a>, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwBaM">Mesopotamia</a>.<sup about="#mwt696" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-221" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-221"}}'><a href="#cite_note-221" id="mwBaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBaU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBaY">[</span>217<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBac">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBag"><b id="mwBak">2000 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noodle" title="Noodle" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBao">Noodle</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lajia" title="Lajia" id="mwBas">Lajia</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwBaw">China</a><sup about="#mwt699" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-222" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-222"}}'><a href="#cite_note-222" id="mwBa0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBa4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBa8">[</span>218<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbA">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

<ul id="mwBbE"><li id="mwBbI"><b id="mwBbM">1850 BC:</b> Proto-alphabet (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Sinaitic_script" title="Proto-Sinaitic script" id="mwBbQ">Proto-Sinaitic script</a>) in Egypt.<sup about="#mwt702" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-223" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-223"}}'><a href="#cite_note-223" id="mwBbU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBbY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbc">[</span>219<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBbk"><b id="mwBbo">1600 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwin_Smith_Papyrus" title="Edwin Smith Papyrus" id="mwBbs">Surgical treatise</a> appeared in Egypt.<sup about="#mwt705" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WilkinsRobert_224-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WilkinsRobert"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WilkinsRobert-224"}}'><a href="#cite_note-WilkinsRobert-224" id="mwBbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBb0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBb4">[</span>220<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBb8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBcA"><b id="mwBcE">1500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sundial" title="Sundial" id="mwBcI">Sundial</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egypt" title="Ancient Egypt" id="mwBcM">Ancient Egypt</a><sup about="#mwt708" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-225" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-225"}}'><a href="#cite_note-225" id="mwBcQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBcU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcY">[</span>221<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcc">]</span></span></a></sup> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babylonia" title="Babylonia" id="mwBcg">Babylonia</a> (modern-day Iraq).</li>
<li id="mwBck"><b id="mwBco">1500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glass" title="Glass" id="mwBcs">Glass</a> manufacture in either <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesopotamia" title="Mesopotamia" id="mwBcw">Mesopotamia</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egypt" title="Ancient Egypt" id="mwBc0">Ancient Egypt</a>.<sup about="#mwt711" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-226" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-226"}}'><a href="#cite_note-226" id="mwBc4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBc8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdA">[</span>222<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBdI"><b id="mwBdM">1500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seed_drill" title="Seed drill" id="mwBdQ">Seed drill</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babylonia" title="Babylonia" id="mwBdU">Babylonia</a>.<sup about="#mwt712" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ReferenceA_227-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ReferenceA"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReferenceA-227"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ReferenceA-227" id="mwBdY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBdc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdg">[</span>223<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBdo"><b id="mwBds">1400 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesoamerican_rubber_balls" title="Mesoamerican rubber balls" id="mwBdw">Rubber</a>,<sup about="#mwt713" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_228-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-228" id="mwBd0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBd4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBd8">[</span>224<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeA">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesoamerican_ballgame" title="Mesoamerican ballgame" id="mwBeE">Mesoamerican ballgame</a>.<sup about="#mwt716" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:3_228-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:3-228"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:3-228" id="mwBeI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBeM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeQ">[</span>224<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt717" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-229" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-229"}}'><a href="#cite_note-229" id="mwBeY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBec"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeg">[</span>225<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBek">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBeo"><b id="mwBes">1400 BC – 1200 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concrete" title="Concrete" id="mwBew">Concrete</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiryns" title="Tiryns" id="mwBe0">Tiryns</a> (Mycenaean Greece),<sup about="#mwt720" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-230" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-230"}}'><a href="#cite_note-230" id="mwBe4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBe8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfA">[</span>226<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt723" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-231" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-231"}}'><a href="#cite_note-231" id="mwBfI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfQ">[</span>227<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBfY"><b id="mwBfc">1300 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lathe" title="Lathe" id="mwBfg">Lathe</a> in Ancient Egypt.<sup about="#mwt726" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-232" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-232"}}'><a href="#cite_note-232" id="mwBfk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfs">[</span>228<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBf0"><b id="mwBf4">1200 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distillation" title="Distillation" id="mwBf8">Distillation</a> is described on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akkadian_language" title="Akkadian language" id="mwBgA">Akkadian</a> tablets documenting perfumery operations.<sup about="#mwt729" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-233" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-233"}}'><a href="#cite_note-233" id="mwBgE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgM">[</span>229<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwBgU" aria-labelledby="Iron_Age"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Iron_Age">Iron Age</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Iron Age"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBgY">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Bronze_Age_collapse" title="Late Bronze Age collapse" id="mwBgc">Late Bronze Age collapse</a> occurs around 1200 BC,<sup about="#mwt735" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-234" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-234"}}'><a href="#cite_note-234" id="mwBgg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgo">[</span>230<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgs">]</span></span></a></sup> extinguishing most Bronze-Age Near Eastern cultures, and significantly weakening the rest. This is coincident with the complete collapse of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indus_Valley_Civilisation" title="Indus Valley Civilisation" id="mwBgw">Indus Valley Civilisation</a>. This event is followed by the beginning of the Iron Age. We define the Iron Age as ending in 510 BC for the purposes of this article, even though the typical definition is region-dependent (e.g. 510 BC in Greece, 322 BC in India, 200 BC in China), thus being an 800-year period.<sup about="#mwt730" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-235" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-235"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"The uncertainty in dating several Indian developments between 600 BC and 300 AD, due to the tradition that existed of editing existing documents (such as the Sushruta Samhita and Arthashastra) without specifically documenting the edit. Most such documents were canonized at the start of the Gupta empire (mid-3rd century AD)."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-235" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwBg0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBg4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBg8">[</span>e<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<ul id="mwBhE"><li id="mwBhI"><b id="mwBhM">1100 BC</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_catalogue" title="Star catalogue" id="mwBhQ">Star catalogue</a> — <em id="mwBhU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babylonian_star_catalogues#Three_Stars_Each" title="Babylonian star catalogues" id="mwBhY">Three Stars Each</a></em> is the earliest known catalogue in long-running tradition of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babylonian_astronomy" title="Babylonian astronomy" id="mwBhc">Babylonian astronomy</a>,<sup about="#mwt738" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-236" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-236"}}'><a href="#cite_note-236" id="mwBhg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBho">[</span>231<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhs">]</span></span></a></sup> likely drawing on Sumerian<sup about="#mwt740" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-237" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-237"}}'><a href="#cite_note-237" id="mwBhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBh0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBh4">[</span>232<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBh8">]</span></span></a></sup> and/or Elamite constellations.<sup about="#mwt742" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-238" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-238"}}'><a href="#cite_note-238" id="mwBiA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBiE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiI">[</span>233<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBiM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBiQ"><b id="mwBiU">700 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saddle" title="Saddle" id="mwBiY">Saddle</a> (fringed cloths or pads used by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assyrian_cavalry" title="Assyrian cavalry" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBic">Assyrian cavalry</a>).<sup about="#mwt746" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Beatie18_239-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Beatie18"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Beatie18-239"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Beatie18-239" id="mwBig"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBik"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBio">[</span>234<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBis">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBiw"><b id="mwBi0">7th century BC:</b> The royal <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library_of_Ashurbanipal" title="Library of Ashurbanipal" id="mwBi4">Library of Ashurbanipal</a> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nineveh" title="Nineveh" id="mwBi8">Nineveh</a> had 30,000 clay tablets, in several languages, organized according to shape and separated by content. The first recorded example of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Library_catalog" title="Library catalog" id="mwBjA">library catalog</a>.<sup about="#mwt749" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-240" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-240"}}'><a href="#cite_note-240" id="mwBjE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjM">[</span>235<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBjU"><b id="mwBjY">688 BC:</b> Waterproof concrete in use, by the Assyrians.<sup about="#mwt750" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-241" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-241"}}'><a href="#cite_note-241" id="mwBjc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjk">[</span>236<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBjo">]</span></span></a></sup> Later, the Romans developed concretes that could set underwater,<sup about="#mwt751" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Lechtman_and_Hobbs_242-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Lechtman and Hobbs"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lechtman_and_Hobbs-242"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Lechtman_and_Hobbs-242" id="mwBjs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBjw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBj0">[</span>237<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBj4">]</span></span></a></sup> and used concrete extensively for construction from 300 BC to 476 AD.<sup about="#mwt754" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MAST_243-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"MAST"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MAST-243"}}'><a href="#cite_note-MAST-243" id="mwBj8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkE">[</span>238<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBkM"><b id="mwBkQ">650 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossbow" title="Crossbow" id="mwBkU">Crossbow</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwBkY">China</a>.<sup about="#mwt757" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-244" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-244"}}'><a href="#cite_note-244" id="mwBkc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBkk">[</span>239<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBko">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBks"><b id="mwBkw">600 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coins" title="Coins" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBk0">Coins</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenicia" title="Phoenicia" id="mwBk4">Phoenicia</a> (Modern Lebanon) or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lydia" title="Lydia" id="mwBk8">Lydia</a>.<sup about="#mwt758" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-245" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-245"}}'><a href="#cite_note-245" id="mwBlA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlI">[</span>240<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBlQ"><b id="mwBlU">Late 7th or early 6th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagonway" title="Wagonway" id="mwBlY">Wagonway</a> called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diolkos" title="Diolkos" id="mwBlc">Diolkos</a> across the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isthmus_of_Corinth" title="Isthmus of Corinth" id="mwBlg">Isthmus of Corinth</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greece" title="Ancient Greece" id="mwBlk">Ancient Greece</a>.<sup about="#mwt761" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-246" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-246"}}'><a href="#cite_note-246" id="mwBlo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBls"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlw">[</span>241<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBl0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt764" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-247" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-247"}}'><a href="#cite_note-247" id="mwBl4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBl8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmA">[</span>242<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmE">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBmI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Trispastos_scheme.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBmM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Trispastos_scheme.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Trispastos_scheme.svg/250px-Trispastos_scheme.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Trispastos_scheme.svg/500px-Trispastos_scheme.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1520" data-file-height="1370" data-file-type="drawing" height="225" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBmQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwBmU">With the Greco-Roman <i id="mwBmY">trispastos</i> ("three-pulley-crane"), the simplest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_crane" title="Ancient crane" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBmc">ancient crane</a>, a single man tripled the weight he could lift than with his muscular strength alone.<sup about="#mwt765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-248" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248"}}'><a href="#cite_note-248" id="mwBmg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmo">[</span>243<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBms">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwBmw"><li id="mwBm0"><b id="mwBm4">6th century BC – 10th century AD:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel#Wootz_steel_and_Damascus_steel" title="Steel" id="mwBm8">High Carbon Steel</a>, produced by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crucible_steel" title="Crucible steel" id="mwBnA">Closed Crucible method</a>, later known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wootz_steel" title="Wootz steel" id="mwBnE">Wootz steel</a>, of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_India" title="South India" id="mwBnI">South India</a>.<sup about="#mwt778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wootz-davidson_249-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wootz-davidson"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-wootz-davidson-249"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wootz-davidson-249" id="mwBnM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnU">[</span>244<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt781" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wootz-iisc_250-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wootz-iisc"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-wootz-iisc-250"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wootz-iisc-250" id="mwBnc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBng"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnk">[</span>245<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBno">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt766" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-252" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-252"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"A 10th century AD, [[Damascus]] steel blade, analysed under an electron microscope, contains nano-meter tubes in its metal alloy. Their presence has been suggested to be down to transition-metal impurities in the ores once used to produce Wootz Steel in South India.&lt;ref>{{cite journal |url=http://www.nature.com/news/2006/061113/full/news061113-11.html |title=Sharpest cut from nanotube sword |first=Katharine |last=Sanderson |date=15 November 2006 |journal=[[Nature (journal)|Nature]] |pages=news061113–11 |doi=10.1038/news061113-11|s2cid=136774602 |doi-access=free }}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-252" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwBns"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn0">[</span>f<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBn8"><b id="mwBoA">6th century – 2nd century BC:</b> Systematization of medicine and surgery in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sushruta_Samhita" title="Sushruta Samhita" id="mwBoE">Sushruta Samhita</a> in Vedic Northern India.<sup about="#mwt782" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sush_253-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sush"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-sush-253"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sush-253" id="mwBoI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoQ">[</span>247<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt787" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-254" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-254"}}'><a href="#cite_note-254" id="mwBoY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBog">[</span>248<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBok">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt790" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sush_date_255-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sush_date"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-sush_date-255"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sush_date-255" id="mwBoo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBos"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBow">[</span>249<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBo0">]</span></span></a></sup> Documented procedures to:
<ul id="mwBo4"><li id="mwBo8">Perform <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cataract_surgery" title="Cataract surgery" id="mwBpA">cataract surgery</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Couching_(ophthalmology)" title="Couching (ophthalmology)" id="mwBpE">couching</a>). Babylonian and Egyptian texts, a millennium before, depict and mention oculists, but not the procedure itself.<sup about="#mwt793" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-256" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-256"}}'><a href="#cite_note-256" id="mwBpI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpQ">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBpY">Perform <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caesarean_section" title="Caesarean section" id="mwBpc">Caesarean section</a>.<sup about="#mwt794" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sush_info_257-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sush_info"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sush_info-257" id="mwBpg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpo">[</span>251<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBps">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBpw">Construct <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prosthetic_limb" title="Prosthetic limb" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBp0">Prosthetic limbs</a>.<sup about="#mwt795" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sush_info_257-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sush_info"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sush_info-257" id="mwBp4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBp8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqA">[</span>251<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBqI">Perform <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plastic_surgery" title="Plastic surgery" id="mwBqM">Plastic surgery</a>, though reconstructive <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasal_surgery" title="Nasal surgery" id="mwBqQ">nasal surgery</a> is described in millennia older <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwin_Smith_Papyrus" title="Edwin Smith Papyrus" id="mwBqU">Egyptian papyri</a>.<sup about="#mwt798" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sush_info_257-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sush_info"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-sush_info-257"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sush_info-257" id="mwBqY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqg">[</span>251<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt800" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Dwivedi&amp;Dwivedi_258-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Dwivedi&amp;Dwivedi"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Dwivedi&amp;Dwivedi-258"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Dwivedi&amp;Dwivedi-258" id="mwBqo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqw">[</span>252<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBq0">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></li>
<li id="mwBq4"><b id="mwBq8">Late 6th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crank_(mechanism)" title="Crank (mechanism)" id="mwBrA">Crank</a> motion (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rotary_quern" title="Rotary quern" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBrE">rotary quern</a>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Carthage" title="Ancient Carthage" id="mwBrI">Carthage</a><sup about="#mwt801" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECurtis2008375_259-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECurtis2008375"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECurtis2008375-259"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Curtis"},"2":{"wt":"2008"},"p":{"wt":"375"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECurtis2008375-259" id="mwBrM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrU">[</span>253<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrY">]</span></span></a></sup> or 5th century BC <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celtiberians" title="Celtiberians" id="mwBrc">Celtiberian</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spain" title="Spain" id="mwBrg">Spain</a><sup about="#mwt804" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Frankel_2003,_17–19_260-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Frankel 2003, 17–19"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Frankel_2003,_17–19-260"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Frankel_2003,_17–19-260" id="mwBrk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBro"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrs">[</span>254<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt805" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-261" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-261"}}'><a href="#cite_note-261" id="mwBr0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBr4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr8">[</span>255<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsA">]</span></span></a></sup> Later during the Roman empire, a mechanism appeared that incorporated a connecting rod.</li>
<li id="mwBsE"><b id="mwBsI">Before 5th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deed" title="Deed" id="mwBsM">Loan deeds</a> in Upanishadic India.<sup about="#mwt808" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-262" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-262"}}'><a href="#cite_note-262" id="mwBsQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsY">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBsg"><b id="mwBsk">500 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lighthouse" title="Lighthouse" id="mwBso">Lighthouse</a> in Greece.<sup about="#mwt811" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-263" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-263"}}'><a href="#cite_note-263" id="mwBss"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBs0">[</span>257<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBs4">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwBs8" aria-labelledby="Classical_antiquity_and_medieval_era"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Classical_antiquity_and_medieval_era">Classical antiquity and medieval era</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Classical antiquity and medieval era"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwBtA" aria-labelledby="5th_century_BC"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="5th_century_BC">5th century BC</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: 5th century BC"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwBtE"><li id="mwBtI"><b id="mwBtM">500 – 200 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stirrup#Precursors" title="Stirrup" id="mwBtQ">Toe stirrup</a>, depicted in 2nd century Buddhist art, of the Sanchi and Bhaja Caves, of the Deccan <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satavahana_dynasty" title="Satavahana dynasty" id="mwBtU">Satavahana empire</a> (modern-day India)<sup about="#mwt814" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-264" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-264"}}'><a href="#cite_note-264" id="mwBtY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBtc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtg">[</span>258<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt817" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-265" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-265"}}'><a href="#cite_note-265" id="mwBto"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBts"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtw">[</span>259<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBt0">]</span></span></a></sup> although may have originated as early as 500 BC.<sup about="#mwt820" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-266" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-266"}}'><a href="#cite_note-266" id="mwBt4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBt8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuA">[</span>260<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBuI"><b id="mwBuM">485 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catapult" title="Catapult" id="mwBuQ">Catapult</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajatashatru" title="Ajatashatru" id="mwBuU">Ajatashatru</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magadha_(Mahajanapada)" title="Magadha (Mahajanapada)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBuY">Magadha</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India" title="India" id="mwBuc">India</a>.<sup about="#mwt823" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ajatashatru_267-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ajatashatru"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ajatashatru-267"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ajatashatru-267" id="mwBug"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuo">[</span>261<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBus">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt826" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-aja_date_268-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"aja_date"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-aja_date-268"}}'><a href="#cite_note-aja_date-268" id="mwBuw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBu0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBu4">[</span>262<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBu8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBvA"><b id="mwBvE">485 BC:</b> Scythed chariot by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajatashatru" title="Ajatashatru" id="mwBvI">Ajatashatru</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magadha_(Mahajanapada)" title="Magadha (Mahajanapada)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBvM">Magadha</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India" title="India" id="mwBvQ">India</a>.<sup about="#mwt827" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ajatashatru_267-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ajatashatru"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ajatashatru-267" id="mwBvU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvc">[</span>261<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt828" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-aja_date_268-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"aja_date"}}'><a href="#cite_note-aja_date-268" id="mwBvk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvs">[</span>262<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBv0"><b id="mwBv4">5th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cast_iron" title="Cast iron" id="mwBv8">Cast iron</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_China#Ancient_China" title="History of China" id="mwBwA">Ancient China</a>: Confirmed by archaeological evidence, the earliest cast iron is developed in China by the early 5th century BC during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhou_dynasty" title="Zhou dynasty" id="mwBwE">Zhou dynasty</a> (1122–256 BC), the oldest specimens found in a tomb of Luhe County in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiangsu" title="Jiangsu" id="mwBwI">Jiangsu</a> province.<sup about="#mwt829" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wagner_7_36_37_64_68_269-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wagner 7 36 37 64 68"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-wagner_7_36_37_64_68-269"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wagner_7_36_37_64_68-269" id="mwBwM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwU">[</span>263<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt830" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-270" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-270"}}'><a href="#cite_note-270" id="mwBwc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwk">[</span>264<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt831" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-pigott_1999_177_271-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"pigott 1999 177"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-pigott_1999_177-271"}}'><a href="#cite_note-pigott_1999_177-271" id="mwBws"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBww"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBw0">[</span>265<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBw4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBw8"><b id="mwBxA">480 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spiral_stairs" title="Spiral stairs" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBxE">Spiral stairs</a> (Temple A) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selinunte" title="Selinunte" id="mwBxI">Selinunte</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sicily" title="Sicily" id="mwBxM">Sicily</a> (see also <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ancient_spiral_stairs" title="List of ancient spiral stairs" id="mwBxQ">List of ancient spiral stairs</a>)<sup about="#mwt832" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-272" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-272"}}'><a href="#cite_note-272" id="mwBxU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxc">[</span>266<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt835" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-273" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-273"}}'><a href="#cite_note-273" id="mwBxk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBxo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxs">[</span>267<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBxw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwBx0"><b id="mwBx4">By 407 BC:</b> Early descriptions of what may be a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheelbarrow" title="Wheelbarrow" id="mwBx8">Wheelbarrow</a> in Greece.<sup about="#mwt836" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-274" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-274"}}'><a href="#cite_note-274" id="mwByA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwByE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByI">[</span>268<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByM">]</span></span></a></sup> First actual depiction of one (tomb mural) shows up in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwByQ">China</a> in 118 AD.<sup about="#mwt837" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-275" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-275"}}'><a href="#cite_note-275" id="mwByU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwByY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByc">[</span>269<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwByg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwByk"><b id="mwByo">By 400 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camera_obscura" title="Camera obscura" id="mwBys">Camera obscura</a> described by Mo-tzu (or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozi" title="Mozi" id="mwByw">Mozi</a>) in China.<sup about="#mwt840" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-276" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-276"}}'><a href="#cite_note-276" id="mwBy0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBy4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBy8">[</span>270<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzA">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwBzE" aria-labelledby="4th_century_BC"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="4th_century_BC">4th century BC</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: 4th century BC"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBzI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Musée_du_Louvre_-_Antiquités_égyptiennes_-_Salle_06_-_02f.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBzM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Musée_du_Louvre_-_Antiquités_égyptiennes_-_Salle_06_-_02f.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_-_Antiquit%C3%A9s_%C3%A9gyptiennes_-_Salle_06_-_02f.jpg/250px-Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_-_Antiquit%C3%A9s_%C3%A9gyptiennes_-_Salle_06_-_02f.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_-_Antiquit%C3%A9s_%C3%A9gyptiennes_-_Salle_06_-_02f.jpg/500px-Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_-_Antiquit%C3%A9s_%C3%A9gyptiennes_-_Salle_06_-_02f.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2560" data-file-height="1920" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBzQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwBzU">Egyptian reed pens inside ivory and wooden palettes, the Louvre<sup about="#mwt843" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-277" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-277"}}'><a href="#cite_note-277" id="mwBzY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzg">[</span>271<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzk">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwBzo"><li id="mwBzs"><b id="mwBzw">400 and 300 BC:</b> Invention of the concept of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/0" title="0" id="mwBz0">zero</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babylon" title="Babylon" id="mwBz4">Babylon</a> (now Iraq). It was invented independently by the  <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maya_civilization" title="Maya civilization" id="mwBz8">Maya</a> in the first few centuries AD.<sup about="#mwt846" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-278" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-278"}}'><a href="#cite_note-278" id="mwB0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0I">[</span>272<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB0Q"><b id="mwB0U">4th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trebuchet" title="Trebuchet" id="mwB0Y">Traction trebuchet</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_China#Ancient_China" title="History of China" id="mwB0c">Ancient China</a>.<sup about="#mwt849" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-O'Callaghan_279-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"O&apos;Callaghan"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-O&apos;Callaghan-279"}}'><a href="#cite_note-O'Callaghan-279" id="mwB0g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0o">[</span>273<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB0w"><b id="mwB00">4th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gear" title="Gear" id="mwB04">Gears</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_China#Ancient_China" title="History of China" id="mwB08">Ancient China</a>.<sup about="#mwt852" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-280" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-280"}}'><a href="#cite_note-280" id="mwB1A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1I">[</span>274<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB1Q"><b id="mwB1U">4th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_pen" title="Reed pen" id="mwB1Y">Reed pens</a>, utilising a split nib, were used to write with ink on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papyrus" title="Papyrus" id="mwB1c">Papyrus</a> in Egypt.<sup about="#mwt853" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-O'Callaghan_279-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"O&apos;Callaghan"}}'><a href="#cite_note-O'Callaghan-279" id="mwB1g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1o">[</span>273<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB1w"><b id="mwB10">4th century BC:</b> Nailed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horseshoe" title="Horseshoe" id="mwB14">horseshoe</a>, with 4 bronze shoes found in an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_civilization" title="Etruscan civilization" id="mwB18">Etruscan tomb</a>.<sup about="#mwt856" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-281" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-281"}}'><a href="#cite_note-281" id="mwB2A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2I">[</span>275<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB2Q"><b id="mwB2U">375 BC – 350 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horse_mill" title="Horse mill" id="mwB2Y">Animal-driven rotary mill</a> in Carthage.<sup about="#mwt857" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTECurtis2008376_282-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTECurtis2008376"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECurtis2008376-282"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Curtis"},"2":{"wt":"2008"},"p":{"wt":"376"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTECurtis2008376-282" id="mwB2c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2k">[</span>276<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB2o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt860" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEde_Vos2011178_283-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEde Vos2011178"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEde_Vos2011178-283"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"de Vos"},"2":{"wt":"2011"},"p":{"wt":"178"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEde_Vos2011178-283" id="mwB2s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB2w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB20">[</span>277<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB24">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB28"><b id="mwB3A">By the late 4th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corporation" title="Corporation" id="mwB3E">Corporations</a> in either the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurya_Empire" title="Maurya Empire" id="mwB3I">Maurya Empire</a> of India<sup about="#mwt863" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-284" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-284"}}'><a href="#cite_note-284" id="mwB3M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3U">[</span>278<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB3Y">]</span></span></a></sup> or in Ancient Rome (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collegium_(ancient_Rome)" title="Collegium (ancient Rome)" id="mwB3c">Collegium</a>).</li>
<li id="mwB3g"><b id="mwB3k">Late 4th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheque" title="Cheque" id="mwB3o">Cheque</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurya_Empire" title="Maurya Empire" id="mwB3s">Maurya Empire</a> of India.<sup about="#mwt866" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-285" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-285"}}'><a href="#cite_note-285" id="mwB3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB30"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB34">[</span>279<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB38">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB4A"><b id="mwB4E">Late 4th century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formal_system" title="Formal system" id="mwB4I">Formal systems</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pāṇini" title="Pāṇini" id="mwB4M">Pāṇini</a> in India, possibly during the reign of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chandragupta_Maurya" title="Chandragupta Maurya" id="mwB4Q">Chandragupta Maurya</a>.<sup about="#mwt867" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-286" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-286"}}'><a href="#cite_note-286" id="mwB4U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB4Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4c">[</span>280<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB4g">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB4k"><b id="mwB4o">4th to 3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zinc_mining#History" title="Zinc mining" id="mwB4s">Zinc production</a> in North-Western <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India" title="India" id="mwB4w">India</a> during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurya_Empire" title="Maurya Empire" id="mwB40">Maurya Empire</a>.<sup about="#mwt868" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-287" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-287"}}'><a href="#cite_note-287" id="mwB44"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB48"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5A">[</span>281<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5E">]</span></span></a></sup> The earliest known zinc mines and smelting sites are from Zawar, near <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Udaipur" title="Udaipur" id="mwB5I">Udaipur</a>, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rajasthan" title="Rajasthan" id="mwB5M">Rajasthan</a>.<sup about="#mwt871" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-288" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-288"}}'><a href="#cite_note-288" id="mwB5Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5Y">[</span>282<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5c">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt874" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-289" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-289"}}'><a href="#cite_note-289" id="mwB5g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB5k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5o">[</span>283<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB5s">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwB5w" aria-labelledby="3rd_century_BC"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="3rd_century_BC">3rd century BC</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: 3rd century BC"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB50"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Making_Paper_4.PNG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB54"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Making_Paper_4.PNG" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Making_Paper_4.PNG/250px-Making_Paper_4.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Making_Paper_4.PNG/330px-Making_Paper_4.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="352" data-file-height="510" data-file-type="bitmap" height="203" width="140" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB58"/></a><figcaption id="mwB6A">An illustration depicting the papermaking process in Han dynasty China.</figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwB6E"><li id="mwB6I"><b id="mwB6M">3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Analog_computer" title="Analog computer" id="mwB6Q">Analog computers</a> in the Hellenistic world (see e.g. the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antikythera_mechanism" title="Antikythera mechanism" id="mwB6U">Antikythera mechanism</a>), possibly in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhodes" title="Rhodes" id="mwB6Y">Rhodes</a>.<sup about="#mwt877" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-290" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-290"}}'><a href="#cite_note-290" id="mwB6c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6k">[</span>284<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6o">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB6s"><b id="mwB6w">By at least the 3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archimedes'_screw" title="Archimedes' screw" id="mwB60">Archimedes' screw</a>, one of the earliest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydraulic" title="Hydraulic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB64">hydraulic</a> machines, was first used in the Nile river for irrigation purposes in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Egypt" title="Ancient Egypt" id="mwB68">Ancient Egypt</a><sup about="#mwt880" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-291" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-291"}}'><a href="#cite_note-291" id="mwB7A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7I">[</span>285<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB7Q"><b id="mwB7U">Early 3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lock_(water_transport)" title="Lock (water transport)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB7Y">Canal lock</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal_of_the_Pharaohs" title="Canal of the Pharaohs" id="mwB7c">Canal of the Pharaohs</a> under <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemy_II" title="Ptolemy II" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB7g">Ptolemy II</a> (283–246 BC) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellenistic_Egypt" title="Hellenistic Egypt" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB7k">Hellenistic Egypt</a><sup about="#mwt881" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-292" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-292"}}'><a href="#cite_note-292" id="mwB7o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB7s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB7w">[</span>286<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB70">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt882" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-293" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-293"}}'><a href="#cite_note-293" id="mwB74"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB78"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8A">[</span>287<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt883" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-294" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-294"}}'><a href="#cite_note-294" id="mwB8I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8Q">[</span>288<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8U">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB8Y"><b id="mwB8c">3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cam_(mechanism)" title="Cam (mechanism)" id="mwB8g">Cam</a> during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellenistic_period" title="Hellenistic period" id="mwB8k">Hellenistic period</a>, used in water-driven <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automata" title="Automata" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB8o">automata</a>.<sup about="#mwt885" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-295" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-295"}}'><a href="#cite_note-295" id="mwB8s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB80">[</span>289<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB84">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB88"><b id="mwB9A">By the 3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_wheel" title="Water wheel" id="mwB9E">Water wheel</a>. The origin is unclear: Indian Pali texts dating to the 4th century BCE refer to the <i id="mwB9I">cakkavattaka</i>, which later commentaries describe as <i id="mwB9M">arahatta-ghati-yanta</i> (machine with wheel-pots attached). <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helaine_Selin" title="Helaine Selin" id="mwB9Q">Helaine Selin</a> suggests that the device existed in Persia before 350 BC.<sup about="#mwt888" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-296" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-296"}}'><a href="#cite_note-296" id="mwB9U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9c">[</span>290<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9g">]</span></span></a></sup> The clearest description of the water wheel and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escapement#Liquid-driven_escapements" title="Escapement" id="mwB9k">liquid-driven escapement</a> is provided by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philo_of_Byzantium" title="Philo of Byzantium" id="mwB9o">Philo of Byzantium</a> (c. 280 – 220 BC) in the Hellenistic kingdoms.<sup about="#mwt891" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-297" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-297"}}'><a href="#cite_note-297" id="mwB9s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB90">[</span>291<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB94">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB98"><b id="mwB-A">3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gimbal" title="Gimbal" id="mwB-E">Gimbal</a> described by Philo of Byzantium<sup about="#mwt894" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-298" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-298"}}'><a href="#cite_note-298" id="mwB-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-Q">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-U">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB-Y"><b id="mwB-c">Late 3rd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dry_dock" title="Dry dock" id="mwB-g">Dry dock</a> under <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemy_IV" title="Ptolemy IV" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-k">Ptolemy IV</a> (221–205 BC) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellenistic_Egypt" title="Hellenistic Egypt" class="mw-redirect" id="mwB-o">Hellenistic Egypt</a><sup about="#mwt897" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-299" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-299"}}'><a href="#cite_note-299" id="mwB-s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-0">[</span>293<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwB-8"><b id="mwB_A">3rd century BC – 2nd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blast_furnace" title="Blast furnace" id="mwB_E">Blast furnace</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_China#Ancient_China" title="History of China" id="mwB_I">Ancient China</a>: The earliest discovered blast furnaces in China date to the 3rd and 2nd centuries BC, although most sites are from the later <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty" title="Han dynasty" id="mwB_M">Han dynasty</a>.<sup about="#mwt898" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wagner_7_36_37_64_68_269-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wagner 7 36 37 64 68"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wagner_7_36_37_64_68-269" id="mwB_Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_Y">[</span>263<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_c">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt899" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-300" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-300"}}'><a href="#cite_note-300" id="mwB_g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_o">[</span>294<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_s">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB_w"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Museum_für_Antike_Schiffahrt,_Mainz_02._Spritsail.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB_0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Museum_für_Antike_Schiffahrt,_Mainz_02._Spritsail.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Museum_f%C3%BCr_Antike_Schifffahrt%2C_Mainz_02._Spritsail.jpg/250px-Museum_f%C3%BCr_Antike_Schifffahrt%2C_Mainz_02._Spritsail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Museum_f%C3%BCr_Antike_Schifffahrt%2C_Mainz_02._Spritsail.jpg/500px-Museum_f%C3%BCr_Antike_Schifffahrt%2C_Mainz_02._Spritsail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2000" data-file-height="1130" data-file-type="bitmap" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB_4"/></a><figcaption id="mwB_8">The earliest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fore-and-aft_rig" title="Fore-and-aft rig" id="mwCAA">fore-and-aft rigs</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spritsails" title="Spritsails" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCAE">spritsails</a>, appeared in the 2nd century BC in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aegean_Sea" title="Aegean Sea" id="mwCAI">Aegean Sea</a> on small Greek craft.<sup about="#mwt902" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Casson_1995,_243–245_301-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Casson 1995, 243–245"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Casson_1995,_243–245-301"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Casson_1995,_243–245-301" id="mwCAM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAU">[</span>295<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAY">]</span></span></a></sup> Here a spritsail used on a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire" title="Roman Empire" id="mwCAc">Roman</a> merchant ship (3rd century AD).</figcaption></figure>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwCAg" aria-labelledby="2nd_century_BC"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="2nd_century_BC">2nd century BC</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: 2nd century BC"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt903" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCAk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main list","href":"./Template:Main_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2nd century BC#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt904" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt903" id="mwCAo">For a more comprehensive list, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_century_BC#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="2nd century BC">2nd century BC §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a>.</div>
<ul id="mwCAs"><li id="mwCAw"><b id="mwCA0">2nd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper" title="Paper" id="mwCA4">Paper</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty" title="Han dynasty" id="mwCA8">Han dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCBA">China</a><sup about="#mwt905" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-303" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-303"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Although it is recorded that the Han dynasty (202 BC – AD 220) court eunuch [[Cai Lun]] (born c. 50–121 AD) invented the pulp papermaking process and established the use of new raw materials used in making paper, ancient padding and wrapping paper artifacts dating to the 2nd century BC have been found in China, the oldest example of pulp papermaking [[History of cartography#China|being a map]] from [[Fangmatan]], [[Gansu]].&lt;ref>Buisseret (1998), 12.&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-303" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwCBE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBM">[</span>g<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCBU"><b id="mwCBY">206 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compass" title="Compass" id="mwCBc">Compass</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty" title="Han dynasty" id="mwCBg">Han dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCBk">China</a><sup about="#mwt913" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-304" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-304"}}'><a href="#cite_note-304" id="mwCBo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBw">[</span>297<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCB0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCB4"><b id="mwCB8">Early 2nd century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astrolabe" title="Astrolabe" id="mwCCA">Astrolabe</a> invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollonius_of_Perga" title="Apollonius of Perga" id="mwCCE">Apollonius of Perga</a><sup about="#mwt916" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-305" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-305"}}'><a href="#cite_note-305" id="mwCCI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCQ">[</span>298<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCU">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwCCY" aria-labelledby="1st_century_BC"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1st_century_BC">1st century BC</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: 1st century BC"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwCCc"><li id="mwCCg"><b id="mwCCk">1st century BC:</b> Segmental <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arch_bridge" title="Arch bridge" id="mwCCo">arch bridge</a> (e.g. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pont-Saint-Martin_(bridge)" title="Pont-Saint-Martin (bridge)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCCs">Pont-Saint-Martin</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponte_San_Lorenzo" title="Ponte San Lorenzo" id="mwCCw">Ponte San Lorenzo</a>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy" title="Italy" id="mwCC0">Italy</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Republic" title="Roman Republic" id="mwCC4">Roman Republic</a><sup about="#mwt919" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-306" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-306"}}'><a href="#cite_note-306" id="mwCC8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDE">[</span>299<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt922" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-307" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-307"}}'><a href="#cite_note-307" id="mwCDM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDU">[</span>300<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCDc"><b id="mwCDg">1st century BC:</b> News bulletin during the reign of Julius Caesar.<sup about="#mwt925" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Chisholm_1911,_p._159_308-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Chisholm 1911, p. 159"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Chisholm_1911,_p._159-308"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Chisholm_1911,_p._159-308" id="mwCDk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDs">[</span>301<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDw">]</span></span></a></sup> A paper form, i.e. the earliest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newspaper" title="Newspaper" id="mwCD0">newspaper</a>, later appeared during the late Han dynasty in the form of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dibao" title="Dibao" id="mwCD4">Dibao</a>.<sup about="#mwt928" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-309" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-309"}}'><a href="#cite_note-309" id="mwCD8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEE">[</span>302<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt929" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-if30_310-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"if30"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-if30-310"}}'><a href="#cite_note-if30-310" id="mwCEM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEU">[</span>303<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt930" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-311" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-311"}}'><a href="#cite_note-311" id="mwCEc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEk">[</span>304<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCEs"><b id="mwCEw">1st century BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arch_dam" title="Arch dam" id="mwCE0">Arch dam</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glanum_Dam" title="Glanum Dam" id="mwCE4">Glanum Dam</a>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallia_Narbonensis" title="Gallia Narbonensis" id="mwCE8">Gallia Narbonensis</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Republic" title="Roman Republic" id="mwCFA">Roman Republic</a> (see also <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Roman_dams" title="List of Roman dams" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCFE">List of Roman dams</a>)<sup about="#mwt933" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-312" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-312"}}'><a href="#cite_note-312" id="mwCFI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFQ">[</span>305<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt934" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-313" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-313"}}'><a href="#cite_note-313" id="mwCFY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFg">[</span>306<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt937" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-314" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-314"}}'><a href="#cite_note-314" id="mwCFo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFw">[</span>307<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt940" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-315" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-315"}}'><a href="#cite_note-315" id="mwCF4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCF8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGA">[</span>308<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt943" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-316" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-316"}}'><a href="#cite_note-316" id="mwCGI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGQ">[</span>309<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCGY"><b id="mwCGc">Before 40 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trip_hammer" title="Trip hammer" id="mwCGg">Trip hammer</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCGk">China</a><sup about="#mwt944" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-needham_volume_4_part_2_184_317-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"needham volume 4 part 2 184"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-needham_volume_4_part_2_184-317"}}'><a href="#cite_note-needham_volume_4_part_2_184-317" id="mwCGo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGw">[</span>310<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCG0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCG4"><b id="mwCG8">37 BC – 14 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glass_blowing" title="Glass blowing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCHA">Glass blowing</a> developed in Jerusalem.<sup about="#mwt947" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Avigad_318-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Avigad"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Avigad-318"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Avigad-318" id="mwCHE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHM">[</span>311<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt950" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Tattona_319-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Tattona"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Tattona-319"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Tattona-319" id="mwCHU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHc">[</span>312<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt953" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Stern_320-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Stern"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Stern-320"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Stern-320" id="mwCHk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHs">[</span>313<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCH0"><b id="mwCH4">Before 25 BC:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reverse_overshot_water_wheel" title="Reverse overshot water wheel" id="mwCH8">Reverse overshot water wheel</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_engineering" title="Roman engineering" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCIA">Roman engineers</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_Tinto_(river)" title="Rio Tinto (river)" id="mwCIE">Rio Tinto</a>, Spain<sup about="#mwt954" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-321" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-321"}}'><a href="#cite_note-321" id="mwCII"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIQ">[</span>314<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIU">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwCIY" aria-labelledby="1st_century_AD"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1st_century_AD">1st century AD</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: 1st century AD"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwCIc"><li id="mwCIg"><b id="mwCIk">1st century AD:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeolipile" title="Aeolipile" id="mwCIo">aeolipile</a>, a simple <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_turbine" title="Steam turbine" id="mwCIs">steam turbine</a> is recorded by Hero of Alexandria.<sup about="#mwt957" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-322" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-322"}}'><a href="#cite_note-322" id="mwCIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCI0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI4">[</span>315<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCJA"><b id="mwCJE">1st century AD:</b> The first use of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Respiratory_protective_equipment" title="Respiratory protective equipment" id="mwCJI">respiratory protective equipment</a> is documented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pliny_the_Elder" title="Pliny the Elder" id="mwCJM">Pliny the Elder</a> (<abbr title="circa" about="#mwt958" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCJQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"circa","href":"./Template:Circa"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"23 AD"}},"i":0}}]}'>c.</abbr><span style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt958" id="mwCJU"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>23 AD</span>–79) using animal bladder skins to protect workers in Roman mines from red lead oxide dust.<sup about="#mwt961" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-323" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-323"}}'><a href="#cite_note-323" id="mwCJY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJg">[</span>316<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCJo"><b id="mwCJs">1st century AD:</b> Oldest surviving <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine" title="Wine" id="mwCJw">wine</a>.<sup about="#mwt964" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-324" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-324"}}'><a href="#cite_note-324" id="mwCJ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJ8">[</span>317<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCKE"><b id="mwCKI">1st century AD:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vending_machine" title="Vending machine" id="mwCKM">Vending machines</a> invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hero_of_Alexandria" title="Hero of Alexandria" id="mwCKQ">Hero of Alexandria</a><sup about="#mwt967" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-325" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-325"}}'><a href="#cite_note-325" id="mwCKU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKc">[</span>318<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwCKk" aria-labelledby="2nd_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="2nd_century">2nd century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section: 2nd century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt968" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCKo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2nd century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt969" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt968" id="mwCKs">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2nd_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="2nd century">2nd century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<ul id="mwCKw"><li id="mwCK0"><b id="mwCK4">132:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seismometer" title="Seismometer" id="mwCK8">Seismometer</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pendulum" title="Pendulum" id="mwCLA">pendulum</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty" title="Han dynasty" id="mwCLE">Han dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCLI">China</a>, built by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhang_Heng" title="Zhang Heng" id="mwCLM">Zhang Heng</a>. It is a large metal urn-shaped instrument which employed either a suspended pendulum or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverted_pendulum" title="Inverted pendulum" id="mwCLQ">inverted pendulum</a> acting on inertia, like the ground tremors from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earthquake" title="Earthquake" id="mwCLU">earthquakes</a>, to dislodge a metal ball by a lever trip device.<sup about="#mwt972" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-326" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-326"}}'><a href="#cite_note-326" id="mwCLY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLg">[</span>319<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt975" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-327" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-327"}}'><a href="#cite_note-327" id="mwCLo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLw">[</span>320<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCL0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCL4"><b id="mwCL8">2nd century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carding" title="Carding" id="mwCMA">Carding</a> in India.<sup about="#mwt976" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Baber1_328-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Baber1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Baber1-328"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Baber1-328" id="mwCME"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCMI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMM">[</span>321<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwCMU" aria-labelledby="3rd_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="3rd_century">3rd century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17" title="Edit section: 3rd century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCMY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Römische_Sägemühle.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCMc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Römische_Sägemühle.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/R%C3%B6mische_S%C3%A4gem%C3%BChle.svg/250px-R%C3%B6mische_S%C3%A4gem%C3%BChle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/R%C3%B6mische_S%C3%A4gem%C3%BChle.svg/500px-R%C3%B6mische_S%C3%A4gem%C3%BChle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="800" data-file-height="500" data-file-type="drawing" height="156" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCMg"/></a><figcaption id="mwCMk">Schematic of the Roman <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hierapolis_sawmill" title="Hierapolis sawmill" id="mwCMo">Hierapolis sawmill</a>. Dated to the 3rd<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCMs"> </span>century<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCMw"> </span>AD, it is the earliest known machine to incorporate a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crank_(mechanism)" title="Crank (mechanism)" id="mwCM0">crank</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connecting_rod" title="Connecting rod" id="mwCM4">connecting rod</a> mechanism.<sup about="#mwt977" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ritti,_Grewe,_Kessener_2007,_140,_161_329-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ritti, Grewe, Kessener 2007, 140, 161"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ritti,_Grewe,_Kessener_2007,_140,_161-329"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ritti,_Grewe,_Kessener_2007,_140,_161-329" id="mwCM8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNE">[</span>322<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt981" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Grewe_2009,_429_330-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Grewe 2009, 429"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Grewe_2009,_429-330"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Grewe_2009,_429-330" id="mwCNM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNU">[</span>323<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt982" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Grewe_2010_331-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Grewe 2010"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Grewe_2010-331"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Grewe_2010-331" id="mwCNc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNk">[</span>324<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNo">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwCNs"><li id="mwCNw"><b id="mwCN0">By at least the 3rd century:</b> Crystallized sugar in India.<sup about="#mwt985" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-332" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-332"}}'><a href="#cite_note-332" id="mwCN4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCN8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOA">[</span>325<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCOI"><b id="mwCOM">Early 3rd century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodblock_printing" title="Woodblock printing" id="mwCOQ">Woodblock printing</a> is invented in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_dynasty" title="Han dynasty" id="mwCOU">Han dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCOY">China</a> at sometime before 220 AD. This made China become the world's first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Print_culture" title="Print culture" id="mwCOc">print culture</a>.<sup about="#mwt988" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-333" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-333"}}'><a href="#cite_note-333" id="mwCOg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOo">[</span>326<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCOw"><b id="mwCO0">Late 3rd century – Early 4th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_turbine" title="Water turbine" id="mwCO4">Water turbine</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire" title="Roman Empire" id="mwCO8">Roman Empire</a> in modern-day <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunisia" title="Tunisia" id="mwCPA">Tunisia</a>.<sup about="#mwt989" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-334" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-334"}}'><a href="#cite_note-334" id="mwCPE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPM">[</span>327<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt992" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-335" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-335"}}'><a href="#cite_note-335" id="mwCPU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPc">[</span>328<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt993" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-336" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-336"}}'><a href="#cite_note-336" id="mwCPk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPs">[</span>329<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPw">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwCP0" aria-labelledby="4th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="4th_century">4th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18" title="Edit section: 4th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt994" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCP4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"4th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt995" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt994" id="mwCP8">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="4th century">4th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<ul id="mwCQA"><li id="mwCQE"><b id="mwCQI">280 – 550:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaturanga" title="Chaturanga" id="mwCQM">Chaturanga</a>, a precursor of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chess" title="Chess" id="mwCQQ">Chess</a> was invented in India during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gupta_Empire" title="Gupta Empire" id="mwCQU">Gupta Empire</a>.<sup about="#mwt998" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-337" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-337"}}'><a href="#cite_note-337" id="mwCQY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQg">[</span>330<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1001" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-338" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-338"}}'><a href="#cite_note-338" id="mwCQo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQw">[</span>331<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQ0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1004" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-339" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-339"}}'><a href="#cite_note-339" id="mwCQ4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQ8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRA">[</span>332<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCRI"><b id="mwCRM">4th century:</b> Roman <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dichroic_glass" title="Dichroic glass" id="mwCRQ">Dichroic glass</a>, which displays one of two different colors depending on lighting conditions.</li>
<li id="mwCRU"><b id="mwCRY">4th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simple_suspension_bridge#History" title="Simple suspension bridge" id="mwCRc">Simple suspension bridge</a>, independently invented in Pre-Columbian South America,  and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindu_Kush" title="Hindu Kush" id="mwCRg">Hindu Kush</a> range, of present-day <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afghanistan" title="Afghanistan" id="mwCRk">Afghanistan</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistan" title="Pakistan" id="mwCRo">Pakistan</a>. With Han dynasty travelers noting bridges being constructed from 3 or more vines or 3 ropes.<sup about="#mwt1007" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-needham_1986_volume_4_part_3_187−189_340-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"needham 1986 volume 4 part 3 187−189"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-needham_1986_volume_4_part_3_187−189-340"}}'><a href="#cite_note-needham_1986_volume_4_part_3_187−189-340" id="mwCRs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCR0">[</span>333<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCR4">]</span></span></a></sup> Later bridges constructed utilizing cables of iron chains appeared in Tibet.<sup about="#mwt1010" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Peters_341-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Peters"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Peters-341"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Peters-341" id="mwCR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSE">[</span>334<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1011" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-342" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-342"}}'><a href="#cite_note-342" id="mwCSM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSU">[</span>335<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCSc"><b id="mwCSg">4th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fishing_reel" title="Fishing reel" id="mwCSk">Fishing reel</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_China#Ancient_China" title="History of China" id="mwCSo">Ancient China</a>: In literary records, the earliest evidence of the fishing reel comes from a 4th-century AD<sup about="#mwt1012" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-343" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-343"}}'><a href="#cite_note-343" id="mwCSs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCS0">[</span>336<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCS4">]</span></span></a></sup> work entitled <i id="mwCS8">Lives of Famous Immortals</i>.<sup about="#mwt1013" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-344" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-344"}}'><a href="#cite_note-344" id="mwCTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTI">[</span>337<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCTQ"><b id="mwCTU">347:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_Well" title="Oil Well" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCTY">Oil Wells</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borehole" title="Borehole" id="mwCTc">Borehole</a> drilling in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCTg">China</a>. Such wells could reach depths of up to 240<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCTk"> </span>m (790<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwCTo"> </span>ft).<sup about="#mwt1016" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ASTM_345-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ASTM"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ASTM-345"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ASTM-345" id="mwCTs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCT0">[</span>338<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCT4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCT8">4th century – 5th century: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddle_wheel_boat" title="Paddle wheel boat" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCUA">Paddle wheel boat</a> (in <i id="mwCUE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_rebus_bellicis" title="De rebus bellicis" id="mwCUI">De rebus bellicis</a></i>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Empire" title="Roman Empire" id="mwCUM">Roman Empire</a><sup about="#mwt1017" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-346" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-346"}}'><a href="#cite_note-346" id="mwCUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCUU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUY">[</span>339<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUc">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwCUg" aria-labelledby="5th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="5th_century">5th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section: 5th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1018" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCUk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"5th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1019" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1018" id="mwCUo">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="5th century">5th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<ul id="mwCUs"><li id="mwCUw"><b id="mwCU0">400:</b> The construction of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_pillar_of_Delhi" title="Iron pillar of Delhi" id="mwCU4">Iron pillar of Delhi</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathura" title="Mathura" id="mwCU8">Mathura</a> by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gupta_Empire" title="Gupta Empire" id="mwCVA">Gupta Empire</a> shows the development of rust-resistant ferrous metallurgy in Ancient India,<sup about="#mwt1020" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-347" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-347"}}'><a href="#cite_note-347" id="mwCVE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCVI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVM">[</span>340<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1023" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-348" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-348"}}'><a href="#cite_note-348" id="mwCVU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCVY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVc">[</span>341<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVg">]</span></span></a></sup> although original texts do not survive to detail the specific processes invented in this period.</li>
<li id="mwCVk"><b id="mwCVo">5th century:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horse_collar" title="Horse collar" id="mwCVs">horse collar</a> as a fully developed collar harness is developed in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_and_Southern_dynasties" title="Northern and Southern dynasties" id="mwCVw">Northern and Southern dynasties</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCV0">China</a> during the 5th century AD.<sup about="#mwt1024" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-needham_volume_4_part_2_28_349-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"needham volume 4 part 2 28"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-needham_volume_4_part_2_28-349"}}'><a href="#cite_note-needham_volume_4_part_2_28-349" id="mwCV4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCV8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWA">[</span>342<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWE">]</span></span></a></sup> The earliest depiction of it is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunhuang" title="Dunhuang" id="mwCWI">Dunhuang</a> cave <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mural" title="Mural" id="mwCWM">mural</a> from the Chinese <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Wei" title="Northern Wei" id="mwCWQ">Northern Wei</a> dynasty, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Painting" title="Painting" id="mwCWU">painting</a> dated to 477–499.<sup about="#mwt1025" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-needham_volume_4_part_2_322_350-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"needham volume 4 part 2 322"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-needham_volume_4_part_2_322-350"}}'><a href="#cite_note-needham_volume_4_part_2_322-350" id="mwCWY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCWc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWg">[</span>343<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCWo"><b id="mwCWs">5th century – 6th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pointed_arch_bridge" title="Pointed arch bridge" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCWw">Pointed arch bridge</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karamagara_Bridge" title="Karamagara Bridge" id="mwCW0">Karamagara Bridge</a>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cappadocia" title="Cappadocia" id="mwCW4">Cappadocia</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Roman_Empire" title="Eastern Roman Empire" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCW8">Eastern Roman Empire</a><sup about="#mwt1028" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-351" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-351"}}'><a href="#cite_note-351" id="mwCXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCXE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXI">[</span>344<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1029" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-352" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-352"}}'><a href="#cite_note-352" id="mwCXQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCXU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXY">[</span>345<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXc">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCXg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nepali_charka_in_action.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCXk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Nepali_charka_in_action.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Nepali_charka_in_action.jpg/250px-Nepali_charka_in_action.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Nepali_charka_in_action.jpg/500px-Nepali_charka_in_action.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1073" data-file-height="720" data-file-type="bitmap" height="168" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCXo"/></a><figcaption id="mwCXs">A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demographics_of_Nepal" title="Demographics of Nepal" id="mwCXw">Nepali</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinning_wheel" title="Spinning wheel" id="mwCX0">Charkha</a> in action</figcaption></figure>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="20" id="mwCX4" aria-labelledby="6th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="6th_century">6th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20" title="Edit section: 6th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwCX8"><li id="mwCYA"><b id="mwCYE">By the 6th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incense_clock" title="Incense clock" id="mwCYI">Incense clock</a> in China.<sup about="#mwt1030" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Schafer161_353-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Schafer161"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Schafer161-353"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Schafer161-353" id="mwCYM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYU">[</span>346<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1031" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bedini69_354-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bedini69"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bedini69-354"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bedini69-354" id="mwCYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYk">[</span>347<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCYs"><b id="mwCYw">After 500:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charkha_(spinning_wheel)" title="Charkha (spinning wheel)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCY0">Charkha</a> (spinning wheel/cotton gin) invented in India (probably during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vakataka_dynasty" title="Vakataka dynasty" id="mwCY4">Vakataka dynasty</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maharashtra,_India" title="Maharashtra, India" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCY8">Maharashtra, India</a>), between 500 and 1000 A.D.<sup about="#mwt1034" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-355" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-355"}}'><a href="#cite_note-355" id="mwCZA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZI">[</span>348<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCZQ"><b id="mwCZU">563:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pendentive" title="Pendentive" id="mwCZY">Pendentive</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dome" title="Dome" id="mwCZc">dome</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hagia_Sophia" title="Hagia Sophia" id="mwCZg">Hagia Sophia</a>) in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantinople" title="Constantinople" id="mwCZk">Constantinople</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Roman_Empire" title="Eastern Roman Empire" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCZo">Eastern Roman Empire</a><sup about="#mwt1037" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-356" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-356"}}'><a href="#cite_note-356" id="mwCZs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZ0">[</span>349<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZ4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCZ8"><b id="mwCaA">577:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Match#Early_matches" title="Match" id="mwCaE">Sulfur matches</a> exist in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCaI">China</a><sup about="#mwt1040" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-357" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-357"}}'><a href="#cite_note-357" id="mwCaM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCaQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCaU">[</span>350<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCaY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1043" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-358" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-358"}}'><a href="#cite_note-358" id="mwCac"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCak">[</span>351<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCao">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCas"><b id="mwCaw">589:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toilet_paper" title="Toilet paper" id="mwCa0">Toilet paper</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sui_dynasty" title="Sui dynasty" id="mwCa4">Sui dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCa8">China</a>, first mentioned by the official <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yan_Zhitui" title="Yan Zhitui" id="mwCbA">Yan Zhitui</a> (531–591), with full evidence of continual use in subsequent dynasties.<sup about="#mwt1044" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-needham_volume_5_part_1_123_359-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"needham volume 5 part 1 123"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-needham_volume_5_part_1_123-359"}}'><a href="#cite_note-needham_volume_5_part_1_123-359" id="mwCbE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCbI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbM">[</span>352<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1045" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-360" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-360"}}'><a href="#cite_note-360" id="mwCbU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCbY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbc">[</span>353<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="21" id="mwCbk" aria-labelledby="7th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="7th_century">7th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21" title="Edit section: 7th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1046" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCbo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"7th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1047" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1046" id="mwCbs">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="7th century">7th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<ul id="mwCbw"><li id="mwCb0"><b id="mwCb4">619:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toothbrush" title="Toothbrush" id="mwCb8">Toothbrush</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCcA">China</a> during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty" title="Tang dynasty" id="mwCcE">Tang dynasty</a><sup about="#mwt1050" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kumar-412413_361-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"kumar-412413"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-kumar-412413-361"}}'><a href="#cite_note-kumar-412413-361" id="mwCcI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCcM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcQ">[</span>354<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCcY"><b id="mwCcc">672:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_fire" title="Greek fire" id="mwCcg">Greek fire</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantinople" title="Constantinople" id="mwCck">Constantinople</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_Empire" title="Byzantine Empire" id="mwCco">Byzantine Empire</a>: Greek fire, an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incendiary_device" title="Incendiary device" id="mwCcs">incendiary weapon</a> likely based on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petroleum" title="Petroleum" id="mwCcw">petroleum</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naphtha" title="Naphtha" id="mwCc0">naphtha</a>, is invented by Kallinikos, a Lebanese Greek refugee from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baalbek" title="Baalbek" id="mwCc4">Baalbek</a>, as described by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theophanes_the_Confessor" title="Theophanes the Confessor" id="mwCc8">Theophanes</a>.<sup about="#mwt1052" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-362" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-362"}}'><a href="#cite_note-362" id="mwCdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdI">[</span>355<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdM">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the historicity and exact chronology of this account is dubious,<sup about="#mwt1054" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-363" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-363"}}'><a href="#cite_note-363" id="mwCdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdY">[</span>356<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdc">]</span></span></a></sup> and it could be that Kallinikos merely introduced an improved version of an established weapon.<sup about="#mwt1057" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-364" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-364"}}'><a href="#cite_note-364" id="mwCdg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdo">[</span>357<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCds">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCdw"><b id="mwCd0">7th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banknote" title="Banknote" id="mwCd4">Banknote</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty" title="Tang dynasty" id="mwCd8">Tang dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCeA">China</a>: The banknote is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economy_of_the_Song_dynasty#The_world's_first_paper_money" title="Economy of the Song dynasty" id="mwCeE">first developed in China</a> during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty" title="Tang dynasty" id="mwCeI">Tang</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_dynasty" title="Song dynasty" id="mwCeM">Song</a> dynasties, starting in the 7th century. Its roots are in merchant <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Receipt" title="Receipt" id="mwCeQ">receipts</a> of deposit during the Tang dynasty (618–907), as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_occupations#The_shang_(商)" title="Four occupations" id="mwCeU">merchants</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wholesaler" title="Wholesaler" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCeY">wholesalers</a> desire to avoid the heavy bulk of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Chinese_coinage" title="Ancient Chinese coinage" id="mwCec">copper coinage</a> in large commercial transactions.<sup about="#mwt1058" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ebrey,_Walthall,_and_Palais_365-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ebrey, Walthall, and Palais"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ebrey,_Walthall,_and_Palais-365"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ebrey,_Walthall,_and_Palais-365" id="mwCeg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCek"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeo">[</span>358<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCes">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1059" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bowman_366-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bowman"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bowman-366"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bowman-366" id="mwCew"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCe0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCe4">[</span>359<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCe8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1060" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-gernet_1962_80_367-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"gernet 1962 80"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-gernet_1962_80-367"}}'><a href="#cite_note-gernet_1962_80-367" id="mwCfA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCfE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfI">[</span>360<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCfQ"><b id="mwCfU">7th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porcelain" title="Porcelain" id="mwCfY">Porcelain</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty" title="Tang dynasty" id="mwCfc">Tang dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCfg">China</a>: True porcelain is manufactured in northern China from roughly the beginning of the Tang dynasty in the 7th century, while true porcelain was not manufactured in southern China until about 300 years later, during the early 10th century.<sup about="#mwt1061" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-368" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-368"}}'><a href="#cite_note-368" id="mwCfk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCfo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfs">[</span>361<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfw">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwCf0" aria-labelledby="8th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="8th_century">8th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22" title="Edit section: 8th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1062" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCf4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"8th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1063" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1062" id="mwCf8">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="8th century">8th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwCgA" aria-labelledby="9th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="9th_century">9th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23" title="Edit section: 9th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1064" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCgE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"9th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1065" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1064" id="mwCgI">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/9th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="9th century">9th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCgM"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Mōko_Shūrai_Ekotoba.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCgQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Mōko_Shūrai_Ekotoba.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg/250px-M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg/500px-M%C5%8Dko_Sh%C5%ABrai_Ekotoba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2520" data-file-height="843" data-file-type="bitmap" height="84" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCgU"/></a><figcaption id="mwCgY">A Mongol bomb thrown against a charging <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan" title="Japan" id="mwCgc">Japanese</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samurai" title="Samurai" id="mwCgg">samurai</a> during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Japan" title="Mongol invasions of Japan" id="mwCgk">Mongol invasions of Japan</a> after founding the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuan_dynasty" title="Yuan dynasty" id="mwCgo">Yuan dynasty</a>, 1281.</figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwCgs"><li id="mwCgw"><b id="mwCg0">9th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunpowder" title="Gunpowder" id="mwCg4">Gunpowder</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty" title="Tang dynasty" id="mwCg8">Tang dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwChA">China</a>: Gunpowder is, according to prevailing academic consensus, discovered in the 9th century by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_alchemy" title="Chinese alchemy" id="mwChE">Chinese alchemists</a> searching for an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elixir_of_life" title="Elixir of life" id="mwChI">elixir of immortality</a>.<sup about="#mwt1068" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Jack_Kelly_2005_369-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Jack Kelly 2005"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Jack_Kelly_2005-369"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Jack_Kelly_2005-369" id="mwChM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwChQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChU">[</span>362<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChY">]</span></span></a></sup> Evidence of gunpowder's first use in China comes from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Dynasties_and_Ten_Kingdoms_period" title="Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms period" id="mwChc">Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms period</a> (618–907).<sup about="#mwt1069" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-370" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-370"}}'><a href="#cite_note-370" id="mwChg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwChk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCho">[</span>363<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChs">]</span></span></a></sup> The earliest known recorded recipes for gunpowder are written by Zeng Gongliang, Ding Du, and Yang Weide in the <i id="mwChw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wujing_Zongyao" title="Wujing Zongyao" id="mwCh0">Wujing Zongyao</a></i>, a military manuscript compiled in 1044 during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_dynasty" title="Song dynasty" id="mwCh4">Song dynasty</a> (960–1279).<sup about="#mwt1070" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-371" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-371"}}'><a href="#cite_note-371" id="mwCh8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCiA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiE">[</span>364<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1071" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-gernet_1996_311_372-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"gernet 1996 311"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-gernet_1996_311-372"}}'><a href="#cite_note-gernet_1996_311-372" id="mwCiM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiU">[</span>365<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1072" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-373" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-373"}}'><a href="#cite_note-373" id="mwCic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCik">[</span>366<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCio">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCis"><b id="mwCiw">9th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Playing_card" title="Playing card" id="mwCi0">Playing card</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty" title="Tang dynasty" id="mwCi4">Tang dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCi8">China</a><sup about="#mwt1074" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-374" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-374"}}'><a href="#cite_note-374" id="mwCjA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjI">[</span>367<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1077" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wilkinson_375-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wilkinson"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-wilkinson-375"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wilkinson-375" id="mwCjQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjY">[</span>368<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1080" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-lo_2000_390_376-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"lo 2000 390"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-lo_2000_390-376"}}'><a href="#cite_note-lo_2000_390-376" id="mwCjg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjo">[</span>369<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1082" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-377" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-377"}}'><a href="#cite_note-377" id="mwCjw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCj0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCj4">[</span>370<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCj8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1084" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-378" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-378"}}'><a href="#cite_note-378" id="mwCkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCkE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkI">[</span>371<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkM">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="24" id="mwCkQ" aria-labelledby="10th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="10th_century">10th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24" title="Edit section: 10th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1085" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCkU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"10th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1086" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1085" id="mwCkY">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/10th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="10th century">10th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<ul id="mwCkc"><li id="mwCkg"><b id="mwCkk">10th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_lance" title="Fire lance" id="mwCko">Fire lance</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_dynasty" title="Song dynasty" id="mwCks">Song dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCkw">China</a>, developed in the 10th century with a tube of first bamboo and later on metal that shot a weak <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunpowder" title="Gunpowder" id="mwCk0">gunpowder</a> blast of flame and shrapnel, its earliest depiction is a painting found at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunhuang" title="Dunhuang" id="mwCk4">Dunhuang</a>.<sup about="#mwt1087" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-379" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-379"}}'><a href="#cite_note-379" id="mwCk8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClE">[</span>372<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClI">]</span></span></a></sup> Fire lance is the earliest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firearm" title="Firearm" id="mwClM">firearm</a> in the world and one of the earliest gunpowder weapons.<sup about="#mwt1090" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Helaine_380-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Helaine"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Helaine-380"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Helaine-380" id="mwClQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClY">[</span>373<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1093" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-381" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-381"}}'><a href="#cite_note-381" id="mwClg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClo">[</span>374<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCls">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwClw"><b id="mwCl0">10th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fireworks" title="Fireworks" id="mwCl4">Fireworks</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_dynasty" title="Song dynasty" id="mwCl8">Song dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCmA">China</a>: Fireworks first appear in China during the Song dynasty (960–1279), in the early age of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunpowder" title="Gunpowder" id="mwCmE">gunpowder</a>. Fireworks could be purchased from market vendors; these were made of sticks of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bamboo" title="Bamboo" id="mwCmI">bamboo</a> packed with gunpowder.<sup about="#mwt1094" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-382" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-382"}}'><a href="#cite_note-382" id="mwCmM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCmQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmU">[</span>375<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCmc"><b id="mwCmg">974:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_pen" title="Fountain pen" id="mwCmk">Fountain pen</a>: invented at the request of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Mu'izz_li-Din_Allah" title="Al-Mu'izz li-Din Allah" id="mwCmo">al-Mu'izz li-Din Allah</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt_in_the_Middle_Ages" title="Egypt in the Middle Ages" id="mwCms">Arab Egypt</a>.<sup about="#mwt1097" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-383" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-383"}}'><a href="#cite_note-383" id="mwCmw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCm0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCm4">[</span>376<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCm8">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="25" id="mwCnA" aria-labelledby="11th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="11th_century">11th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25" title="Edit section: 11th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1098" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCnE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main list","href":"./Template:Main_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"11th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1099" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1098" id="mwCnI">For a more comprehensive list, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/11th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="11th century">11th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a>.</div>
<ul id="mwCnM"><li id="mwCnQ"><b id="mwCnU">11th century:</b> Early versions of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bessemer_process" title="Bessemer process" id="mwCnY">Bessemer process</a> are developed in China.</li>
<li id="mwCnc"><b id="mwCng">11th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Su_Song#The_endless_chain_drive" title="Su Song" id="mwCnk">Endless power-transmitting chain drive</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Su_Song" title="Su Song" id="mwCno">Su Song</a> for the development an astronomical clock (the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Su_Song#Horology_and_mechanical_engineering" title="Su Song" id="mwCns">Cosmic Engine</a>)<sup about="#mwt1100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-needham_volume_4_111_384-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"needham volume 4 111"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-needham_volume_4_111-384"}}'><a href="#cite_note-needham_volume_4_111-384" id="mwCnw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCn0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCn4">[</span>377<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCn8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCoA"><b id="mwCoE">11th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico" title="Calico" id="mwCoI">Calico</a> was developed in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kozhikode" title="Kozhikode" id="mwCoM">Calicut</a>, India.<sup about="#mwt1101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-eb-calico2_385-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"eb-calico2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-eb-calico2-385"}}'><a href="#cite_note-eb-calico2-385" id="mwCoQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCoU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCoY">[</span>378<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCoc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCog"><b id="mwCok">1088:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movable_type" title="Movable type" id="mwCoo">Movable type</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_dynasty" title="Song dynasty" id="mwCos">Song dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCow">China</a>: The first record of a movable type system is in the <i id="mwCo0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream_Pool_Essays" title="Dream Pool Essays" id="mwCo4">Dream Pool Essays</a></i>, which attributes the invention of the movable type to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bi_Sheng" title="Bi Sheng" id="mwCo8">Bi Sheng</a>.<sup about="#mwt1102" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-386" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-386"}}'><a href="#cite_note-386" id="mwCpA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCpE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCpI">[</span>379<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCpM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-gernet_1996_335_387-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"gernet 1996 335"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-gernet_1996_335-387"}}'><a href="#cite_note-gernet_1996_335-387" id="mwCpQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCpU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCpY">[</span>380<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCpc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1104" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-bowman_2000_599_388-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"bowman 2000 599"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-bowman_2000_599-388"}}'><a href="#cite_note-bowman_2000_599-388" id="mwCpg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCpk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCpo">[</span>381<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCps">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1105" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-day_mcneil_70_389-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"day mcneil 70"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-day_mcneil_70-389"}}'><a href="#cite_note-day_mcneil_70-389" id="mwCpw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCp0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCp4">[</span>382<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCp8">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="26" id="mwCqA" aria-labelledby="12th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="12th_century">12th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26" title="Edit section: 12th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1106" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCqE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"12th century#Inventions, discoveries, and introductions by year"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1107" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1106" id="mwCqI">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/12th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_and_introductions_by_year" title="12th century">12th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, and introductions by year</a></div>
<ul id="mwCqM"><li id="mwCqQ">The oldest known representation of a bombard is a 12th-century (circa 1128 AD) high-relief sculpture found in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dazu_Rock_Carvings" title="Dazu Rock Carvings" id="mwCqU">Dazu Rock Carvings</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sichuan" title="Sichuan" id="mwCqY">Sichuan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCqc">China</a>.<sup about="#mwt1110" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-390" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-390"}}'><a href="#cite_note-390" id="mwCqg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCqk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCqo">[</span>383<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCqs">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="27" id="mwCqw" aria-labelledby="13th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="13th_century">13th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27" title="Edit section: 13th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1111" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCq0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"13th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1112" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1111" id="mwCq4">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/13th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="13th century">13th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<ul id="mwCq8"><li id="mwCrA"><b id="mwCrE">13th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket" title="Rocket" id="mwCrI">Rocket</a> for military and recreational uses date back to at least 13th-century China.<sup about="#mwt1115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-391" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-391"}}'><a href="#cite_note-391" id="mwCrM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCrQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrU">[</span>384<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCrc"><b id="mwCrg">13th century:</b> The earliest form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_escapement" title="Mechanical escapement" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCrk">mechanical escapement</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verge_escapement" title="Verge escapement" id="mwCro">verge escapement</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Europe" title="Europe" id="mwCrs">Europe</a>.<sup about="#mwt1118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-392" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-392"}}'><a href="#cite_note-392" id="mwCrw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCr0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCr4">[</span>385<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCr8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCsA"><b id="mwCsE">13th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Button" title="Button" id="mwCsI">Buttons</a> (combined with buttonholes) as a functional fastening for closing clothes appear first in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany" title="Germany" id="mwCsM">Germany</a>.<sup about="#mwt1119" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-393" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-393"}}'><a href="#cite_note-393" id="mwCsQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCsU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsY">[</span>386<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCsg"><b id="mwCsk">13th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomb" title="Bomb" id="mwCso">Explosive bomb</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jin_dynasty_(1115–1234)" title="Jin dynasty (1115–1234)" id="mwCss">Jin dynasty</a> Manchuria: Explosive bombs are used in 1221 by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jin_dynasty_(1115–1234)" title="Jin dynasty (1115–1234)" id="mwCsw">Jin dynasty</a> against a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_dynasty" title="Song dynasty" id="mwCs0">Song dynasty</a> city.<sup about="#mwt1122" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Connolly_394-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Connolly"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Connolly-394"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Connolly-394" id="mwCs4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCs8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtA">[</span>387<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtE">]</span></span></a></sup> The first accounts of bombs made of cast iron shells packed with explosive gunpowder are documented in the 13th century in China and are called "thunder-crash bombs",<sup about="#mwt1123" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-395" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-395"}}'><a href="#cite_note-395" id="mwCtI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCtM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtQ">[</span>388<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtU">]</span></span></a></sup> coined during a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jin_dynasty_(1115–1234)" title="Jin dynasty (1115–1234)" id="mwCtY">Jin dynasty</a> naval battle in 1231.<sup about="#mwt1124" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-needham_volume_5_part_7_171_396-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"needham volume 5 part 7 171"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-needham_volume_5_part_7_171-396"}}'><a href="#cite_note-needham_volume_5_part_7_171-396" id="mwCtc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCtg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtk">[</span>389<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCto">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCts"><b id="mwCtw">13th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hand_cannon" title="Hand cannon" id="mwCt0">Hand cannon</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuan_dynasty" title="Yuan dynasty" id="mwCt4">Yuan dynasty</a> China: The earliest hand cannon dates to the 13th century based on archaeological evidence from a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heilongjiang" title="Heilongjiang" id="mwCt8">Heilongjiang</a> excavation. There is also written evidence in the <i id="mwCuA">Yuanshi</i> (1370) on Li Tang, an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jurchens" title="Jurchens" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCuE">ethnic Jurchen</a> commander under the Yuan dynasty who in 1288 suppresses the rebellion of the Christian prince Nayan with his "gun-soldiers" or <i id="mwCuI">chongzu</i>, this being the earliest known event where this phrase is used.<sup about="#mwt1125" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-397" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-397"}}'><a href="#cite_note-397" id="mwCuM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuU">[</span>390<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCuc"><b id="mwCug">13th century:</b> Earliest documented <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_goggles" title="Snow goggles" id="mwCuk">snow goggles</a>, a type of sunglasses, made of flattened walrus or caribou ivory are used by the Inuit peoples in the arctic regions of North America.<sup about="#mwt1130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-398" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-398"}}'><a href="#cite_note-398" id="mwCuo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCus"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuw">[</span>391<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCu0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1132" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-399" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-399"}}'><a href="#cite_note-399" id="mwCu4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCu8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvA">[</span>392<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvE">]</span></span></a></sup> In China, the first sunglasses consisting of flat panes of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoky_quartz" title="Smoky quartz" id="mwCvI">smoky quartz</a> are documented.<sup about="#mwt1135" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-400" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-400"}}'><a href="#cite_note-400" id="mwCvM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvU">[</span>393<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Vision_401-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Vision"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Vision-401"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Vision-401" id="mwCvc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvk">[</span>394<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCvs"><b id="mwCvw">13th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double-entry_bookkeeping" title="Double-entry bookkeeping" id="mwCv0">Double-entry bookkeeping</a> in Italy.<sup about="#mwt1141" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-402" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-402"}}'><a href="#cite_note-402" id="mwCv4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCv8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwA">[</span>395<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCwI"><b id="mwCwM">13th century - 14th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton_gin" title="Cotton gin" id="mwCwQ">Worm gear cotton gin</a> in India.<sup about="#mwt1144" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-403" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-403"}}'><a href="#cite_note-403" id="mwCwU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwc">[</span>396<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCwk"><b id="mwCwo">1277:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_mine" title="Land mine" id="mwCws">Land mine</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_dynasty" title="Song dynasty" id="mwCww">Song dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCw0">China</a>: Textual evidence suggests that the first use of a land mine in history is by a Song dynasty brigadier general known as Lou Qianxia, who uses an 'enormous bomb' (<i id="mwCw4">huo pao</i>) to kill <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_the_Song_dynasty#Yuan_invasion_and_end_of_the_Song_dynasty" title="History of the Song dynasty" id="mwCw8">Mongol soldiers</a> invading <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guangxi" title="Guangxi" id="mwCxA">Guangxi</a> in 1277.<sup about="#mwt1145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-404" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-404"}}'><a href="#cite_note-404" id="mwCxE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxM">[</span>397<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCxU"><b id="mwCxY">1286:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyeglasses" title="Eyeglasses" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCxc">Eyeglasses</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy" title="Italy" id="mwCxg">Italy</a><sup about="#mwt1146" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-405" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-405"}}'><a href="#cite_note-405" id="mwCxk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxs">[</span>398<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxw">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="28" id="mwCx0" aria-labelledby="14th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="14th_century">14th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=28" title="Edit section: 14th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwCx4"><li id="mwCx8"><b id="mwCyA">Early 14th century – Mid 14th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huolongchushui" title="Huolongchushui" id="mwCyE">Huolongchushui</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multistage_rocket" title="Multistage rocket" id="mwCyI">Multistage rocket</a>, was developed in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ming_dynasty" title="Ming dynasty" id="mwCyM">Ming dynasty</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCyQ">China</a> and described in <i id="mwCyU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huolongjing" title="Huolongjing" id="mwCyY">Huolongjing</a></i> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiao_Yu" title="Jiao Yu" id="mwCyc">Jiao Yu</a>.<sup about="#mwt1149" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-406" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-406"}}'><a href="#cite_note-406" id="mwCyg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCyk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyo">[</span>399<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCys">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCyw"><b id="mwCy0">14th century:</b> Painting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas" title="Canvas" id="mwCy4">Canvas</a> was first used in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy" title="Italy" id="mwCy8">Italy</a>.<sup about="#mwt1150" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-407" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-407"}}'><a href="#cite_note-407" id="mwCzA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzI">[</span>400<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCzQ"><b id="mwCzU">14th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob's_staff" title="Jacob's staff" id="mwCzY">Jacob's staff</a> described by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levi_ben_Gerson" title="Levi ben Gerson" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCzc">Levi ben Gerson</a><sup about="#mwt1153" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-408" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-408"}}'><a href="#cite_note-408" id="mwCzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzo">[</span>401<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwCzw"><b id="mwCz0">14th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naval_mine" title="Naval mine" id="mwCz4">Naval mine</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ming_dynasty" title="Ming dynasty" id="mwCz8">Ming dynasty</a> Mentioned in the <i id="mwC0A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huolongjing" title="Huolongjing" id="mwC0E">Huolongjing</a></i> military manuscript written by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiao_Yu" title="Jiao Yu" id="mwC0I">Jiao Yu</a> (fl. 14th to early 15th century) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liu_Bowen" title="Liu Bowen" id="mwC0M">Liu Bowen</a> (1311–1375), describing naval mines used at sea or on rivers and lakes, made of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrought_iron" title="Wrought iron" id="mwC0Q">wrought iron</a> and enclosed in an ox bladder. A later model is documented in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Song_Yingxing" title="Song Yingxing" id="mwC0U">Song Yingxing</a>'s encyclopedia written in 1637.<sup about="#mwt1154" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-409" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-409"}}'><a href="#cite_note-409" id="mwC0Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0g">[</span>402<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0k">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC0o"><b id="mwC0s">14th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bidriware" title="Bidriware" id="mwC0w">Bidriware</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahmani_Sultanate" title="Bahmani Sultanate" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC00">Bahmani Sultanate</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India" title="India" id="mwC04">India</a>.<sup about="#mwt1157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TOI_410-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TOI"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TOI-410"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TOI-410" id="mwC08"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1E">[</span>403<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1I">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC1M"><b id="mwC1Q">1364:</b> first use of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Handgun" title="Handgun" id="mwC1U">handgun</a><sup about="#mwt1160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:11_411-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":11"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:11-411"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:11-411" id="mwC1Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC1c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1g">[</span>404<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1k">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwC1o"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Handtiegelpresse_von_1811.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwC1s"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Handtiegelpresse_von_1811.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Handtiegelpresse_von_1811.jpg/250px-Handtiegelpresse_von_1811.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Handtiegelpresse_von_1811.jpg/500px-Handtiegelpresse_von_1811.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2304" data-file-height="3456" data-file-type="bitmap" height="285" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwC1w"/></a><figcaption id="mwC10">The 15th-century invention of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Printing_press" title="Printing press" id="mwC14">printing press</a> with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movable_type" title="Movable type" id="mwC18">movable type</a> by the German <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannes_Gutenberg" title="Johannes Gutenberg" id="mwC2A">Johannes Gutenberg</a>.<sup about="#mwt1162" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-412" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-412"}}'><a href="#cite_note-412" id="mwC2E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2M">[</span>405<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2Q">]</span></span></a></sup> </figcaption></figure>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="29" id="mwC2U" aria-labelledby="15th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="15th_century">15th century</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=29" title="Edit section: 15th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1163" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC2Y" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"15th century#Inventions, discoveries, introductions"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1164" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1163" id="mwC2c">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/15th_century#Inventions,_discoveries,_introductions" title="15th century">15th century §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Inventions, discoveries, introductions</a></div>
<ul id="mwC2g"><li id="mwC2k"><b id="mwC2o">Early 15th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coil_spring" title="Coil spring" id="mwC2s">Coil spring</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Europe" title="Europe" id="mwC2w">Europe</a><sup about="#mwt1167" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-White1966_413-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"White1966"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-White1966-413"}}'><a href="#cite_note-White1966-413" id="mwC20"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC24"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC28">[</span>406<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC3E"><b id="mwC3I">15th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mainspring" title="Mainspring" id="mwC3M">Mainspring</a> in Europe<sup about="#mwt1168" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-White1966_413-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"White1966"}}'><a href="#cite_note-White1966-413" id="mwC3Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3Y">[</span>406<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3c">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC3g"><b id="mwC3k">1420s:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brace_(tool)" title="Brace (tool)" id="mwC3o">Brace</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/County_of_Flanders" title="County of Flanders" id="mwC3s">Flanders</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Roman_Empire" title="Holy Roman Empire" id="mwC3w">Holy Roman Empire</a><sup about="#mwt1169" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-White_1968,_462f._414-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"White 1968, 462f."},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-White_1968,_462f.-414"}}'><a href="#cite_note-White_1968,_462f.-414" id="mwC30"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC34"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC38">[</span>407<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC4E"><b id="mwC4I">1439:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Printing_press" title="Printing press" id="mwC4M">Printing press</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mainz,_Germany" title="Mainz, Germany" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC4Q">Mainz, Germany</a>: The printing press is invented in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Roman_Empire" title="Holy Roman Empire" id="mwC4U">Holy Roman Empire</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannes_Gutenberg" title="Johannes Gutenberg" id="mwC4Y">Johannes Gutenberg</a> before 1440, based on existing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Screw_press" title="Screw press" id="mwC4c">screw presses</a>.<sup about="#mwt1170" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwC4g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4o">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4s">]</span></span></a></sup> The first confirmed record of a press appeared in a 1439 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawsuit" title="Lawsuit" id="mwC4w">lawsuit</a> against Gutenberg.<sup about="#mwt1173" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-meggs58-69_416-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"meggs58-69"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-meggs58-69-416"}}'><a href="#cite_note-meggs58-69-416" id="mwC40"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC44"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC48">[</span>409<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC5E"><b id="mwC5I">Mid 15th century:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arquebus" title="Arquebus" id="mwC5M">Arquebus</a> (also spelled Harquebus) is invented, possibly in Spain.<sup about="#mwt1176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-417" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-417"}}'><a href="#cite_note-417" id="mwC5Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC5U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5Y">[</span>410<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5c">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1179" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-418" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-418"}}'><a href="#cite_note-418" id="mwC5g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC5k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5o">[</span>411<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC5w"><b id="mwC50">1453:</b> First large scale use of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liquation" title="Liquation" id="mwC54">Liquation</a> for separating <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver" title="Silver" id="mwC58">silver</a> from silver-bearing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper" title="Copper" id="mwC6A">copper</a> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuremberg" title="Nuremberg" id="mwC6E">Nuremberg</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Roman_Empire" title="Holy Roman Empire" id="mwC6I">Holy Roman Empire</a>.<sup about="#mwt1182" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-419" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-419"}}'><a href="#cite_note-419" id="mwC6M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC6Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6U">[</span>412<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC6c"><b id="mwC6g">1480s:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariner's_astrolabe" title="Mariner's astrolabe" id="mwC6k">Mariner's astrolabe</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese_discoveries" title="Portuguese discoveries" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC6o">Portuguese circumnavigation of Africa</a><sup about="#mwt1183" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-420" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-420"}}'><a href="#cite_note-420" id="mwC6s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC60">[</span>413<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC64">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="30" id="mwC68" aria-labelledby="Early_modern_era"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Early_modern_era">Early modern era</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=30" title="Edit section: Early modern era"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="31" id="mwC7A" aria-labelledby="16th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="16th_century">16th century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=31" title="Edit section: 16th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwC7E"><li id="mwC7I"><b id="mwC7M">16th century:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chintz" title="Chintz" id="mwC7Q">Chintz</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodblock_printing" title="Woodblock printing" id="mwC7U">printed</a> clothing in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qutb_Shahi_dynasty" title="Qutb Shahi dynasty" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC7Y">Golconda</a>, India<sup about="#mwt1186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Allen_G._Noble_421-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Allen G. Noble"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Allen_G._Noble-421"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Allen_G._Noble-421" id="mwC7c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7k">[</span>414<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7o">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC7s"><b id="mwC7w">16th century:</b>  <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hookah" title="Hookah" id="mwC70">Hookah</a> by Irfan Shaikh, at the court of the Mughal emperor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akbar" title="Akbar" id="mwC74">Akbar</a> I<sup about="#mwt1189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-iranica_422-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"iranica"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-iranica-422"}}'><a href="#cite_note-iranica-422" id="mwC78"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8E">[</span>415<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8I">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1192" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Sivaramakrishnan4-5_423-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Sivaramakrishnan4-5"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Sivaramakrishnan4-5-423"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Sivaramakrishnan4-5-423" id="mwC8M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8U">[</span>416<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC8c"><b id="mwC8g">1540:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rifling" title="Rifling" id="mwC8k">Rifling</a> is first used in firearms, after being invented in 1498<sup about="#mwt1193" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:11_411-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:11-411" id="mwC8o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8w">[</span>404<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC80">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC84"><b id="mwC88">1560:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dry_dock#Floating" title="Dry dock" id="mwC9A">Floating dry dock</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venice" title="Venice" id="mwC9E">Venice</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venetian_Republic" title="Venetian Republic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC9I">Venetian Republic</a><sup about="#mwt1194" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-424" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-424"}}'><a href="#cite_note-424" id="mwC9M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC9Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9U">[</span>417<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC9c"><b id="mwC9g">1569:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercator_Projection" title="Mercator Projection" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC9k">Mercator Projection</a> map created by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerardus_Mercator" title="Gerardus Mercator" id="mwC9o">Gerardus Mercator</a></li>
<li id="mwC9s"><b id="mwC9w">1589:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stocking_frame" title="Stocking frame" id="mwC90">Stocking frame</a>: Invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Lee_(inventor)" title="William Lee (inventor)" id="mwC94">William Lee</a>.<sup about="#mwt1197" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-425" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-425"}}'><a href="#cite_note-425" id="mwC98"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-E">[</span>418<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-I">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwC-M"><b id="mwC-Q">1594:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backstaff" title="Backstaff" id="mwC-U">Backstaff</a>: Invented by Captain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Davis_(English_explorer)" title="John Davis (English explorer)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC-Y">John Davis</a><sup about="#mwt1200" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-426" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-426"}}'><a href="#cite_note-426" id="mwC-c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-k">[</span>419<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1203" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-427" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-427"}}'><a href="#cite_note-427" id="mwC-s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-0">[</span>420<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-4">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="32" id="mwC-8" aria-labelledby="17th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="17th_century">17th century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=32" title="Edit section: 17th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwC_A"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Relation_Aller_Fuernemmen_und_gedenckwuerdigen_Historien_(1609).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwC_E"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Relation_Aller_Fuernemmen_und_gedenckwuerdigen_Historien_(1609).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Relation_Aller_Fuernemmen_und_gedenckwuerdigen_Historien_%281609%29.jpg/250px-Relation_Aller_Fuernemmen_und_gedenckwuerdigen_Historien_%281609%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Relation_Aller_Fuernemmen_und_gedenckwuerdigen_Historien_%281609%29.jpg/500px-Relation_Aller_Fuernemmen_und_gedenckwuerdigen_Historien_%281609%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1024" data-file-height="1235" data-file-type="bitmap" height="229" width="190" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75" id="mwC_I"/></a><figcaption id="mwC_M">A 1609 title page of the <i id="mwC_Q"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relation_aller_Fürnemmen_und_gedenckwürdigen_Historien" title="Relation aller Fürnemmen und gedenckwürdigen Historien" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC_U">Relation</a></i>, the world's first newspaper (first published in 1605)<sup about="#mwt1204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-World_Association_of_Newspapers_428-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"World Association of Newspapers"}}'><a href="#cite_note-World_Association_of_Newspapers-428" id="mwC_Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC_c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_g">[</span>421<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_k">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1205" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Weber_2006,_396f._429-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Weber 2006, 396f."}}'><a href="#cite_note-Weber_2006,_396f.-429" id="mwC_o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC_s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_w">[</span>422<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_0">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwC_4"><li id="mwC_8"><b id="mwDAA">1605:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newspaper" title="Newspaper" id="mwDAE">Newspaper</a> (<i id="mwDAI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relation_aller_Fürnemmen_und_gedenckwürdigen_Historien" title="Relation aller Fürnemmen und gedenckwürdigen Historien" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDAM">Relation</a></i>): <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Carolus" title="Johann Carolus" id="mwDAQ">Johann Carolus</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strassburg" title="Strassburg" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDAU">Strassburg</a> (see also <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_the_oldest_newspapers" title="List of the oldest newspapers" id="mwDAY">List of the oldest newspapers</a>)<sup about="#mwt1207" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-World_Association_of_Newspapers_428-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"World Association of Newspapers"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-World_Association_of_Newspapers-428"}}'><a href="#cite_note-World_Association_of_Newspapers-428" id="mwDAc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAk">[</span>421<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1208" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Weber_2006,_396f._429-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Weber 2006, 396f."},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Weber_2006,_396f.-429"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Weber_2006,_396f.-429" id="mwDAs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA0">[</span>422<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDA8"><b id="mwDBA">1608:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telescope" title="Telescope" id="mwDBE">Telescope</a>: Patent applied for by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Lippershey" title="Hans Lippershey" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDBI">Hans Lippershey</a>. Actual inventor unknown since it seemed to already be a common item being offered by the spectacle makers in the Netherlands with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Metius" title="Jacob Metius" id="mwDBM">Jacob Metius</a> also applying for patent and the son of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zacharias_Janssen" title="Zacharias Janssen" id="mwDBQ">Zacharias Janssen</a> making a claim 47 years later that his father invented it.</li>
<li id="mwDBU"><b id="mwDBY">1620:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optical_microscope#Compound_microscope" title="Optical microscope" id="mwDBc">Compound microscopes</a>, which combine an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Objective_(optics)" title="Objective (optics)" id="mwDBg">objective lens</a> with an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyepiece" title="Eyepiece" id="mwDBk">eyepiece</a> to view a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Real_image" title="Real image" id="mwDBo">real image</a>, first appear in Europe. Apparently derived from the telescope, actual inventor unknown, variously attributed to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zacharias_Janssen" title="Zacharias Janssen" id="mwDBs">Zacharias Janssen</a> (his son claiming it was invented in 1590), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornelis_Drebbel" title="Cornelis Drebbel" id="mwDBw">Cornelis Drebbel</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galileo_Galilei" title="Galileo Galilei" id="mwDB0">Galileo Galilei</a>.<sup about="#mwt1209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-430" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-430"}}'><a href="#cite_note-430" id="mwDB4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDB8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCA">[</span>423<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDCI"><b id="mwDCM">1630:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slide_rule" title="Slide rule" id="mwDCQ">Slide rule</a>: invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Oughtred" title="William Oughtred" id="mwDCU">William Oughtred</a><sup about="#mwt1210" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-431" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-431"}}'><a href="#cite_note-431" id="mwDCY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDCc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCg">[</span>424<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1213" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-432" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-432"}}'><a href="#cite_note-432" id="mwDCo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDCs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCw">[</span>425<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDC0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDC4"><b id="mwDC8">1630:</b> first use of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flintlock" title="Flintlock" id="mwDDA">flintlock</a><sup about="#mwt1214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:11_411-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:11-411" id="mwDDE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDDI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDM">[</span>404<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDDU"><b id="mwDDY">1642:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_calculator" title="Mechanical calculator" id="mwDDc">Mechanical calculator</a>. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pascaline" title="Pascaline" id="mwDDg">Pascaline</a> is built by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blaise_Pascal" title="Blaise Pascal" id="mwDDk">Blaise Pascal</a>.<sup about="#mwt1217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-433" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-433"}}'><a href="#cite_note-433" id="mwDDo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDDs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDw">[</span>426<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDD0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDD4"><b id="mwDD8">1643:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barometer" title="Barometer" id="mwDEA">Barometer</a>: invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evangelista_Torricelli" title="Evangelista Torricelli" id="mwDEE">Evangelista Torricelli</a>, or possibly up to three years earlier by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gasparo_Berti" title="Gasparo Berti" id="mwDEI">Gasparo Berti</a>.<sup about="#mwt1220" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-http://www.islandnet.com/~see/weather/history/barometerhistory1.htm_434-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"http://www.islandnet.com/~see/weather/history/barometerhistory1.htm"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-http://www.islandnet.com/~see/weather/history/barometerhistory1.htm-434"}}'><a href="#cite_note-http://www.islandnet.com/~see/weather/history/barometerhistory1.htm-434" id="mwDEM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEU">[</span>427<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDEc"><b id="mwDEg">1650:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacuum_pump" title="Vacuum pump" id="mwDEk">Vacuum pump</a>: Invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_von_Guericke" title="Otto von Guericke" id="mwDEo">Otto von Guericke</a>.<sup about="#mwt1223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-435" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-435"}}'><a href="#cite_note-435" id="mwDEs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDE0">[</span>428<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDE4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDE8"><b id="mwDFA">1656:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pendulum_clock" title="Pendulum clock" id="mwDFE">Pendulum clock</a>: Invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christiaan_Huygens" title="Christiaan Huygens" id="mwDFI">Christiaan Huygens</a>. It was first conceptualized in 1637 by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galileo_Galilei" title="Galileo Galilei" id="mwDFM">Galileo Galilei</a> but he was unable to create a working model.<sup about="#mwt1226" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-436" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-436"}}'><a href="#cite_note-436" id="mwDFQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDFU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFY">[</span>429<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDFg"><b id="mwDFk">1668:</b> First functional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reflecting_telescope" title="Reflecting telescope" id="mwDFo">reflecting telescope</a> constructed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Newton" title="Isaac Newton" id="mwDFs">Isaac Newton</a>.<sup about="#mwt1229" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-437" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-437"}}'><a href="#cite_note-437" id="mwDFw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDF0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDF4">[</span>430<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDF8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDGA"><b id="mwDGE">1679:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pressure-cooker" title="Pressure-cooker" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDGI">Pressure-cooker</a>: Invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denis_Papin" title="Denis Papin" id="mwDGM">Denis Papin</a>.<sup about="#mwt1232" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-438" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-438"}}'><a href="#cite_note-438" id="mwDGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGY">[</span>431<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDGg"><b id="mwDGk">1680:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christiaan_Huygens" title="Christiaan Huygens" id="mwDGo">Christiaan Huygens</a> provides the first known description of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunpowder_engine" title="Gunpowder engine" id="mwDGs">piston engine</a>.<sup about="#mwt1233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-439" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-439"}}'><a href="#cite_note-439" id="mwDGw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDG0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDG4">[</span>432<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDG8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDHA"><b id="mwDHE">1698:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Savery" title="Thomas Savery" id="mwDHI">Thomas Savery</a> develops a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Savery#Steam-powered_pump" title="Thomas Savery" id="mwDHM">steam-powered water pump</a>: for draining mines<sup about="#mwt1236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-440" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-440"}}'><a href="#cite_note-440" id="mwDHQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDHU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHY">[</span>433<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHc">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="33" id="mwDHg" aria-labelledby="18th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="18th_century">18th century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=33" title="Edit section: 18th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwDHk"><li id="mwDHo"><b id="mwDHs">1709:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bartolomeo_Cristofori" title="Bartolomeo Cristofori" id="mwDHw">Bartolomeo Cristofori</a> crafts the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piano" title="Piano" id="mwDH0">piano</a>, which became a leading instrument of Western art music<sup about="#mwt1239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-441" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-441"}}'><a href="#cite_note-441" id="mwDH4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDH8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIA">[</span>434<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDII"><b id="mwDIM">1712:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Newcomen" title="Thomas Newcomen" id="mwDIQ">Thomas Newcomen</a> builds the first commercial steam engine to pump water out of mines.<sup about="#mwt1242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-McNeil1990_442-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"McNeil1990"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-McNeil1990-442"}}'><a href="#cite_note-McNeil1990-442" id="mwDIU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIc">[</span>435<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDIk"><b id="mwDIo">1738:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewis_Paul" title="Lewis Paul" id="mwDIs">Lewis Paul</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Wyatt_(inventor)" title="John Wyatt (inventor)" id="mwDIw">John Wyatt</a> invent the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul-Wyatt_cotton_mills" title="Paul-Wyatt cotton mills" id="mwDI0">mechanized cotton spinning machine</a>, helping to establish the British textile industry<sup about="#mwt1245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-443" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-443"}}'><a href="#cite_note-443" id="mwDI4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDI8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJA">[</span>436<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDJI"><b id="mwDJM">1745:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pieter_van_Musschenbroek" title="Pieter van Musschenbroek" id="mwDJQ">Musschenbroek</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ewald_Georg_von_Kleist" title="Ewald Georg von Kleist" id="mwDJU">Kleist</a> independently develop the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leyden_jar" title="Leyden jar" id="mwDJY">Leyden jar</a>, an early form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capacitor" title="Capacitor" id="mwDJc">capacitor</a>.<sup about="#mwt1246" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwDJg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJo">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDJw"><b id="mwDJ0">1746:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Roebuck" title="John Roebuck" id="mwDJ4">John Roebuck</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lead_chamber_process" title="Lead chamber process" id="mwDJ8">lead chamber process</a>, mass producing sulfuric acid for manufacturing<sup about="#mwt1249" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-444" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-444"}}'><a href="#cite_note-444" id="mwDKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKI">[</span>437<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDKQ"><b id="mwDKU">1755:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Cullen" title="William Cullen" id="mwDKY">William Cullen</a> invents the first artificial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Refrigeration" title="Refrigeration" id="mwDKc">refrigeration</a> machine<sup about="#mwt1252" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-445" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-445"}}'><a href="#cite_note-445" id="mwDKg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKo">[</span>438<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDKw"><b id="mwDK0">1764:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Hargreaves" title="James Hargreaves" id="mwDK4">James Hargreaves</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinning_jenny" title="Spinning jenny" id="mwDK8">spinning jenny</a>, revolutionizing textile production during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Industrial_Revolution" title="Industrial Revolution" id="mwDLA">Industrial Revolution</a><sup about="#mwt1255" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-446" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-446"}}'><a href="#cite_note-446" id="mwDLE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLM">[</span>439<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDLU"><b id="mwDLY">1769:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas-Joseph_Cugnot" title="Nicolas-Joseph Cugnot" id="mwDLc">Nicolas-Joseph Cugnot</a> invents the first steam-powered vehicle capable of carrying passengers, an early <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Car" title="Car" id="mwDLg">car</a><sup about="#mwt1258" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-447" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-447"}}'><a href="#cite_note-447" id="mwDLk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLs">[</span>440<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1261" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-448" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-448"}}'><a href="#cite_note-448" id="mwDL0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDL4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDL8">[</span>441<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDME"><b id="mwDMI">1774:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Wilkinson_(industrialist)" title="John Wilkinson (industrialist)" id="mwDMM">John Wilkinson</a> invents his <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boring_(manufacturing)" title="Boring (manufacturing)" id="mwDMQ">boring</a> machine, considered by some to be the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_tool" title="Machine tool" id="mwDMU">machine tool</a><sup about="#mwt1264" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-449" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-449"}}'><a href="#cite_note-449" id="mwDMY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDMc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMg">[</span>442<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDMo"><b id="mwDMs">1775:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jesse_Ramsden" title="Jesse Ramsden" id="mwDMw">Jesse Ramsden</a> invents the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Screw-cutting_lathe" title="Screw-cutting lathe" id="mwDM0">screw-cutting lathe</a><sup about="#mwt1267" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-450" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-450"}}'><a href="#cite_note-450" id="mwDM4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDM8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNA">[</span>443<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1270" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-451" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-451"}}'><a href="#cite_note-451" id="mwDNI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNQ">[</span>444<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDNY"><b id="mwDNc">1776:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Wilkinson_(industrialist)" title="John Wilkinson (industrialist)" id="mwDNg">John Wilkinson</a> invents a mechanical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_compressor" title="Air compressor" id="mwDNk">air compressor</a> that would become the prototype for all later mechanical compressors<sup about="#mwt1273" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-452" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-452"}}'><a href="#cite_note-452" id="mwDNo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNw">[</span>445<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDN0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1276" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-453" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-453"}}'><a href="#cite_note-453" id="mwDN4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDN8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOA">[</span>446<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDOI"><b id="mwDOM">1780:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyder_Ali" title="Hyder Ali" id="mwDOQ">Hyder Ali</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Mysore" title="Kingdom of Mysore" id="mwDOU">Mysore</a>, India develops the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mysorean_rockets" title="Mysorean rockets" id="mwDOY">metal-cylinder rockets</a>.<sup about="#mwt1279" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Roddam_454-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Roddam"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Roddam-454"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Roddam-454" id="mwDOc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDOg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOk">[</span>447<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDOs"><b id="mwDOw">1783:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_de_Jouffroy" title="Claude de Jouffroy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDO0">Claude de Jouffroy</a> builds the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steamboat" title="Steamboat" id="mwDO4">steamboat</a><sup about="#mwt1282" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-455" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-455"}}'><a href="#cite_note-455" id="mwDO8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPE">[</span>448<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1285" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-456" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-456"}}'><a href="#cite_note-456" id="mwDPM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPU">[</span>449<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDPc"><b id="mwDPg">1783:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgolfier_brothers" title="Montgolfier brothers" id="mwDPk">Joseph-Ralf</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgolfier_brothers" title="Montgolfier brothers" id="mwDPo">Jacques-Étienne Montgolfier</a> build the first manned <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_air_balloon" title="Hot air balloon" id="mwDPs">hot air balloon</a><sup about="#mwt1288" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-457" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-457"}}'><a href="#cite_note-457" id="mwDPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDP4">[</span>450<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDP8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1291" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-458" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-458"}}'><a href="#cite_note-458" id="mwDQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQI">[</span>451<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDQQ"><b id="mwDQU">1783:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis-Sébastien_Lenormand" title="Louis-Sébastien Lenormand" id="mwDQY">Louis-Sébastien Lenormand</a> invents and uses the first modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parachute" title="Parachute" id="mwDQc">parachute</a><sup about="#mwt1294" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-459" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-459"}}'><a href="#cite_note-459" id="mwDQg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQo">[</span>452<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDQw"><b id="mwDQ0">1785:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martinus_van_Marum" title="Martinus van Marum" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDQ4">Martinus van Marum</a> is the first to use the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrolysis" title="Electrolysis" id="mwDQ8">electrolysis</a> technique<sup about="#mwt1297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-460" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-460"}}'><a href="#cite_note-460" id="mwDRA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRI">[</span>453<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDRQ"><b id="mwDRU">1786:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Meikle" title="Andrew Meikle" id="mwDRY">Andrew Meikle</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Threshing_machine" title="Threshing machine" id="mwDRc">threshing machine</a><sup about="#mwt1300" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-461" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-461"}}'><a href="#cite_note-461" id="mwDRg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRo">[</span>454<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1301" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-462" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-462"}}'><a href="#cite_note-462" id="mwDRw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDR0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDR4">[</span>455<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDR8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDSA"><b id="mwDSE">1789:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Cartwright" title="Edmund Cartwright" id="mwDSI">Edmund Cartwright</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_loom" title="Power loom" id="mwDSM">power loom</a><sup about="#mwt1304" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-463" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-463"}}'><a href="#cite_note-463" id="mwDSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDSU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSY">[</span>456<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDSg"><b id="mwDSk">1792:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Chappe" title="Claude Chappe" id="mwDSo">Claude Chappe</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chappe_telegraph" title="Chappe telegraph" id="mwDSs">semaphore telegraph</a><sup about="#mwt1307" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-464" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-464"}}'><a href="#cite_note-464" id="mwDSw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDS0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDS4">[</span>457<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDS8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1310" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-465" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-465"}}'><a href="#cite_note-465" id="mwDTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTI">[</span>458<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDTQ"><b id="mwDTU">1793:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eli_Whitney" title="Eli Whitney" id="mwDTY">Eli Whitney</a> invents the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton_gin" title="Cotton gin" id="mwDTc">cotton gin</a><sup about="#mwt1313" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-466" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-466"}}'><a href="#cite_note-466" id="mwDTg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTo">[</span>459<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDTw"><b id="mwDT0">1795:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Bramah" title="Joseph Bramah" id="mwDT4">Joseph Bramah</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydraulic_press" title="Hydraulic press" id="mwDT8">hydraulic press</a><sup about="#mwt1316" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-467" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-467"}}'><a href="#cite_note-467" id="mwDUA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUI">[</span>460<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1319" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-468" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-468"}}'><a href="#cite_note-468" id="mwDUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUY">[</span>461<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDUg"><b id="mwDUk">1796:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alois_Senefelder" title="Alois Senefelder" id="mwDUo">Alois Senefelder</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithography" title="Lithography" id="mwDUs">lithography</a> printing technique.<sup about="#mwt1322" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-meggspage146_469-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"meggspage146"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-meggspage146-469"}}'><a href="#cite_note-meggspage146-469" id="mwDUw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDU0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDU4">[</span>462<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDU8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDVA"><b id="mwDVE">1796</b>: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Jenner" title="Edward Jenner" id="mwDVI">Edward Jenner</a> invented the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaccine" title="Vaccine" id="mwDVM">vaccine</a> and inoculates an individual for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smallpox" title="Smallpox" id="mwDVQ">smallpox</a><sup about="#mwt1325" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:6-415"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwDVU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVc">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1328" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-470" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-470"}}'><a href="#cite_note-470" id="mwDVk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVs">[</span>463<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDV0"><b id="mwDV4">1799:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_machine" title="Paper machine" id="mwDV8">paper machine</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis-Nicolas_Robert" title="Louis-Nicolas Robert" id="mwDWA">Louis-Nicolas Robert</a><sup about="#mwt1331" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-471" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-471"}}'><a href="#cite_note-471" id="mwDWE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWM">[</span>464<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="34" id="mwDWU" aria-labelledby="Late_modern_period"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Late_modern_period">Late modern period</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=34" title="Edit section: Late modern period"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="35" id="mwDWY" aria-labelledby="19th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="19th_century">19th century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=35" title="Edit section: 19th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="36" id="mwDWc" aria-labelledby="1800s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1800s">1800s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=36" title="Edit section: 1800s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwDWg"><li id="mwDWk"><b id="mwDWo">1800:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alessandro_Volta" title="Alessandro Volta" id="mwDWs">Alessandro Volta</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voltaic_pile" title="Voltaic pile" id="mwDWw">voltaic pile</a>, an early form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battery_(electricity)" title="Battery (electricity)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDW0">battery</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy" title="Italy" id="mwDW4">Italy</a>, based on previous works by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luigi_Galvani" title="Luigi Galvani" id="mwDW8">Luigi Galvani</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDXA"><b id="mwDXE">1802:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humphry_Davy" title="Humphry Davy" id="mwDXI">Humphry Davy</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arc_lamp" title="Arc lamp" id="mwDXM">arc lamp</a> (exact date unclear; not practical as a light source until the invention of efficient electric generators).<sup about="#mwt1334" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-472" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-472"}}'><a href="#cite_note-472" id="mwDXQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXY">[</span>465<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDXg"><b id="mwDXk">1804:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Sertürner" title="Friedrich Sertürner" id="mwDXo">Friedrich Sertürner</a> discovers <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morphine" title="Morphine" id="mwDXs">morphine</a> as the first active alkaloid extracted from the opium poppy plant.<sup about="#mwt1337" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-473" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-473"}}'><a href="#cite_note-473" id="mwDXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDX0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDX4">[</span>466<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDX8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDYA"><b id="mwDYE">1804:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Marie_Jacquard" title="Joseph Marie Jacquard" id="mwDYI">Joseph Marie Jacquard</a> develops his automated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacquard_loom" title="Jacquard loom" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDYM">Jacquard loom</a>.<sup about="#mwt1340" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-474" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-474"}}'><a href="#cite_note-474" id="mwDYQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDYU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYY">[</span>467<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDYg"><b id="mwDYk">1804:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Trevithick" title="Richard Trevithick" id="mwDYo">Richard Trevithick</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_locomotive" title="Steam locomotive" id="mwDYs">steam locomotive</a>.<sup about="#mwt1343" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-475" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-475"}}'><a href="#cite_note-475" id="mwDYw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDY0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDY4">[</span>468<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDY8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDZA"><b id="mwDZE">1804:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanaoka_Seishū" title="Hanaoka Seishū" id="mwDZI">Hanaoka Seishū</a> creates tsūsensan, the first modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_anesthetic" title="General anesthetic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDZM">general anesthetic</a>.<sup about="#mwt1346" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-476" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-476"}}'><a href="#cite_note-476" id="mwDZQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZY">[</span>469<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDZg"><b id="mwDZk">1807:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicéphore_Niépce" title="Nicéphore Niépce" id="mwDZo">Nicéphore Niépce</a> invents  an early <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internal_combustion_engine" title="Internal combustion engine" id="mwDZs">internal combustion engine</a> capable of doing useful work.</li>
<li id="mwDZw"><b id="mwDZ0">1807:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/François_Isaac_de_Rivaz" title="François Isaac de Rivaz" id="mwDZ4">François Isaac de Rivaz</a> designs the first automobile powered by an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internal_combustion_engine" title="Internal combustion engine" id="mwDZ8">internal combustion engine</a> fuelled by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydrogen" title="Hydrogen" id="mwDaA">hydrogen</a>.<sup about="#mwt1347" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwDaE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDaI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaM">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDaU"><b id="mwDaY">1807:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Fulton" title="Robert Fulton" id="mwDac">Robert Fulton</a> expands water transportation and trade with the workable steamboat.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="37" id="mwDag" aria-labelledby="1810s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1810s">1810s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=37" title="Edit section: 1810s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDak"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:KarlVonDrais.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDao"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:KarlVonDrais.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/KarlVonDrais.jpg/250px-KarlVonDrais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/KarlVonDrais.jpg/500px-KarlVonDrais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3440" data-file-height="2781" data-file-type="bitmap" height="202" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDas"/></a><figcaption id="mwDaw">Karl von Drais on his original Laufmaschine, the earliest two-wheeler, or hobbyhorse, in 1819</figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwDa0"><li id="mwDa4"><b id="mwDa8">1810:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Appert" title="Nicolas Appert" id="mwDbA">Nicolas Appert</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canning" title="Canning" id="mwDbE">canning</a> process for food.<sup about="#mwt1348" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-477" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-477"}}'><a href="#cite_note-477" id="mwDbI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbQ">[</span>470<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDbY"><b id="mwDbc">1810:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abraham-Louis_Breguet" title="Abraham-Louis Breguet" id="mwDbg">Abraham-Louis Breguet</a> creates the first wristwatch.<sup about="#mwt1351" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-478" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-478"}}'><a href="#cite_note-478" id="mwDbk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbs">[</span>471<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDb0"><b id="mwDb4">1811:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Koenig" title="Friedrich Koenig" id="mwDb8">Friedrich Koenig</a> invents the first powered <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Printing_press" title="Printing press" id="mwDcA">printing press</a>, which was also the first to use a cylinder.</li>
<li id="mwDcE"><b id="mwDcI">1812:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Reid_Clanny" title="William Reid Clanny" id="mwDcM">William Reid Clanny</a> pioneered the invention of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safety_lamp" title="Safety lamp" id="mwDcQ">safety lamp</a> which he improved in later years. Safety lamps based on Clanny's improved design were used until the adoption of electric lamps.</li>
<li id="mwDcU"><b id="mwDcY">1814:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Fox_(engineer)" title="James Fox (engineer)" id="mwDcc">James Fox</a> invents the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planer_(metalworking)" title="Planer (metalworking)" id="mwDcg">planing machine</a>, though <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Murray" title="Matthew Murray" id="mwDck">Matthew Murray</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leeds" title="Leeds" id="mwDco">Leeds</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Roberts_(engineer)" title="Richard Roberts (engineer)" id="mwDcs">Richard Roberts</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchester" title="Manchester" id="mwDcw">Manchester</a> have also been credited at times with its invention.</li>
<li id="mwDc0"><b id="mwDc4">1816:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/René_Laennec" title="René Laennec" id="mwDc8">René Laennec</a>  invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stethoscope" title="Stethoscope" id="mwDdA">Stethoscope</a>.<sup about="#mwt1354" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-479" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-479"}}'><a href="#cite_note-479" id="mwDdE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdM">[</span>472<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDdU"><b id="mwDdY">1816:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Ronalds" title="Francis Ronalds" id="mwDdc">Francis Ronalds</a> builds the first working <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_telegraph" title="Electric telegraph" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDdg">electric telegraph</a> using <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrostatic" title="Electrostatic" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDdk">electrostatic</a> means.</li>
<li id="mwDdo"><b id="mwDds">1816:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Stirling" title="Robert Stirling" id="mwDdw">Robert Stirling</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stirling_engine" title="Stirling engine" id="mwDd0">Stirling engine</a>.<sup about="#mwt1355" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-480" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-480"}}'><a href="#cite_note-480" id="mwDd4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDd8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeA">[</span>473<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDeI"><b id="mwDeM">1817:</b> Baron <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_von_Drais" title="Karl von Drais" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDeQ">Karl von Drais</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dandy_horse" title="Dandy horse" id="mwDeU">dandy horse</a>, an early <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velocipede" title="Velocipede" id="mwDeY">velocipede</a> and precursor to the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bicycle" title="Bicycle" id="mwDec">bicycle</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDeg"><b id="mwDek">1818:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marc_Isambard_Brunel" title="Marc Isambard Brunel" id="mwDeo">Marc Isambard Brunel</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunnelling_shield" title="Tunnelling shield" id="mwDes">tunnelling shield</a>.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="38" id="mwDew" aria-labelledby="1820s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1820s">1820s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=38" title="Edit section: 1820s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwDe0"><li id="mwDe4"><b id="mwDe8">1822:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Blanchard_(inventor)" title="Thomas Blanchard (inventor)" id="mwDfA">Thomas Blanchard</a> invents the pattern-tracing lathe (actually more like a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaper" title="Shaper" id="mwDfE">shaper</a>). The lathe can copy symmetrical shapes and is used for making gun stocks, and later, ax handles.<sup about="#mwt1358" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Thomson_2009_481-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Thomson 2009"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Thomson_2009-481"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Thomson_2009-481" id="mwDfI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfQ">[</span>474<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1360" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hounshell1984p35_482-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hounshell1984p35"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hounshell1984p35-482"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hounshell1984p35-482" id="mwDfY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfg">[</span>475<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDfo"><b id="mwDfs">1822:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicéphore_Niépce" title="Nicéphore Niépce" id="mwDfw">Nicéphore Niépce</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliography" title="Heliography" id="mwDf0">Heliography</a>, the first photographic process.</li>
<li id="mwDf4"><b id="mwDf8">1822:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Babbage" title="Charles Babbage" id="mwDgA">Charles Babbage</a>, considered the "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_pioneer" title="Computer pioneer" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDgE">father of the computer</a>",<sup about="#mwt1363" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-483" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-483"}}'><a href="#cite_note-483" id="mwDgI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgQ">[</span>476<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgU">]</span></span></a></sup> begins building the first programmable <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_computer" title="Mechanical computer" id="mwDgY">mechanical computer</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDgc"><b id="mwDgg">1823:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Wolfgang_Döbereiner" title="Johann Wolfgang Döbereiner" id="mwDgk">Johann Wolfgang Döbereiner</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Döbereiner's_lamp" title="Döbereiner's lamp" id="mwDgo">first lighter</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDgs"><b id="mwDgw">1824:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Nikolaus_von_Dreyse" title="Johann Nikolaus von Dreyse" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDg0">Johann Nikolaus von Dreyse</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolt_action" title="Bolt action" id="mwDg4">bolt-action rifle</a>.<sup about="#mwt1366" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-484" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-484"}}'><a href="#cite_note-484" id="mwDg8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhE">[</span>477<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDhM"><b id="mwDhQ">1824:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Sturgeon" title="William Sturgeon" id="mwDhU">William Sturgeon</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electromagnet" title="Electromagnet" id="mwDhY">electromagnet</a>.<sup about="#mwt1371" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-485" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-485"}}'><a href="#cite_note-485" id="mwDhc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhk">[</span>478<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDho">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1375" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-486" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-486"}}'><a href="#cite_note-486" id="mwDhs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDh0">[</span>479<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDh4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDh8"><b id="mwDiA">1826:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Walker_(inventor)" title="John Walker (inventor)" id="mwDiE">John Walker</a> invents the friction <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Match" title="Match" id="mwDiI">match</a>.<sup about="#mwt1378" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBCwalker_487-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBCwalker"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBCwalker-487"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBCwalker-487" id="mwDiM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiU">[</span>480<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDic"><b id="mwDig">1826:</b> James Sharp invents and goes on to manufacture the first practical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gas_stove" title="Gas stove" id="mwDik">gas stove</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDio"><b id="mwDis">1828:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Beaumont_Neilson" title="James Beaumont Neilson" id="mwDiw">James Beaumont Neilson</a> develops the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_blast" title="Hot blast" id="mwDi0">hot blast</a> process.</li>
<li id="mwDi4"><b id="mwDi8">1828:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Bell" title="Patrick Bell" id="mwDjA">Patrick Bell</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reaping_machine" title="Reaping machine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDjE">reaping machine</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDjI"><b id="mwDjM">1828:</b> Hungarian physicist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ányos_Jedlik" title="Ányos Jedlik" id="mwDjQ">Ányos Jedlik</a> invents the first commutated rotary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_electric_motor" title="Timeline of the electric motor" id="mwDjU">electromechanical machine</a> with electromagnets.</li>
<li id="mwDjY"><b id="mwDjc">1829:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Braille" title="Louis Braille" id="mwDjg">Louis Braille</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Braille" title="Braille" id="mwDjk">Braille</a> reading system for the blind.<sup about="#mwt1381" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-488" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-488"}}'><a href="#cite_note-488" id="mwDjo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjw">[</span>481<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDj0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDj4"><b id="mwDj8">1829:</b> William Mann invents the compound <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_compressor" title="Air compressor" id="mwDkA">air compressor</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDkE"><b id="mwDkI">1829:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Robinson_Palmer" title="Henry Robinson Palmer" id="mwDkM">Henry Robinson Palmer</a> is awarded a patent for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corrugated_galvanised_iron" title="Corrugated galvanised iron" id="mwDkQ">corrugated galvanised iron</a>.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="39" id="mwDkU" aria-labelledby="1830s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1830s">1830s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=39" title="Edit section: 1830s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwDkY"><li id="mwDkc"><b id="mwDkg">1830:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwin_Budding" title="Edwin Budding" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDkk">Edwin Budding</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawn_mower" title="Lawn mower" id="mwDko">lawn mower</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDks"><b id="mwDkw">1831:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Faraday" title="Michael Faraday" id="mwDk0">Michael Faraday</a> invents a method of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electromagnetic_induction" title="Electromagnetic induction" id="mwDk4">electromagnetic induction</a>. It would be independently invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Henry" title="Joseph Henry" id="mwDk8">Joseph Henry</a> the following year. Faraday is credited with inventing the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_generator" title="Electric generator" id="mwDlA">electric generator</a> called the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homopolar_generator" title="Homopolar generator" id="mwDlE">Faraday disk</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDlI"><b id="mwDlM">1833</b>: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Babbage" title="Charles Babbage" id="mwDlQ">Charles Babbage</a> introduces his "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_calculating_machine" title="Mechanical calculating machine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDlU">mechanical calculating machine</a>", the first mechanical computer<sup about="#mwt1382" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwDlY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlg">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDlo"><b id="mwDls">1834:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moritz_von_Jacobi" title="Moritz von Jacobi" id="mwDlw">Moritz von Jacobi</a> invents the first practical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_motor" title="Electric motor" id="mwDl0">electric motor</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDl4"><b id="mwDl8">1835:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Henry" title="Joseph Henry" id="mwDmA">Joseph Henry</a> invents the electromechanical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relay" title="Relay" id="mwDmE">relay</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDmI"><b id="mwDmM">1837:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_Morse" title="Samuel Morse" id="mwDmQ">Samuel Morse</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morse_code" title="Morse code" id="mwDmU">Morse code</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDmY"><b id="mwDmc">1838:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moritz_von_Jacobi" title="Moritz von Jacobi" id="mwDmg">Moritz von Jacobi</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrotyping" title="Electrotyping" id="mwDmk">electrotyping</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDmo"><b id="mwDms">1839:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Otis" title="William Otis" id="mwDmw">William Otis</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_shovel" title="Steam shovel" id="mwDm0">steam shovel</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDm4"><b id="mwDm8">1839:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Nasmyth" title="James Nasmyth" id="mwDnA">James Nasmyth</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_hammer" title="Steam hammer" id="mwDnE">steam hammer</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDnI"><b id="mwDnM">1839:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmond_Becquerel" title="Edmond Becquerel" id="mwDnQ">Edmond Becquerel</a> invents a method for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photovoltaic_effect" title="Photovoltaic effect" id="mwDnU">photovoltaic effect</a>, effectively producing the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_cell" title="Solar cell" id="mwDnY">solar cell</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDnc"><b id="mwDng">1839:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Goodyear" title="Charles Goodyear" id="mwDnk">Charles Goodyear</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vulcanization" title="Vulcanization" id="mwDno">vulcanized rubber</a>.<sup about="#mwt1385" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-489" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-489"}}'><a href="#cite_note-489" id="mwDns"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDnw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDn0">[</span>482<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDn4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDn8"><b id="mwDoA">1839:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Daguerre" title="Louis Daguerre" id="mwDoE">Louis Daguerre</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daguerreotype" title="Daguerreotype" id="mwDoI">daguerreotype</a> photography.<sup about="#mwt1388" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-490" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-490"}}'><a href="#cite_note-490" id="mwDoM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoU">[</span>483<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDoc"><b id="mwDog">1839:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirkpatrick_Macmillan" title="Kirkpatrick Macmillan" id="mwDok">Kirkpatrick Macmillan</a> invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bicycle" title="Bicycle" id="mwDoo">bicycle</a><sup about="#mwt1391" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-491" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-491"}}'><a href="#cite_note-491" id="mwDos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDo0">[</span>484<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDo4">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="40" id="mwDo8" aria-labelledby="1840s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1840s">1840s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=40" title="Edit section: 1840s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1392" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDpA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main list","href":"./Template:Main_list"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1840s#Science and technology"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1393" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1392" id="mwDpE">For a more comprehensive list, see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1840s#Science_and_technology" title="1840s">1840s §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Science and technology</a>.</div>
<ul id="mwDpI"><li id="mwDpM"><b id="mwDpQ">1840:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Herschel" title="John Herschel" id="mwDpU">John Herschel</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blueprint" title="Blueprint" id="mwDpY">blueprint</a>.<sup about="#mwt1397" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-492" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-492"}}'><a href="#cite_note-492" id="mwDpc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpk">[</span>485<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDps"><b id="mwDpw">1841:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Bain_(inventor)" title="Alexander Bain (inventor)" id="mwDp0">Alexander Bain</a> devises a printing telegraph.<sup about="#mwt1400" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-493" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-493"}}'><a href="#cite_note-493" id="mwDp4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDp8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqA">[</span>486<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDqI"><b id="mwDqM">1842:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Robert_Grove" title="William Robert Grove" id="mwDqQ">William Robert Grove</a> invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuel_cell" title="Fuel cell" id="mwDqU">fuel cell</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDqY"><b id="mwDqc">1842:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Bennet_Lawes" title="John Bennet Lawes" id="mwDqg">John Bennet Lawes</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superphosphate" title="Superphosphate" id="mwDqk">superphosphate</a>, the first man-made <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fertilizer" title="Fertilizer" id="mwDqo">fertilizer</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDqs"><b id="mwDqw">1844:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Gottlob_Keller" title="Friedrich Gottlob Keller" id="mwDq0">Friedrich Gottlob Keller</a> and, independently, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Fenerty" title="Charles Fenerty" id="mwDq4">Charles Fenerty</a> come up with the wood pulp method of paper production.</li>
<li id="mwDq8"><b id="mwDrA">1844:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Rynd" title="Francis Rynd" id="mwDrE">Francis Rynd</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypodermic_needle" title="Hypodermic needle" id="mwDrI">hypodermic needle</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDrM"><b id="mwDrQ">1844:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horace_Wells" title="Horace Wells" id="mwDrU">Horace Wells</a> successfully used <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nitrous_oxide" title="Nitrous oxide" id="mwDrY">nitrous oxide</a> as an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anesthesia" title="Anesthesia" id="mwDrc">anesthesia</a><sup about="#mwt1401" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwDrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDro">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDrw"><b id="mwDr0">1845:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Charles_Johnson" title="Isaac Charles Johnson" id="mwDr4">Isaac Charles Johnson</a> invents modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portland_cement" title="Portland cement" id="mwDr8">Portland cement</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDsA"><b id="mwDsE">1846:</b> Henri-Joseph Maus invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunnel_boring_machine" title="Tunnel boring machine" id="mwDsI">tunnel boring machine</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDsM"><b id="mwDsQ">1846:</b>  <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elias_Howe" title="Elias Howe" id="mwDsU">Elias Howe</a> received a patent for a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sewing_machine" title="Sewing machine" id="mwDsY">sewing machine</a>, the model for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singer_Sewing_Machine" title="Singer Sewing Machine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDsc">Singer Sewing Machine</a><sup about="#mwt1404" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-494" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-494"}}'><a href="#cite_note-494" id="mwDsg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDsk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDso">[</span>487<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDss">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1407" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-495" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-495"}}'><a href="#cite_note-495" id="mwDsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDs0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDs4">[</span>488<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDs8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDtA"><b id="mwDtE">1847:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascanio_Sobrero" title="Ascanio Sobrero" id="mwDtI">Ascanio Sobrero</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nitroglycerin" title="Nitroglycerin" id="mwDtM">nitroglycerin</a>, the first explosive made that was stronger than <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_powder" title="Black powder" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDtQ">black powder</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDtU"><b id="mwDtY">1848:</b> Jonathan J. Couch invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jackhammer" title="Jackhammer" id="mwDtc">pneumatic drill</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDtg"><b id="mwDtk">1848:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linus_Yale_Jr." title="Linus Yale Jr." id="mwDto">Linus Yale Sr.</a> invents the first modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pin_tumbler_lock" title="Pin tumbler lock" id="mwDts">pin tumbler lock</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDtw"><b id="mwDt0">1849:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Hunt_(inventor)" title="Walter Hunt (inventor)" id="mwDt4">Walter Hunt</a> invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Repeating_rifle" title="Repeating rifle" id="mwDt8">repeating rifle</a> to use metallic cartridges (of his own design) and a spring-fed magazine.</li>
<li id="mwDuA"><b id="mwDuE">1849:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_B._Francis" title="James B. Francis" id="mwDuI">James B. Francis</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_turbine" title="Francis turbine" id="mwDuM">Francis turbine</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDuQ"><b id="mwDuU">1849:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Hunt_(inventor)" title="Walter Hunt (inventor)" id="mwDuY">Walter Hunt</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safety_pin" title="Safety pin" id="mwDuc">safety pin</a>.<sup about="#mwt1410" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-496" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-496"}}'><a href="#cite_note-496" id="mwDug"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDuk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDuo">[</span>489<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDus">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="41" id="mwDuw" aria-labelledby="1850s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1850s">1850s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=41" title="Edit section: 1850s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwDu0"><li id="mwDu4"><b id="mwDu8">1850:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Armstrong,_1st_Baron_Armstrong" title="William Armstrong, 1st Baron Armstrong" id="mwDvA">William Armstrong</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydraulic_accumulator" title="Hydraulic accumulator" id="mwDvE">hydraulic accumulator</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDvI"><b id="mwDvM">1851:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Jennings" title="George Jennings" id="mwDvQ">George Jennings</a> offers the first public <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flush_toilet" title="Flush toilet" id="mwDvU">flush toilets</a>, accessible for a penny per visit, and in 1852 receives a UK patent for the single piece, free standing, earthenware, trap plumed, flushing, water-closet.<sup about="#mwt1413" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-497" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-497"}}'><a href="#cite_note-497" id="mwDvY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDvc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvg">[</span>490<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDvo"><b id="mwDvs">1852:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Bunsen" title="Robert Bunsen" id="mwDvw">Robert Bunsen</a> is the first to use a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_vapor_deposition" title="Chemical vapor deposition" id="mwDv0">chemical vapor deposition</a> technique.</li>
<li id="mwDv4"><b id="mwDv8">1852:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elisha_Otis" title="Elisha Otis" id="mwDwA">Elisha Otis</a> invents the safety brake elevator.<sup about="#mwt1414" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-498" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-498"}}'><a href="#cite_note-498" id="mwDwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwM">[</span>491<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDwU"><b id="mwDwY">1852:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Giffard" title="Henri Giffard" id="mwDwc">Henri Giffard</a> becomes the first person to make a manned, controlled and powered flight using a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirigible" title="Dirigible" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDwg">dirigible</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDwk"><b id="mwDwo">1853:</b> François Coignet invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reinforced_concrete" title="Reinforced concrete" id="mwDws">reinforced concrete</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDww"><b id="mwDw0">1855:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Clerk_Maxwell" title="James Clerk Maxwell" id="mwDw4">James Clerk Maxwell</a> invents the first practical method for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_photography" title="Color photography" id="mwDw8">color photography</a>, whether chemical or electronic.</li>
<li id="mwDxA"><b id="mwDxE">1855:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Bessemer" title="Henry Bessemer" id="mwDxI">Henry Bessemer</a> patents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bessemer_process" title="Bessemer process" id="mwDxM">Bessemer process</a> for making steel, with improvements made by others over the following years.</li>
<li id="mwDxQ"><b id="mwDxU">1856:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Parkes" title="Alexander Parkes" id="mwDxY">Alexander Parkes</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkesine" title="Parkesine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDxc">parkesine</a>, also known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celluloid" title="Celluloid" id="mwDxg">celluloid</a>, the first man-made <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plastic" title="Plastic" id="mwDxk">plastic</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDxo"><b id="mwDxs">1856:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Harrison_(engineer)" title="James Harrison (engineer)" id="mwDxw">James Harrison</a> produces the world's first practical ice making machine and refrigerator using the principle of vapour compression in Geelong, Australia.<sup about="#mwt1417" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-499" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-499"}}'><a href="#cite_note-499" id="mwDx0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDx4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDx8">[</span>492<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDyE"><b id="mwDyI">1856:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Henry_Perkin" title="William Henry Perkin" id="mwDyM">William Henry Perkin</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauveine" title="Mauveine" id="mwDyQ">mauveine</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthetic_dye" title="Synthetic dye" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDyU">synthetic dye</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDyY"><b id="mwDyc">1857:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heinrich_Geissler" title="Heinrich Geissler" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDyg">Heinrich Geissler</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geissler_tube" title="Geissler tube" id="mwDyk">Geissler tube</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDyo"><b id="mwDys">1857:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phonautograph" title="Phonautograph" id="mwDyw">phonautograph</a>, the earliest known device for recording sound, is patented and invented by Frenchman <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Édouard-Léon_Scott_de_Martinville" title="Édouard-Léon Scott de Martinville" id="mwDy0">Édouard-Léon Scott de Martinville</a>.</li>
<li id="mwDy4"><b id="mwDy8">1859:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaston_Planté" title="Gaston Planté" id="mwDzA">Gaston Planté</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lead-acid" title="Lead-acid" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDzE">lead acid battery</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rechargeable_battery" title="Rechargeable battery" id="mwDzI">rechargeable battery</a>.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="42" id="mwDzM" aria-labelledby="1860s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1860s">1860s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=42" title="Edit section: 1860s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwDzQ"><li id="mwDzU"><b id="mwDzY">1860:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Swan" title="Joseph Swan" id="mwDzc">Joseph Swan</a> produces <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_fibers" title="Carbon fibers" id="mwDzg">carbon fibers</a>.<sup about="#mwt1420" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-500" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-500"}}'><a href="#cite_note-500" id="mwDzk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDzo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzs">[</span>493<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwDz0"><b id="mwDz4">1862:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Jordan_Gatling" title="Richard Jordan Gatling" id="mwDz8">Richard Jordan Gatling</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gatling_gun" title="Gatling gun" id="mwD0A">Gatling gun</a>, the first multi-barrel rapid-fire gun.<sup about="#mwt1421" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:11_411-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:11-411" id="mwD0E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD0I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0M">[</span>404<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0Q">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1424" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-501" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-501"}}'><a href="#cite_note-501" id="mwD0U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD0Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0c">[</span>494<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0g">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD0k"><b id="mwD0o">1864:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Pasteur" title="Louis Pasteur" id="mwD0s">Louis Pasteur</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pasteurization" title="Pasteurization" id="mwD0w">pasteurization</a> process.<sup about="#mwt1427" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-502" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-502"}}'><a href="#cite_note-502" id="mwD00"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD04"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD08">[</span>495<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1A">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1430" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-503" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-503"}}'><a href="#cite_note-503" id="mwD1E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD1I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1M">[</span>496<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1Q">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD1U"><b id="mwD1Y">1865:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Wilhelm_Siemens" title="Carl Wilhelm Siemens" id="mwD1c">Carl Wilhelm Siemens</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierre-Émile_Martin" title="Pierre-Émile Martin" id="mwD1g">Pierre-Émile Martin</a> invent the Siemens-Martin process for making steel.</li>
<li id="mwD1k"><b id="mwD1o">1867:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfred_Nobel" title="Alfred Nobel" id="mwD1s">Alfred Nobel</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamite" title="Dynamite" id="mwD1w">dynamite</a>, the first safely manageable explosive stronger than <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_powder" title="Black powder" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD10">black powder</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD14"><b id="mwD18">1867:</b> Lucien B. Smith invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbed_wire" title="Barbed wire" id="mwD2A">barbed wire</a>.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="43" id="mwD2E" aria-labelledby="1870s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1870s">1870s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=43" title="Edit section: 1870s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwD2I"><li id="mwD2M"><b id="mwD2Q">1872:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyvinyl_chloride" title="Polyvinyl chloride" id="mwD2U">Polyvinyl chloride</a>, more commonly known as vinyl, is synthesized by German chemist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugen_Baumann" title="Eugen Baumann" id="mwD2Y">Eugen Baumann</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD2c"><b id="mwD2g">1872:</b> J. E. T. Woods and J. Clark invent <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stainless_steel" title="Stainless steel" id="mwD2k">stainless steel</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Brearley" title="Harry Brearley" id="mwD2o">Harry Brearley</a> is the first to commercialize it.<sup about="#mwt1433" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-504" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-504"}}'><a href="#cite_note-504" id="mwD2s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD2w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD20">[</span>497<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD24">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD28"><b id="mwD3A">1873:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_Ransome" title="Frederick Ransome" id="mwD3E">Frederick Ransome</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rotary_kiln" title="Rotary kiln" id="mwD3I">rotary kiln</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD3M"><b id="mwD3Q">1873:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Crookes" title="William Crookes" id="mwD3U">William Crookes</a>, a chemist, invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crookes_radiometer" title="Crookes radiometer" id="mwD3Y">Crookes radiometer</a> as the by-product of some chemical research.</li>
<li id="mwD3c"><b id="mwD3g">1873:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zénobe_Gramme" title="Zénobe Gramme" id="mwD3k">Zénobe Gramme</a> invents the first commercial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electrical_generator" title="Electrical generator" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD3o">electrical generator</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gramme_machine" title="Gramme machine" id="mwD3s">Gramme machine</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD3w"><b id="mwD30">1874:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustave_Trouvé" title="Gustave Trouvé" id="mwD34">Gustave Trouvé</a> invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal_detector" title="Metal detector" id="mwD38">metal detector</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD4A"><b id="mwD4E">1874:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferdinand_von_Zeppelin" title="Ferdinand von Zeppelin" id="mwD4I">Ferdinand von Zeppelin</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeppelin" title="Zeppelin" id="mwD4M">Zeppelin</a> rigid airship.</li>
<li id="mwD4Q"><b id="mwD4U">1875:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fyodor_Pirotsky" title="Fyodor Pirotsky" id="mwD4Y">Fyodor Pirotsky</a> invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_tram" title="Electric tram" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD4c">electric tram</a> near <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Petersburg,_Russia" title="Saint Petersburg, Russia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD4g">Saint Petersburg, Russia</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD4k"><b id="mwD4o">1876:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolaus_August_Otto" title="Nicolaus August Otto" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD4s">Nicolaus August Otto</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four-stroke_cycle" title="Four-stroke cycle" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD4w">four-stroke cycle</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD40"><b id="mwD44">1876:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Graham_Bell" title="Alexander Graham Bell" id="mwD48">Alexander Graham Bell</a> has a patent granted for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telephone" title="Telephone" id="mwD5A">telephone</a>.<sup about="#mwt1434" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwD5E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD5I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5M">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5Q">]</span></span></a></sup> However, other inventors before Bell had worked on the development of the telephone and the invention had several pioneers.<sup about="#mwt1437" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Geisst_505-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Geisst"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Geisst-505"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Geisst-505" id="mwD5U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD5Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5c">[</span>498<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5g">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD5k"><b id="mwD5o">1877:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Edison" title="Thomas Edison" id="mwD5s">Thomas Edison</a> invents the first working <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phonograph" title="Phonograph" id="mwD5w">phonograph</a>.<sup about="#mwt1440" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-506" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-506"}}'><a href="#cite_note-506" id="mwD50"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD54"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD58">[</span>499<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD6E"><b id="mwD6I">1878:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Fleuss" title="Henry Fleuss" id="mwD6M">Henry Fleuss</a> is granted a patent for the first practical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebreather" title="Rebreather" id="mwD6Q">rebreather</a>.<sup about="#mwt1443" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rebreather_hx_507-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rebreather_hx"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-rebreather_hx-507"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rebreather_hx-507" id="mwD6U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD6Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6c">[</span>500<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6g">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD6k"><b id="mwD6o">1878:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lester_Allan_Pelton" title="Lester Allan Pelton" id="mwD6s">Lester Allan Pelton</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelton_wheel" title="Pelton wheel" id="mwD6w">Pelton wheel</a>, a type of water turbine.</li>
<li id="mwD60"><b id="mwD64">1879:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Swan" title="Joseph Swan" id="mwD68">Joseph Swan</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Edison" title="Thomas Edison" id="mwD7A">Thomas Edison</a> both patent a functional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incandescent_light_bulb" title="Incandescent light bulb" id="mwD7E">incandescent light bulb</a>.<sup about="#mwt1444" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwD7I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD7M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7Q">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7U">]</span></span></a></sup> Some two dozen inventors had experimented with electric incandescent lighting over the first three-quarters of the 19th century but never came up with a practical design.<sup about="#mwt1445" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-508" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-508"}}'><a href="#cite_note-508" id="mwD7Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD7c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7g">[</span>501<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7k">]</span></span></a></sup> Swan's, which he had been working on since the 1860s, had a low resistance so was only suited for small installations. Edison designed a high-resistance bulb as part of a large-scale commercial electric lighting utility.<sup about="#mwt1446" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-509" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-509"}}'><a href="#cite_note-509" id="mwD7o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD7s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7w">[</span>502<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD70">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1447" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-510" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-510"}}'><a href="#cite_note-510" id="mwD74"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD78"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8A">[</span>503<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1448" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-511" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-511"}}'><a href="#cite_note-511" id="mwD8I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD8M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8Q">[</span>504<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8U">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="44" id="mwD8Y" aria-labelledby="1880s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1880s">1880s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=44" title="Edit section: 1880s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwD8c"><li id="mwD8g"><b id="mwD8k">1881:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikolay_Benardos" title="Nikolay Benardos" id="mwD8o">Nikolay Benardos</a> presents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_arc_welding" title="Carbon arc welding" id="mwD8s">carbon arc welding</a>, the first practical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arc_welding" title="Arc welding" id="mwD8w">arc welding</a> method.<sup about="#mwt1451" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-512" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-512"}}'><a href="#cite_note-512" id="mwD80"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD84"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD88">[</span>505<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9A">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD9E"><b id="mwD9I">1884:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hiram_Maxim" title="Hiram Maxim" id="mwD9M">Hiram Maxim</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recoil_operation" title="Recoil operation" id="mwD9Q">recoil-operated</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maxim_gun" title="Maxim gun" id="mwD9U">Maxim gun</a>, ushering in the age of semi- and fully automatic firearms.</li>
<li id="mwD9Y"><b id="mwD9c">1884:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Vieille" title="Paul Vieille" id="mwD9g">Paul Vieille</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poudre_B" title="Poudre B" id="mwD9k">Poudre B</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smokeless_powder" title="Smokeless powder" id="mwD9o">smokeless powder</a> for firearms.</li>
<li id="mwD9s"><b id="mwD9w">1884:</b> Sir <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Algernon_Parsons" title="Charles Algernon Parsons" id="mwD90">Charles Parsons</a> invents the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam_turbine" title="Steam turbine" id="mwD94">steam turbine</a>.</li>
<li id="mwD98"><b id="mwD-A">1884:</b> Hungarian engineers <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Károly_Zipernowsky" title="Károly Zipernowsky" id="mwD-E">Károly Zipernowsky</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottó_Bláthy" title="Ottó Bláthy" id="mwD-I">Ottó Bláthy</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miksa_Déri" title="Miksa Déri" id="mwD-M">Miksa Déri</a> invent the closed core high efficiency transformer and the AC parallel power distribution.</li>
<li id="mwD-Q"><b id="mwD-U">1885:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Kemp_Starley" title="John Kemp Starley" id="mwD-Y">John Kemp Starley</a> invents the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safety_bicycle" title="Safety bicycle" id="mwD-c">safety bicycle</a>.<sup about="#mwt1454" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-513" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-513"}}'><a href="#cite_note-513" id="mwD-g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-o">[</span>506<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1458" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-514" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-514"}}'><a href="#cite_note-514" id="mwD-w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-4">[</span>507<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwD_A"><b id="mwD_E">1886:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Gassner" title="Carl Gassner" id="mwD_I">Carl Gassner</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zinc–carbon_battery" title="Zinc–carbon battery" id="mwD_M">zinc–carbon battery</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dry_cell" title="Dry cell" id="mwD_Q">dry cell battery</a>, making portable electronics practical.</li>
<li id="mwD_U"><b id="mwD_Y">1886:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Martin_Hall" title="Charles Martin Hall" id="mwD_c">Charles Martin Hall</a> and independently <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Héroult" title="Paul Héroult" id="mwD_g">Paul Héroult</a> invent the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hall–Héroult_process" title="Hall–Héroult process" id="mwD_k">Hall–Héroult process</a> for economically producing aluminum in 1886.</li>
<li id="mwD_o"><b id="mwD_s">1886:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Benz" title="Karl Benz" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD_w">Karl Benz</a> invents the first petrol or gasoline powered auto-mobile (car).<sup about="#mwt1460" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-515" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-515"}}'><a href="#cite_note-515" id="mwD_0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD_4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_8">[</span>508<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1461" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwEAE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEAI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAM">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEAU"><b id="mwEAY">1887:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Josef_Bayer" title="Carl Josef Bayer" id="mwEAc">Carl Josef Bayer</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayer_process" title="Bayer process" id="mwEAg">Bayer process</a> for the production of alumina.</li>
<li id="mwEAk"><b id="mwEAo">1887:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Blyth_(engineer)" title="James Blyth (engineer)" id="mwEAs">James Blyth</a> invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind_turbine" title="Wind turbine" id="mwEAw">wind turbine</a> used for generating electricity.</li>
<li id="mwEA0"><b id="mwEA4">1887:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stewart_MacArthur" title="John Stewart MacArthur" id="mwEA8">John Stewart MacArthur</a>, working in collaboration with brothers Dr. Robert and Dr. William Forrest, develops the process of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_cyanidation" title="Gold cyanidation" id="mwEBA">gold cyanidation</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEBE"><b id="mwEBI">1888:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_J._Loud" title="John J. Loud" id="mwEBM">John J. Loud</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballpoint_pen" title="Ballpoint pen" id="mwEBQ">ballpoint pen</a>.<sup about="#mwt1462" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-516" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-516"}}'><a href="#cite_note-516" id="mwEBU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEBY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBc">[</span>509<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEBk"><b id="mwEBo">1888:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Edison" title="Thomas Edison" id="mwEBs">Thomas Edison</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Kennedy_Dickson" title="William Kennedy Dickson" id="mwEBw">William Kennedy Dickson</a> invent the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinetoscope" title="Kinetoscope" id="mwEB0">Kinetoscope</a>.<sup about="#mwt1465" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-517" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-517"}}'><a href="#cite_note-517" id="mwEB4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEB8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECA">[</span>510<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwECI"><b id="mwECM">1888:</b> The first practical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneumatic_tire" title="Pneumatic tire" class="mw-redirect" id="mwECQ">pneumatic tire</a> was made by Scotsman <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Boyd_Dunlop" title="John Boyd Dunlop" id="mwECU">John Boyd Dunlop</a>, the patent was from 1847 by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_William_Thomson" title="Robert William Thomson" id="mwECY">Robert William Thomson</a></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="45" id="mwECc" aria-labelledby="1890s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1890s">1890s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=45" title="Edit section: 1890s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwECg"><li id="mwECk"><b id="mwECo">1890s:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frédéric_Swarts" title="Frédéric Swarts" id="mwECs">Frédéric Swarts</a> invents the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chlorofluorocarbon" title="Chlorofluorocarbon" id="mwECw">chlorofluorocarbons</a> to be applied as refrigerant.<sup about="#mwt1468" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Sneader2005_518-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Sneader2005"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Sneader2005-518"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Sneader2005-518" id="mwEC0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEC4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEC8">[</span>511<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEDE"><b id="mwEDI">1890:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Gair" title="Robert Gair" id="mwEDM">Robert Gair</a> invents the pre-cut <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardboard_box" title="Cardboard box" id="mwEDQ">cardboard box</a>.<sup about="#mwt1471" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-519" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-519"}}'><a href="#cite_note-519" id="mwEDU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEDY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDc">[</span>512<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEDk"><b id="mwEDo">1891:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitcomb_Judson" title="Whitcomb Judson" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEDs">Whitcomb Judson</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zipper" title="Zipper" id="mwEDw">zipper</a>.</li>
<li id="mwED0"><b id="mwED4">1892:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Léon_Bouly" title="Léon Bouly" id="mwED8">Léon Bouly</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinematograph" title="Cinematograph" id="mwEEA">cinematograph</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEEE"><b id="mwEEI">1892:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Ahearn" title="Thomas Ahearn" id="mwEEM">Thomas Ahearn</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_stove" title="Electric stove" id="mwEEQ">electric oven</a>.<sup about="#mwt1474" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-520" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-520"}}'><a href="#cite_note-520" id="mwEEU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEEY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEc">[</span>513<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEEk"><b id="mwEEo">1892</b>: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Froelich" title="John Froelich" id="mwEEs">John Froelich</a> invented the gas-powered <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tractor" title="Tractor" id="mwEEw">tractor</a><sup about="#mwt1475" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwEE0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEE4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEE8">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEFE"><b id="mwEFI">1893:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudolf_Diesel" title="Rudolf Diesel" id="mwEFM">Rudolf Diesel</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diesel_engine" title="Diesel engine" id="mwEFQ">diesel engine</a> (although <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbert_Akroyd_Stuart" title="Herbert Akroyd Stuart" id="mwEFU">Herbert Akroyd Stuart</a> had experimented with compression ignition before Diesel).</li>
<li id="mwEFY"><b id="mwEFc">1893:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Stewart_Halsted" title="William Stewart Halsted" id="mwEFg">William Stewart Halsted</a>, invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubber_glove" title="Rubber glove" id="mwEFk">rubber glove</a> for his wife <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caroline_Hampton" title="Caroline Hampton" id="mwEFo">Caroline Hampton</a> as he noticed her hands were affected by the daily surgeries she had performed. The gloves were intended to prevent medical staff from developing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dermatitis" title="Dermatitis" id="mwEFs">dermatitis</a> from surgical chemicals.<sup about="#mwt1478" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-521" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-521"}}'><a href="#cite_note-521" id="mwEFw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEF0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEF4">[</span>514<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEF8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1481" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-522" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-522"}}'><a href="#cite_note-522" id="mwEGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGI">[</span>515<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-523" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-523"}}'><a href="#cite_note-523" id="mwEGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGY">[</span>516<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGc">]</span></span></a></sup> The first modern disposable glove was created by Ansell Rubber Co. Pty. Ltd. in 1965.<sup about="#mwt1487" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-524" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-524"}}'><a href="#cite_note-524" id="mwEGg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGo">[</span>517<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1490" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-525" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-525"}}'><a href="#cite_note-525" id="mwEGw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEG0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEG4">[</span>518<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEG8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1493" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-526" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-526"}}'><a href="#cite_note-526" id="mwEHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEHE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHI">[</span>519<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEHQ"><b id="mwEHU">1895:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guglielmo_Marconi" title="Guglielmo Marconi" id="mwEHY">Guglielmo Marconi</a> invents the radio, a system of wireless communication using radio waves.<sup about="#mwt1494" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwEHc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEHg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHk">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEHs"><b id="mwEHw">1895:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilhelm_Conrad_Röntgen" title="Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEH0">Wilhelm Conrad Röntgen</a> invented the first radiograph (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xrays" title="Xrays" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEH4">X-ray</a>).</li>
<li id="mwEH8"><b id="mwEIA">1897:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surgical_masks" title="Surgical masks" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEIE">Surgical masks</a> made of cloth were developed in Europe by physicians <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Mikulicz-Radecki" title="Jan Mikulicz-Radecki" id="mwEII">Jan Mikulicz-Radecki</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Breslau" title="University of Breslau" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEIM">University of Breslau</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Berger_(physician)" title="Paul Berger (physician)" id="mwEIQ">Paul Berger</a> in Paris, as a result of increasing awareness of germ theory and the importance of antiseptic procedures in medicine.<sup about="#mwt1497" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-527" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-527"}}'><a href="#cite_note-527" id="mwEIU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEIY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIc">[</span>520<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEIk"><b id="mwEIo">1898:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_von_Pechmann" title="Hans von Pechmann" id="mwEIs">Hans von Pechmann</a> synthesizes <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyethylene" title="Polyethylene" id="mwEIw">polyethylene</a>, now the most common <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plastic" title="Plastic" id="mwEI0">plastic</a> in the world.<sup about="#mwt1500" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-528" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-528"}}'><a href="#cite_note-528" id="mwEI4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEI8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJA">[</span>521<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEJI"><b id="mwEJM">1899:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldemar_Jungner" title="Waldemar Jungner" id="mwEJQ">Waldemar Jungner</a> invents the rechargeable <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nickel-cadmium_battery" title="Nickel-cadmium battery" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEJU">nickel-cadmium battery</a> (NiCd) as well as the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nickel-iron_battery" title="Nickel-iron battery" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEJY">nickel-iron electric storage battery</a> (NiFe) and the rechargeable alkaline <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver-cadmium_battery" title="Silver-cadmium battery" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEJc">silver-cadmium battery</a> (AgCd)</li></ul>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="46" id="mwEJg" aria-labelledby="20th_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="20th_century">20th century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=46" title="Edit section: 20th century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="47" id="mwEJk" aria-labelledby="1900s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1900s">1900s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=47" title="Edit section: 1900s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwEJo"><li id="mwEJs"><b id="mwEJw">1901:</b> The first motorized cleaner using suction, a powered "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacuum_cleaner" title="Vacuum cleaner" id="mwEJ0">vacuum cleaner</a>", is patented independently by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hubert_Cecil_Booth" title="Hubert Cecil Booth" id="mwEJ4">Hubert Cecil Booth</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_T._Kenney" title="David T. Kenney" id="mwEJ8">David T. Kenney</a>.<sup about="#mwt1501" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-529" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-529"}}'><a href="#cite_note-529" id="mwEKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEKE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKI">[</span>522<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEKQ"><b id="mwEKU">1903:</b> The first successful <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gas_turbine" title="Gas turbine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEKY">gas turbine</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ægidius_Elling" title="Ægidius Elling" id="mwEKc">Ægidius Elling</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEKg"><b id="mwEKk">1903:</b> Édouard Bénédictus invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laminated_glass" title="Laminated glass" id="mwEKo">laminated glass</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEKs"><b id="mwEKw">1903:</b> The first successful controlled powered flights of a heavier than air vehicle are made by Wilbur and Orvile Wright</li>
<li id="mwEK0"><b id="mwEK4">1904:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fleming_valve" title="Fleming valve" id="mwEK8">Fleming valve</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacuum_tube" title="Vacuum tube" id="mwELA">vacuum tube</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diode" title="Diode" id="mwELE">diode</a>, is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Ambrose_Fleming" title="John Ambrose Fleming" id="mwELI">John Ambrose Fleming</a>.</li>
<li id="mwELM"><b id="mwELQ">1907:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_Baekeland" title="Leo Baekeland" id="mwELU">Leo Baekeland</a> invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakelite" title="Bakelite" id="mwELY">bakelite</a>,  the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plastic" title="Plastic" id="mwELc">plastic</a> made from synthetic components.</li>
<li id="mwELg"><b id="mwELk">1907:</b> The tuyères thermopropulsives<sup about="#mwt1506" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Peter_530-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Peter"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Peter-530"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Peter-530" id="mwELo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwELs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELw">[</span>523<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEL0">]</span></span></a></sup> after 1945 (<a rel="mw:WikiLink/Interwiki" href="https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurice%20Roy%20(professeur)" title="fr:Maurice Roy (professeur)" class="extiw" id="mwEL4">Maurice Roy (fr)</a>) known as the <i id="mwEL8">statoreacteur</i><sup about="#mwt1507" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Peter_530-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Peter"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Peter-530" id="mwEMA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEME"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMI">[</span>523<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1508" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-531" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-531"}}'><a href="#cite_note-531" id="mwEMQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEMU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMY">[</span>524<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMc">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id="mwEMg">a combustion subsonique</i> (the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramjet" title="Ramjet" id="mwEMk">ramjet</a>)<sup about="#mwt1510" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-532" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-532"}}'><a href="#cite_note-532" id="mwEMo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEMs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMw">[</span>525<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEM0">]</span></span></a></sup> – <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/René_Lorin" title="René Lorin" id="mwEM4">R. Lorin</a><sup about="#mwt1511" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Lorin_533-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Lorin"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Lorin-533"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Lorin-533" id="mwEM8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwENA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENE">[</span>526<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1512" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-534" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-534"}}'><a href="#cite_note-534" id="mwENM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwENQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENU">[</span>527<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1517" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-535" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-535"}}'><a href="#cite_note-535" id="mwENc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwENg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENk">[</span>528<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwENs"><b id="mwENw">1908:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cellophane" title="Cellophane" id="mwEN0">Cellophane</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacques_E._Brandenberger" title="Jacques E. Brandenberger" id="mwEN4">Jacques E. Brandenberger</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEN8"><b id="mwEOA">1909:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fritz_Haber" title="Fritz Haber" id="mwEOE">Fritz Haber</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haber_process" title="Haber process" id="mwEOI">Haber process</a>.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="48" id="mwEOM" aria-labelledby="1910s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1910s">1910s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=48" title="Edit section: 1910s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwEOQ"><li id="mwEOU"><b id="mwEOY">1911:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud_chamber" title="Cloud chamber" id="mwEOc">cloud chamber</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Particle_detector" title="Particle detector" id="mwEOg">particle detector</a>, is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Thomson_Rees_Wilson" title="Charles Thomson Rees Wilson" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEOk">Charles Thomson Rees Wilson</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEOo"><b id="mwEOs">1913:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bergius_process" title="Bergius process" id="mwEOw">Bergius process</a> is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friedrich_Bergius" title="Friedrich Bergius" id="mwEO0">Friedrich Bergius</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEO4"><b id="mwEO8">1913:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaplan_turbine" title="Kaplan turbine" id="mwEPA">Kaplan turbine</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viktor_Kaplan" title="Viktor Kaplan" id="mwEPE">Viktor Kaplan</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEPI"><b id="mwEPM">1915:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Brearley" title="Harry Brearley" id="mwEPQ">Harry Brearley</a> invents a process to create <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martensitic_stainless_steel" title="Martensitic stainless steel" id="mwEPU">Martensitic stainless steel</a>, initially labelled Rustless Steel, later marketed as Staybrite, and AISI Type 420.<sup about="#mwt1520" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYT_536-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYT"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYT-536"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYT-536" id="mwEPY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEPc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPg">[</span>529<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEPo"><b id="mwEPs">1915:</b> The first operational military <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanks" title="Tanks" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEPw">tanks</a> are designed in Great Britain and France. They are used in battle from 1916 and 1917 respectively. The designers in Great Britain are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Gordon_Wilson" title="Walter Gordon Wilson" id="mwEP0">Walter Wilson</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Tritton" title="William Tritton" id="mwEP4">William Tritton</a> and in France, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eugène_Brillié" title="Eugène Brillié" id="mwEP8">Eugène Brillié</a>. (Although it is known that vehicles incorporating at least some of the features of the tank were designed in a number of countries from 1903 onward, none reached a practical form.)</li>
<li id="mwEQA"><b id="mwEQE">1916:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Czochralski_process" title="Czochralski process" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEQI">Czochralski process</a>, widely used for the production of single crystal <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silicon" title="Silicon" id="mwEQM">silicon</a>, is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Czochralski" title="Jan Czochralski" id="mwEQQ">Jan Czochralski</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEQU"><b id="mwEQY">1917:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal_oscillator" title="Crystal oscillator" id="mwEQc">crystal oscillator</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_M._Nicolson" title="Alexander M. Nicolson" id="mwEQg">Alexander M. Nicolson</a> using a crystal of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rochelle_Salt" title="Rochelle Salt" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEQk">Rochelle Salt</a> although his priority was disputed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Guyton_Cady" title="Walter Guyton Cady" id="mwEQo">Walter Guyton Cady</a>.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="49" id="mwEQs" aria-labelledby="1920s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1920s">1920s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=49" title="Edit section: 1920s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwEQw"><li id="mwEQ0"><b id="mwEQ4">1925:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fischer–Tropsch_process" title="Fischer–Tropsch process" id="mwEQ8">Fischer–Tropsch process</a> is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_Joseph_Emil_Fischer" title="Franz Joseph Emil Fischer" id="mwERA">Franz Fischer</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Tropsch" title="Hans Tropsch" id="mwERE">Hans Tropsch</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Max_Planck_Institute_for_Coal_Research" title="Max Planck Institute for Coal Research" id="mwERI">Kaiser-Wilhelm-Institut für Kohlenforschung</a>.</li>
<li id="mwERM"><b id="mwERQ">1926:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yagi-Uda_Antenna" title="Yagi-Uda Antenna" class="mw-redirect" id="mwERU">Yagi-Uda Antenna</a> or simply Yagi Antenna is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shintaro_Uda" title="Shintaro Uda" id="mwERY">Shintaro Uda</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tohoku_Imperial_University" title="Tohoku Imperial University" class="mw-redirect" id="mwERc">Tohoku Imperial University</a>, assisted by his colleague <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidetsugu_Yagi" title="Hidetsugu Yagi" id="mwERg">Hidetsugu Yagi</a>. The Yagi Antenna was widely used during <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II" title="World War II" id="mwERk">World War II</a>. After the war they saw extensive development as home <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Television_antennas" title="Television antennas" class="mw-redirect" id="mwERo">television antennas</a>.</li>
<li id="mwERs"><b id="mwERw">1926:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_H._Goddard" title="Robert H. Goddard" id="mwER0">Robert H. Goddard</a> launches the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bipropellant_rocket" title="Bipropellant rocket" class="mw-redirect" id="mwER4">liquid fueled rocket</a>.</li>
<li id="mwER8"><b id="mwESA">1926:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Ferguson" title="Harry Ferguson" id="mwESE">Harry Ferguson</a>, patents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three-point_hitch" title="Three-point hitch" id="mwESI">Three-point hitch</a> equipment linkage system for tractors.<sup about="#mwt1523" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-537" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-537"}}'><a href="#cite_note-537" id="mwESM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwESQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESU">[</span>530<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwESc"><b id="mwESg">1926:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Logie_Baird" title="John Logie Baird" id="mwESk">John Logie Baird</a> demonstrates the world's first live working <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_television" title="Mechanical television" id="mwESo">television</a> system.<sup about="#mwt1524" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-538" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-538"}}'><a href="#cite_note-538" id="mwESs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwESw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwES0">[</span>531<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwES4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1527" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Telegraph_539-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Telegraph"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Telegraph-539"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Telegraph-539" id="mwES8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwETA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETE">[</span>532<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1530" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-540" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-540"}}'><a href="#cite_note-540" id="mwETM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwETQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETU">[</span>533<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1531" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwETc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwETg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETk">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwETs"><b id="mwETw">1927:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartz_clock" title="Quartz clock" id="mwET0">quartz clock</a> is invented by Warren Marrison and J.W. Horton at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_Telephone_Laboratories" title="Bell Telephone Laboratories" class="mw-redirect" id="mwET4">Bell Telephone Laboratories</a>.<sup about="#mwt1534" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-541" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-541"}}'><a href="#cite_note-541" id="mwET8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEUA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUE">[</span>534<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEUM"><b id="mwEUQ">1928:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penicillin" title="Penicillin" id="mwEUU">Penicillin</a> is first observed to exude antibiotic substances by Nobel laureate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Fleming" title="Alexander Fleming" id="mwEUY">Alexander Fleming</a>.<sup about="#mwt1535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwEUc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUk">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUo">]</span></span></a></sup> Development of medicinal penicillin is attributed to a team of medics and scientists including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Howard_Walter_Florey" title="Howard Walter Florey" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEUs">Howard Walter Florey</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernst_Chain" title="Ernst Chain" id="mwEUw">Ernst Chain</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_Heatley" title="Norman Heatley" id="mwEU0">Norman Heatley</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEU4"><b id="mwEU8">1928:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Whittle" title="Frank Whittle" id="mwEVA">Frank Whittle</a> formally submitted his ideas for a turbo-jet engine. In October 1929, he developed his ideas further.<sup about="#mwt1538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-542" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-542"}}'><a href="#cite_note-542" id="mwEVE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEVI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVM">[</span>535<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVQ">]</span></span></a></sup> On 16 January 1930, Whittle submitted his first patent (granted in 1932).<sup about="#mwt1541" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-543" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-543"}}'><a href="#cite_note-543" id="mwEVU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEVY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVc">[</span>536<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEVk"><b id="mwEVo">1928:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philo_Farnsworth" title="Philo Farnsworth" id="mwEVs">Philo Farnsworth</a> demonstrates the first practical <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_television" title="Electronic television" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEVw">electronic television</a> to the press.</li>
<li id="mwEV0"><b id="mwEV4">1929:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball_screw" title="Ball screw" id="mwEV8">ball screw</a> is invented by Rudolph G. Boehm.</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="50" id="mwEWA" aria-labelledby="1930s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1930s">1930s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=50" title="Edit section: 1930s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwEWE"><li id="mwEWI"><b id="mwEWM">1930:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supersonic_combusting_ramjet" title="Supersonic combusting ramjet" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEWQ">Supersonic combusting ramjet</a> — <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Whittle" title="Frank Whittle" id="mwEWU">Frank Whittle</a>.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt1542" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEWY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"May 2024"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_May_2024" about="#mwt1542"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1542" id="mwEWc"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (May 2024)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></li>
<li id="mwEWg"><b id="mwEWk">1930:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phase-contrast_microscopy" title="Phase-contrast microscopy" id="mwEWo">Phase-contrast microscopy</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frits_Zernike" title="Frits Zernike" id="mwEWs">Frits Zernike</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEWw"><b id="mwEW0">1931:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electron_microscope" title="Electron microscope" id="mwEW4">electron microscope</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernst_Ruska" title="Ernst Ruska" id="mwEW8">Ernst Ruska</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEXA"><b id="mwEXE">1933:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FM_radio" title="FM radio" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEXI">FM radio</a> is patented by inventor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwin_H._Armstrong" title="Edwin H. Armstrong" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEXM">Edwin H. Armstrong</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEXQ"><b id="mwEXU">1933:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everest_and_Jennings" title="Everest and Jennings" id="mwEXY">Harry C. Jennings Sr. and Herbert Everest</a>, both <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanical_engineer" title="Mechanical engineer" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEXc">mechanical engineers</a>, invented the first lightweight, steel, folding, portable <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheelchair" title="Wheelchair" id="mwEXg">wheelchair</a> with their "X-brace" design.<sup about="#mwt1543" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-544" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-544"}}'><a href="#cite_note-544" id="mwEXk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEXo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEXs">[</span>537<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEXw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1546" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-545" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-545"}}'><a href="#cite_note-545" id="mwEX0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEX4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEX8">[</span>538<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEYE"><b id="mwEYI">1935:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nylon" title="Nylon" id="mwEYM">Nylon</a>, the first fully <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthetic_fiber" title="Synthetic fiber" id="mwEYQ">synthetic fiber</a> is produced by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wallace_Carothers" title="Wallace Carothers" id="mwEYU">Wallace Carothers</a> while working at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DuPont" title="DuPont" id="mwEYY">DuPont</a>.<sup about="#mwt1549" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Carothers_546-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Carothers"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Carothers-546"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Carothers-546" id="mwEYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYk">[</span>539<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEYs"><b id="mwEYw">1938:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z1_(computer)" title="Z1 (computer)" id="mwEY0">Z1</a>, built by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konrad_Zuse" title="Konrad Zuse" id="mwEY4">Konrad Zuse</a>, is the first freely programmable <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer" title="Computer" id="mwEY8">computer</a> in the world.</li>
<li id="mwEZA"><b id="mwEZE">1938:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_fission" title="Nuclear fission" id="mwEZI">Nuclear fission</a> discovered in experiment by chemists <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_Hahn" title="Otto Hahn" id="mwEZM">Otto Hahn</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fritz_Strassmann" title="Fritz Strassmann" id="mwEZQ">Fritz Strassmann</a> and physicists <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lise_Meitner" title="Lise Meitner" id="mwEZU">Lise Meitner</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_Robert_Frisch" title="Otto Robert Frisch" id="mwEZY">Otto Robert Frisch</a>. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_nuclear_energy_project" title="German nuclear energy project" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEZc">German nuclear energy project</a> was based on this research. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tube_Alloys" title="Tube Alloys" id="mwEZg">Tube Alloys</a> project and, subsequently, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Project" title="Manhattan Project" id="mwEZk">Manhattan Project</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_atomic_bomb_project" title="Soviet atomic bomb project" id="mwEZo">Soviet atomic bomb project</a> were influenced by this research.</li>
<li id="mwEZs"><b id="mwEZw">1939:</b> G. S. Yunyev or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naum_Gurvich" title="Naum Gurvich" id="mwEZ0">Naum Gurvich</a> invented the electric current <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Defibrillation#Direct_current_method" title="Defibrillation" id="mwEZ4">defibrillator</a></li>
<li id="mwEZ8"><b id="mwEaA">1939</b>: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Vincent_Atanasoff" title="John Vincent Atanasoff" id="mwEaE">John Vincent Atanasoff</a> invented the first electronic digital computer<sup about="#mwt1550" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwEaI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEaM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEaQ">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEaU">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="51" id="mwEaY" aria-labelledby="1940-1944"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="1940-1944">1940-1944</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=51" title="Edit section: 1940-1944"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwEac"><li id="mwEag"><b id="mwEak">1940:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isotopes_of_plutonium#Notable_isotopes" title="Isotopes of plutonium" id="mwEao">Pu-239 isotope</a> (isotope of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plutonium" title="Plutonium" id="mwEas">plutonium</a>)<sup about="#mwt1551" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-t2_547-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"t2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-t2-547"}}'><a href="#cite_note-t2-547" id="mwEaw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEa0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEa4">[</span>540<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEa8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1553" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-t3_548-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"t3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-t3-548"}}'><a href="#cite_note-t3-548" id="mwEbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEbE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbI">[</span>541<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbM">]</span></span></a></sup> a form of matter existing with the capacity for use as a destructive element<sup about="#mwt1554" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-549" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-549"}}'><a href="#cite_note-549" id="mwEbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEbU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbY">[</span>542<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbc">]</span></span></a></sup> (because the isotope has an exponentially increasing<sup about="#mwt1555" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-t2_547-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"t2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-t2-547" id="mwEbg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEbk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbo">[</span>540<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbs">]</span></span></a></sup> spontaneous<sup about="#mwt1558" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-550" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-550"}}'><a href="#cite_note-550" id="mwEbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEb0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEb4">[</span>543<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEb8">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spontaneous_fission" title="Spontaneous fission" id="mwEcA">fissile</a> decay<sup about="#mwt1559" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-551" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-551"}}'><a href="#cite_note-551" id="mwEcE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEcI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcM">[</span>544<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcQ">]</span></span></a></sup>) within <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_devices" title="Nuclear devices" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEcU">nuclear devices</a> — <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenn_Seaborg" title="Glenn Seaborg" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEcY">Glenn Seaborg</a>.<sup about="#mwt1560" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-t3_548-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"t3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-t3-548" id="mwEcc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEcg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEck">[</span>541<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEco">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEcs"><b id="mwEcw">1940:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Randall_(physicist)" title="John Randall (physicist)" id="mwEc0">John Randall</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Boot" title="Harry Boot" id="mwEc4">Harry Boot</a> would develop the high power, microwave generating, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cavity_magnetron" title="Cavity magnetron" id="mwEc8">cavity magnetron</a>, later applied to commercial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radar" title="Radar" id="mwEdA">Radar</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microwave_oven" title="Microwave oven" id="mwEdE">Microwave oven</a> appliances.<sup about="#mwt1563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-552" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-552"}}'><a href="#cite_note-552" id="mwEdI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEdM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEdQ">[</span>545<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEdU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEdY"><b id="mwEdc">1941:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polyester" title="Polyester" id="mwEdg">Polyester</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Rex_Whinfield" title="John Rex Whinfield" id="mwEdk">John Rex Whinfield</a> and James Dickson.<sup about="#mwt1567" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-553" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-553"}}'><a href="#cite_note-553" id="mwEdo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEds"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEdw">[</span>546<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEd0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEd4"><b id="mwEd8">1942:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V-2_rocket" title="V-2 rocket" id="mwEeA">V-2 rocket</a>, the world's first long range <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballistic_missile" title="Ballistic missile" id="mwEeE">ballistic missile</a>, developed by engineer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wernher_von_Braun" title="Wernher von Braun" id="mwEeI">Wernher von Braun</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEeM"><b id="mwEeQ">1942</b>: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enrico_Fermi" title="Enrico Fermi" id="mwEeU">Enrico Fermi</a> developed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_reactor" title="Nuclear reactor" id="mwEeY">nuclear reactor</a> and created the first controlled <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_chain_reaction" title="Nuclear chain reaction" id="mwEec">nuclear chain reaction</a><sup about="#mwt1568" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwEeg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEek"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEeo">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEes">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEew"><b id="mwEe0">1944:</b> The non-infectious viral vaccine is perfected by Dr. Jonas Salk and Thomas Francis.<sup about="#mwt1569" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-554" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-554"}}'><a href="#cite_note-554" id="mwEe4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEe8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfA">[</span>547<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfE">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="52" id="mwEfI" aria-labelledby="Contemporary_history"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Contemporary_history">Contemporary history</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=52" title="Edit section: Contemporary history"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="53" id="mwEfM" aria-labelledby="1945-1950"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1945-1950">1945-1950</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=53" title="Edit section: 1945-1950"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwEfQ"><li id="mwEfU"><b id="mwEfY">1945:</b> The atomic bomb is developed by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Project" title="Manhattan Project" id="mwEfc">Manhattan Project</a> and swiftly used in August 1945 in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atomic_bombings_of_Hiroshima_and_Nagasaki" title="Atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki" id="mwEfg">atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEfk"><b id="mwEfo">1945:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percy_Spencer" title="Percy Spencer" id="mwEfs">Percy Spencer</a>, while employed at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raytheon" title="Raytheon" id="mwEfw">Raytheon</a>, would patent a magnetron based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microwave_oven" title="Microwave oven" id="mwEf0">microwave oven</a>.<sup about="#mwt1572" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-555" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-555"}}'><a href="#cite_note-555" id="mwEf4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEf8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgA">[</span>548<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEgI"><b id="mwEgM">1945:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willard_Libby" title="Willard Libby" id="mwEgQ">Willard Libby</a> began his work on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiocarbon_dating" title="Radiocarbon dating" id="mwEgU">radiocarbon dating</a>. He published his paper in 1946,<sup about="#mwt1573" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bowman_9_556-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bowman_9"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bowman_9-556"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bowman_9-556" id="mwEgY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEgc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgg">[</span>549<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1576" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-557" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-557"}}'><a href="#cite_note-557" id="mwEgo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEgs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgw">[</span>550<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEg0">]</span></span></a></sup> a second paper in <i id="mwEg4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_(journal)" title="Science (journal)" id="mwEg8">Science</a></i> in 1947.<sup about="#mwt1577" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bowman_9_556-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bowman_9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bowman_9-556" id="mwEhA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEhE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhI">[</span>549<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1580" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Anderson_1947_558-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Anderson_1947"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Anderson_1947-558"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Anderson_1947-558" id="mwEhQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEhU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhY">[</span>551<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhc">]</span></span></a></sup> Libby and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_R._Arnold" title="James R. Arnold" id="mwEhg">James Arnold</a> succeeded with the radiocarbon dating theory after results were published in <i id="mwEhk">Science</i> in December 1949.<sup about="#mwt1583" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-libby49_559-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"libby49"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-libby49-559"}}'><a href="#cite_note-libby49-559" id="mwEho"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEhs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhw">[</span>552<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEh0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1584" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Aitken_60_560-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Aitken_60"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Aitken_60-560"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Aitken_60-560" id="mwEh4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEh8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEiA">[</span>553<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEiE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEiI"><b id="mwEiM">1946:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Martin_(engineer)" title="James Martin (engineer)" id="mwEiQ">James Martin</a> invents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ejector_seat" title="Ejector seat" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEiU">ejector seat</a>, inspired by the death of his friend and test pilot Captain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentine_Baker_(pilot)" title="Valentine Baker (pilot)" id="mwEiY">Valentine Baker</a> in an aeroplane crash in 1942.</li>
<li id="mwEic"><b id="mwEig">1947:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holography" title="Holography" id="mwEik">Holography</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dennis_Gabor" title="Dennis Gabor" id="mwEio">Dennis Gabor</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEis"><b id="mwEiw">1947:</b> Floyd Farris and J.B. Clark (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanolind_Oil_and_Gas_Corporation" title="Stanolind Oil and Gas Corporation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEi0">Stanolind Oil and Gas Corporation</a>) invents <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hydraulic_fracturing" title="Hydraulic fracturing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEi4">hydraulic fracturing</a> technology.<sup about="#mwt1587" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hubbarb_561-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hubbarb"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hubbarb-561"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hubbarb-561" id="mwEi8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEjA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEjE">[</span>554<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEjI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEjM"><b id="mwEjQ">1947:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transistor" title="Transistor" id="mwEjU">transistor</a>, a bipolar <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point-contact_transistor" title="Point-contact transistor" id="mwEjY">point-contact transistor</a>, is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Bardeen" title="John Bardeen" id="mwEjc">John Bardeen</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Brattain" title="Walter Brattain" id="mwEjg">Walter Brattain</a> under the supervision of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Shockley" title="William Shockley" id="mwEjk">William Shockley</a> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_Labs" title="Bell Labs" id="mwEjo">Bell Labs</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEjs"><b id="mwEjw">1948:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atomic_clock" title="Atomic clock" id="mwEj0">atomic clock</a> is developed at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Bureau_of_Standards" title="National Bureau of Standards" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEj4">National Bureau of Standards</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEj8"><b id="mwEkA">1948:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basic_oxygen_steelmaking" title="Basic oxygen steelmaking" id="mwEkE">Basic oxygen steelmaking</a> is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Durrer" title="Robert Durrer" id="mwEkI">Robert Durrer</a>. The majority of steel manufactured in the world is produced using the basic oxygen furnace; in 2000, it accounted for 60% of global steel output.<sup about="#mwt1588" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-S978_562-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"S978"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-S978-562"}}'><a href="#cite_note-S978-562" id="mwEkM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEkQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEkU">[</span>555<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEkY">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="54" id="mwEkc" aria-labelledby="1950s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1950s">1950s</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=54" title="Edit section: 1950s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwEkg"><li id="mwEkk"><b id="mwEko">1950:</b> <i id="mwEks"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bertie_the_Brain" title="Bertie the Brain" id="mwEkw">Bertie the Brain</a></i>, debatably the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_game" title="Video game" id="mwEk0">video game</a>, is displayed to the public at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_National_Exhibition" title="Canadian National Exhibition" id="mwEk4">Canadian National Exhibition</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEk8"><b id="mwElA">1950:</b> The Toroidal chamber with axial magnetic fields (the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokamak" title="Tokamak" id="mwElE">Tokamak</a>) is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igor_E._Tamm" title="Igor E. Tamm" class="mw-redirect" id="mwElI">Igor E. Tamm</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrei_D._Sakharov" title="Andrei D. Sakharov" class="mw-redirect" id="mwElM">Andrei D. Sakharov</a>.<sup about="#mwt1593" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-563" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-563"}}'><a href="#cite_note-563" id="mwElQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwElU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwElY">[</span>556<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwElc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwElg"><b id="mwElk">1952:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Float_glass" title="Float glass" id="mwElo">float glass process</a> is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alastair_Pilkington" title="Alastair Pilkington" id="mwEls">Alastair Pilkington</a>.<sup about="#mwt1596" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-564" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-564"}}'><a href="#cite_note-564" id="mwElw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEl0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEl4">[</span>557<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEl8">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEmA"><b id="mwEmE">1952:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermonuclear_weapon" title="Thermonuclear weapon" id="mwEmI">thermonuclear weapon</a> is developed.</li>
<li id="mwEmM"><b id="mwEmQ">1953:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_tape_recorder" title="Video tape recorder" id="mwEmU">video tape recorder</a>, a helical scan recorder, is invented by Norikazu Sawazaki.</li>
<li id="mwEmY"><b id="mwEmc">1954:</b> Invention of the solar battery by Bell Telephone scientists, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calvin_Souther_Fuller" title="Calvin Souther Fuller" id="mwEmg">Calvin Souther Fuller</a>, Daryl Chapin and Gerald Pearson capturing the Sun's power. First practical means of collecting energy from the Sun and turning it into a current of electricity.</li>
<li id="mwEmk"><b id="mwEmo">1955:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hovercraft" title="Hovercraft" id="mwEms">hovercraft</a> is patented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christopher_Cockerell" title="Christopher Cockerell" id="mwEmw">Christopher Cockerell</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEm0"><b id="mwEm4">1955</b>: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonas_Salk" title="Jonas Salk" id="mwEm8">Jonas Salk</a> received the license for his inactivated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polio_vaccine" title="Polio vaccine" id="mwEnA">polio vaccine</a></li>
<li id="mwEnE"><b id="mwEnI">1955:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intermodal_container" title="Intermodal container" id="mwEnM">intermodal container</a> is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malcom_McLean" title="Malcom McLean" id="mwEnQ">Malcom McLean</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEnU"><b id="mwEnY">1956:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_disk_drive" title="Hard disk drive" id="mwEnc">hard disk drive</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM" title="IBM" id="mwEng">IBM</a>.<sup about="#mwt1600" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-565" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-565"}}'><a href="#cite_note-565" id="mwEnk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEno"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEns">[</span>558<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEnw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEn0"><b id="mwEn4">1956:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic_Theorist" title="Logic Theorist" id="mwEn8">Logic Theorist</a> computer program, the first "artificial intelligence program", was written and invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allen_Newell" title="Allen Newell" id="mwEoA">Allen Newell</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbert_A._Simon" title="Herbert A. Simon" id="mwEoE">Herbert A. Simon</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cliff_Shaw" title="Cliff Shaw" id="mwEoI">Cliff Shaw</a>.<sup about="#mwt1604" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-mccCrevRussNorv_566-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"mccCrevRussNorv"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-mccCrevRussNorv-566"}}'><a href="#cite_note-mccCrevRussNorv-566" id="mwEoM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEoU">[</span>559<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEoY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEoc"><b id="mwEog">1957:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser" title="Laser" id="mwEok">laser</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optical_amplifier" title="Optical amplifier" id="mwEoo">optical amplifier</a> are invented and named by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gordon_Gould" title="Gordon Gould" id="mwEos">Gordon Gould</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_H._Townes" title="Charles H. Townes" id="mwEow">Charles Townes</a>. The laser and optical amplifier are foundational to powering the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet" title="Internet" id="mwEo0">Internet</a>.<sup about="#mwt1607" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-567" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-567"}}'><a href="#cite_note-567" id="mwEo4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEo8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEpA">[</span>560<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEpE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEpI"><b id="mwEpM">1957:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Personal_computer" title="Personal computer" id="mwEpQ">personal computer</a> used by one person and controlled by a keyboard, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_personal_computers#The_beginnings_of_the_personal_computer_industry" title="History of personal computers" id="mwEpU">IBM 610</a>, is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM" title="IBM" id="mwEpY">IBM</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEpc"><b id="mwEpg">1957:</b> The first artificial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satellite" title="Satellite" id="mwEpk">satellite</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sputnik_1" title="Sputnik 1" id="mwEpo">Sputnik 1</a>, is launched.</li>
<li id="mwEps"><b id="mwEpw">1958 – 1959:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_circuit" title="Integrated circuit" id="mwEp0">integrated circuit</a> is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invention_of_the_integrated_circuit" title="Invention of the integrated circuit" id="mwEp4">independently invented</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Kilby" title="Jack Kilby" id="mwEp8">Jack Kilby</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Noyce" title="Robert Noyce" id="mwEqA">Robert Noyce</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEqE"><b id="mwEqI">1959:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MOSFET" title="MOSFET" id="mwEqM">MOSFET</a> (MOS transistor) is invented by the Egyptian <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohamed_Atalla" title="Mohamed Atalla" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEqQ">Mohamed Atalla</a> and the Korean <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawon_Kahng" title="Dawon Kahng" id="mwEqU">Dawon Kahng</a> at Bell Labs. It is used in almost all modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_product" title="Electronic product" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEqY">electronic products</a>. It was smaller, faster, more reliable and cheaper to manufacture than earlier bipolar transistors, leading to a revolution in computers, controls and communication.<sup about="#mwt1610" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-568" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-568"}}'><a href="#cite_note-568" id="mwEqc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEqk">[</span>561<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEqo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1613" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-569" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-569"}}'><a href="#cite_note-569" id="mwEqs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEqw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEq0">[</span>562<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEq4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1616" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-570" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-570"}}'><a href="#cite_note-570" id="mwEq8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwErA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwErE">[</span>563<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwErI">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="55" id="mwErM" aria-labelledby="1960s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1960s">1960s</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=55" title="Edit section: 1960s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwErQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:0_series_Yurakucho_19670505.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwErU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:0_series_Yurakucho_19670505.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/0_series_Yurakucho_19670505.jpg/250px-0_series_Yurakucho_19670505.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/0_series_Yurakucho_19670505.jpg/500px-0_series_Yurakucho_19670505.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1020" data-file-height="628" data-file-type="bitmap" height="154" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwErY"/></a><figcaption id="mwErc">The original 0 series Shinkansen train. Introduced in 1964, it reached a speed of <span about="#mwt1617" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwErg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"convert","href":"./Template:Convert"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"210"},"2":{"wt":"km/h"},"abbr":{"wt":"on"}},"i":0}}]}'>210</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1617"> </span><span about="#mwt1617">km/h (130</span><span typeof="mw:Entity" about="#mwt1617"> </span><span about="#mwt1617">mph)</span>.</figcaption></figure>
<ul id="mwErk"><li id="mwEro"><b id="mwErs">1960:</b>  The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combined_oral_contraceptive_pill" title="Combined oral contraceptive pill" id="mwErw">combined oral contraceptive pill</a> becomes publicly available.<sup about="#mwt1620" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-571" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-571"}}'><a href="#cite_note-571" id="mwEr0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEr4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEr8">[</span>564<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEsA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1623" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-572" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-572"}}'><a href="#cite_note-572" id="mwEsE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEsI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEsM">[</span>565<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEsQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEsU"><b id="mwEsY">1960:</b> The first functioning <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser" title="Laser" id="mwEsc">laser</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_Maiman" title="Theodore Maiman" id="mwEsg">Theodore Maiman</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEsk"><b id="mwEso">1960:</b> First <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotic_exoskeleton" title="Robotic exoskeleton" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEss">robotic exoskeleton</a><sup about="#mwt1624" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwEsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEs0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEs4">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEs8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1629" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-574" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-574"}}'><a href="#cite_note-574" id="mwEtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEtE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEtI">[</span>567<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEtM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEtQ"><b id="mwEtU">1963:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_cigarette" title="Electronic cigarette" id="mwEtY">electronic cigarette</a> is created by Herbert A. Gilbert. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hon_Lik" title="Hon Lik" id="mwEtc">Hon Lik</a> is often credited with its invention as he developed the modern electronic cigarette and was the first to commercialize it.<sup about="#mwt1630" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwEtg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEtk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEto">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEts">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEtw"><b id="mwEt0">1964:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinkansen" title="Shinkansen" id="mwEt4">Shinkansen</a>, the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High-speed_rail" title="High-speed rail" id="mwEt8">high-speed rail</a> commercial passenger service.</li>
<li id="mwEuA"><b id="mwEuE">1965:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevlar" title="Kevlar" id="mwEuI">Kevlar</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephanie_Kwolek" title="Stephanie Kwolek" id="mwEuM">Stephanie Kwolek</a> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DuPont" title="DuPont" id="mwEuQ">DuPont</a>.</li>
<li id="mwEuU"><b id="mwEuY">1967:</b> E. A. Johnson of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Radar_Establishment" title="Royal Radar Establishment" id="mwEuc">Royal Radar Establishment</a> developed the capacitive touch display or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touchscreen" title="Touchscreen" id="mwEug">touchscreen</a><sup about="#mwt1631" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwEuk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEuo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEus">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEuw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1634" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-575" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-575"}}'><a href="#cite_note-575" id="mwEu0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEu4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEu8">[</span>568<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEvA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEvE"><b id="mwEvI">1969:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPL_network" title="NPL network" id="mwEvM">NPL network</a> followed by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ARPANET#ARPANET_deployed" title="ARPANET" id="mwEvQ">ARPANET</a> implement <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Packet_switching" title="Packet switching" id="mwEvU">packet switching</a> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_communication" title="Data communication" id="mwEvY">data communication</a>,<sup about="#mwt1637" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:22_576-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":22"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:22-576"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:22-576" id="mwEvc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEvk">[</span>569<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEvo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1640" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-577" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-577"}}'><a href="#cite_note-577" id="mwEvs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEvw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEv0">[</span>570<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEv4">]</span></span></a></sup> drawing on the concepts and designs of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Davies" title="Donald Davies" id="mwEv8">Donald Davies</a>,<sup about="#mwt1643" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Abbate20002_578-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Abbate20002"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Abbate20002-578"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Abbate20002-578" id="mwEwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEwE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEwI">[</span>571<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEwM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1646" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:2_579-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-579"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:2-579" id="mwEwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEwU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEwY">[</span>572<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEwc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1651" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-580" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-580"}}'><a href="#cite_note-580" id="mwEwg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEwk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEwo">[</span>573<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEws">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Baran" title="Paul Baran" id="mwEww">Paul Baran</a>.<sup about="#mwt1654" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:5_581-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":5"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:5-581"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:5-581" id="mwEw0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEw4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEw8">[</span>574<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwExA">]</span></span></a></sup> These are considered precursors to the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet" title="Internet" id="mwExE">Internet</a>.<sup about="#mwt1655" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Abbate20002_578-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Abbate20002"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Abbate20002-578" id="mwExI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwExM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwExQ">[</span>571<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwExU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1656" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:5_581-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:5-581" id="mwExY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwExc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwExg">[</span>574<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwExk">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="56" id="mwExo" aria-labelledby="1970s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1970s">1970s</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=56" title="Edit section: 1970s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwExs"><li id="mwExw"><b id="mwEx0">1970s:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public-key_cryptography" title="Public-key cryptography" id="mwEx4">Public-key cryptography</a> is invented and developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_H._Ellis" title="James H. Ellis" id="mwEx8">James H. Ellis</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clifford_Cocks" title="Clifford Cocks" id="mwEyA">Clifford Cocks</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malcolm_J._Williamson" title="Malcolm J. Williamson" id="mwEyE">Malcolm J. Williamson</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitfield_Diffie" title="Whitfield Diffie" id="mwEyI">Whitfield Diffie</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Hellman" title="Martin Hellman" id="mwEyM">Martin Hellman</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ralph_Merkle" title="Ralph Merkle" id="mwEyQ">Ralph Merkle</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_Rivest" title="Ron Rivest" id="mwEyU">Ron Rivest</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adi_Shamir" title="Adi Shamir" id="mwEyY">Adi Shamir</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonard_Adleman" title="Leonard Adleman" id="mwEyc">Leonard Adleman</a>, et al.</li>
<li id="mwEyg"><b id="mwEyk">1970:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calculator#Pocket_calculators" title="Calculator" id="mwEyo">pocket calculator</a> is invented.</li>
<li id="mwEys"><b id="mwEyw">1971:</b> The first single-chip <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microprocessor" title="Microprocessor" id="mwEy0">microprocessor</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intel_4004" title="Intel 4004" id="mwEy4">Intel 4004</a>, is invented. Its development was led by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federico_Faggin" title="Federico Faggin" id="mwEy8">Federico Faggin</a>, using his <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silicon-gate" title="Silicon-gate" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEzA">silicon-gate</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MOSFET" title="MOSFET" id="mwEzE">MOS</a> technology. This led to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Personal_computer" title="Personal computer" id="mwEzI">personal computer</a> (PC) revolution.<sup about="#mwt1659" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-582" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-582"}}'><a href="#cite_note-582" id="mwEzM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEzQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEzU">[</span>575<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEzY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwEzc"><b id="mwEzg">1971:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_station" title="Space station" id="mwEzk">space station</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salyut_1" title="Salyut 1" id="mwEzo">Salyut 1</a>, is launched.</li>
<li id="mwEzs"><b id="mwEzw">1971:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM" title="IBM" id="mwEz0">IBM</a> developed and released the world's first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floppy_disk" title="Floppy disk" id="mwEz4">floppy disk</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disk_drive" title="Disk drive" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEz8">disk drive</a>.<sup about="#mwt1662" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-computerhistory.org_583-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"computerhistory.org"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-computerhistory.org-583"}}'><a href="#cite_note-computerhistory.org-583" id="mwE0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE0E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE0I">[</span>576<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE0M">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE0Q"><b id="mwE0U">1972:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_game_console" title="Video game console" id="mwE0Y">video game console</a>, used primarily for playing video games on a TV, is the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnavox_Odyssey" title="Magnavox Odyssey" id="mwE0c">Magnavox Odyssey</a>.<sup about="#mwt1663" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HilbertLopez2011_584-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HilbertLopez2011"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HilbertLopez2011-584"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HilbertLopez2011-584" id="mwE0g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE0k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE0o">[</span>577<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE0s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE0w"><b id="mwE00">1972</b>: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbert_Boyer" title="Herbert Boyer" id="mwE04">Herbert Boyer</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanley_Cohen_(biochemist)" title="Stanley Cohen (biochemist)" id="mwE08">Stanley Cohen</a> developed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genetic_modification" title="Genetic modification" class="mw-redirect" id="mwE1A">genetic modification</a> when they successfully modified <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA" title="DNA" id="mwE1E">DNA</a><sup about="#mwt1664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:6_415-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:6-415" id="mwE1I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE1M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE1Q">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE1U">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE1Y"><b id="mwE1c">1973:</b> The first fiber optic communication systems were developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optelecom" title="Optelecom" id="mwE1g">Optelecom</a>.<sup about="#mwt1665" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-585" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-585"}}'><a href="#cite_note-585" id="mwE1k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE1o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE1s">[</span>578<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE1w">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE10"><b id="mwE14">1973:</b> The first commercial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphical_user_interface" title="Graphical user interface" id="mwE18">graphical user interface</a> is introduced in 1973 on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xerox_Alto" title="Xerox Alto" id="mwE2A">Xerox Alto</a>. The modern GUI is later popularized by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xerox_Star" title="Xerox Star" id="mwE2E">Xerox Star</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Lisa" title="Apple Lisa" id="mwE2I">Apple Lisa</a>.</li>
<li id="mwE2M"><b id="mwE2Q">1973:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touchscreen#Capacitive" title="Touchscreen" id="mwE2U">capacitive touchscreen</a> is developed at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CERN" title="CERN" id="mwE2Y">CERN</a>.</li>
<li id="mwE2c"><b id="mwE2g">1974:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transmission_Control_Program" title="Transmission Control Program" class="mw-redirect" id="mwE2k">Transmission Control Program</a> is proposed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinton_Cerf" title="Vinton Cerf" class="mw-redirect" id="mwE2o">Vinton Cerf</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_E._Kahn" title="Robert E. Kahn" class="mw-redirect" id="mwE2s">Robert E. Kahn</a>, building on the work of other <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_pioneer" title="Internet pioneer" class="mw-redirect" id="mwE2w">Internet pioneers</a>, creating the basis for the modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet" title="Internet" id="mwE20">Internet</a>.<sup about="#mwt1668" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-586" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-586"}}'><a href="#cite_note-586" id="mwE24"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE28"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE3A">[</span>579<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE3E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1671" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:7_587-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":7"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:7-587"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:7-587" id="mwE3I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE3M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE3Q">[</span>580<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE3U">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE3Y"><b id="mwE3c">1974:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithium-ion_battery" title="Lithium-ion battery" id="mwE3g">lithium-ion battery</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M._Stanley_Whittingham" title="M. Stanley Whittingham" id="mwE3k">M. Stanley Whittingham</a>, and further developed in the 1980s and 1990s by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_B._Goodenough" title="John B. Goodenough" id="mwE3o">John B. Goodenough</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rachid_Yazami" title="Rachid Yazami" id="mwE3s">Rachid Yazami</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akira_Yoshino" title="Akira Yoshino" id="mwE3w">Akira Yoshino</a>. It has impacted modern <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consumer_electronics" title="Consumer electronics" id="mwE30">consumer electronics</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electric_vehicle" title="Electric vehicle" id="mwE34">electric vehicles</a>.<sup about="#mwt1674" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-588" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-588"}}'><a href="#cite_note-588" id="mwE38"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE4E">[</span>581<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE4I">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE4M"><b id="mwE4Q">1974:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubik's_Cube" title="Rubik's Cube" id="mwE4U">Rubik's cube</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ernő_Rubik" title="Ernő Rubik" id="mwE4Y">Ernő Rubik</a> which went on to be the best selling <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puzzle" title="Puzzle" id="mwE4c">puzzle</a> ever.<sup about="#mwt1677" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-castel_589-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"castel"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-castel-589"}}'><a href="#cite_note-castel-589" id="mwE4g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE4k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE4o">[</span>582<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE4s">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE4w"><b id="mwE40">1975:</b> First general purpose <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home_automation" title="Home automation" id="mwE44">home automation</a> network technology, X10, was developed<sup about="#mwt1680" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-590" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-590"}}'><a href="#cite_note-590" id="mwE48"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE5A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE5E">[</span>583<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE5I">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE5M"><b id="mwE5Q">1977:</b> Dr Walter Gilbert and Frederick Sanger invented a new <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA_sequencing" title="DNA sequencing" id="mwE5U">DNA sequencing</a> method for which they won the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobel_Prize" title="Nobel Prize" id="mwE5Y">Nobel Prize</a>.<sup about="#mwt1683" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-591" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-591"}}'><a href="#cite_note-591" id="mwE5c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE5g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE5k">[</span>584<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE5o">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE5s"><b id="mwE5w">1977:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-driving_car" title="Self-driving car" id="mwE50">self-driving car</a> that did not rely upon rails or wires under the road is designed by the Tsukuba Mechanical Engineering Laboratory.<sup about="#mwt1686" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-592" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-592"}}'><a href="#cite_note-592" id="mwE54"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE58"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE6A">[</span>585<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE6E">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE6I"><b id="mwE6M">1978:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Positioning_System" title="Global Positioning System" id="mwE6Q">Global Positioning System</a> (GPS) enters service. While not the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satellite_navigation" title="Satellite navigation" id="mwE6U">Satellite navigation</a> system, it is the first to enter widespread civilian use</li>
<li id="mwE6Y">1<b id="mwE6c">978:</b> Birth of the first child through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_vitro_fertilisation" title="In vitro fertilisation" id="mwE6g">in vitro fertilization</a> (IVF), based on the research of  <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Steptoe" title="Patrick Steptoe" id="mwE6k">Patrick Steptoe</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Edwards_(physiologist)" title="Robert Edwards (physiologist)" id="mwE6o">Robert Edwards</a><sup about="#mwt1689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-593" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-593"}}'><a href="#cite_note-593" id="mwE6s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE60">[</span>586<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE64">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE68"><b id="mwE7A">1979:</b> The first handheld game console with interchangeable game cartridges, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microvision" title="Microvision" id="mwE7E">Microvision</a> is released.</li>
<li id="mwE7I"><b id="mwE7M">1979:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nippon_Telegraph_and_Telephone" title="Nippon Telegraph and Telephone" id="mwE7Q">Nippon Telegraph and Telephone</a> (NTT) launched the first cellular network in Japan.<sup about="#mwt1690" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-594" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-594"}}'><a href="#cite_note-594" id="mwE7U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE7Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE7c">[</span>587<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE7g">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE7k"><b id="mwE7o">1979:</b> Public dialup information, messaging and e-commerce services, were pioneered through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CompuServe" title="CompuServe" id="mwE7s">CompuServe</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RadioShack" title="RadioShack" id="mwE7w">RadioShack</a>'s MicroNET, and the UK's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post_Office_Telecommunications" title="Post Office Telecommunications" class="mw-redirect" id="mwE70">Post Office Telecommunications</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prestel" title="Prestel" id="mwE74">Prestel</a> services.<sup about="#mwt1693" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-595" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-595"}}'><a href="#cite_note-595" id="mwE78"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE8A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE8E">[</span>588<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE8I">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1696" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-596" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-596"}}'><a href="#cite_note-596" id="mwE8M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE8U">[</span>589<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE8Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="57" id="mwE8c" aria-labelledby="1980s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1980s">1980s</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=57" title="Edit section: 1980s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwE8g"><li id="mwE8k"><b id="mwE8o">1980:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flash_memory" title="Flash memory" id="mwE8s">Flash memory</a> (both NOR and NAND types) was invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujio_Masuoka" title="Fujio Masuoka" id="mwE8w">Fujio Masuoka</a> while working for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toshiba" title="Toshiba" id="mwE80">Toshiba</a>. It was introduced to the public in 1984.</li>
<li id="mwE84"><b id="mwE88">1980:</b> Scientists <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Skolnick" title="Mark Skolnick" id="mwE9A">Mark Skolnick</a>, Ron Davis, Ray White, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Botstein" title="David Botstein" id="mwE9E">David Botstein</a> published their findings on a gene mapping tool using <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Restriction_fragment_length_polymorphism" title="Restriction fragment length polymorphism" id="mwE9I">Restriction Fragment-length Polymorphisms</a> (RFLP), that would have applications to identify heritable disorders, including some forms of cancer.<sup about="#mwt1699" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-597" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-597"}}'><a href="#cite_note-597" id="mwE9M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE9Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE9U">[</span>590<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE9Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1702" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-598" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-598"}}'><a href="#cite_note-598" id="mwE9c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE9g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE9k">[</span>591<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE9o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1703" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-599" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-599"}}'><a href="#cite_note-599" id="mwE9s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE9w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE90">[</span>592<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE94">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE98"><b id="mwE-A">1981:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reusable_spacecraft" title="Reusable spacecraft" id="mwE-E">reusable spacecraft</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle" title="Space Shuttle" id="mwE-I">Space Shuttle</a> undergoes test flights ahead of full operation in 1982<sup about="#mwt1706" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-600" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-600"}}'><a href="#cite_note-600" id="mwE-M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE-Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE-U">[</span>593<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE-Y">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE-c"><b id="mwE-g">1981:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kane_Kramer" title="Kane Kramer" id="mwE-k">Kane Kramer</a> develops the credit card-sized, IXI <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portable_media_player" title="Portable media player" id="mwE-o">digital media player</a>.<sup about="#mwt1709" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-601" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-601"}}'><a href="#cite_note-601" id="mwE-s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE-w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE-0">[</span>594<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE-4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE-8"><b id="mwE_A">1981:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Televerket_(Sweden)" title="Televerket (Sweden)" id="mwE_E">Televerket</a>, a Swedish state-owned corporation, launched the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nordic_Mobile_Telephone" title="Nordic Mobile Telephone" id="mwE_I">Nordic Mobile Telephone</a> (NMT) system.<sup about="#mwt1712" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-602" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-602"}}'><a href="#cite_note-602" id="mwE_M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE_Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE_U">[</span>595<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE_Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1713" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-603" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-603"}}'><a href="#cite_note-603" id="mwE_c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE_g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE_k">[</span>596<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE_o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1716" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-604" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-604"}}'><a href="#cite_note-604" id="mwE_s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwE_w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE_0">[</span>597<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwE_4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwE_8"><b id="mwFAA">1981:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comviq" title="Comviq" id="mwFAE">Comvik</a>, a Swedish telecommunications company, launched the first commercial automatic cellular system. However, according to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swedish_Post_and_Telecom_Authority" title="Swedish Post and Telecom Authority" id="mwFAI">Swedish Post and Telecom Authority</a>, the company launched an unlicensed automatic system. Comvik didn't receive a license to operate until December 1981, two months after the NMT system was launched.<sup about="#mwt1717" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-605" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-605"}}'><a href="#cite_note-605" id="mwFAM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFAQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFAU">[</span>598<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFAY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1720" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-606" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-606"}}'><a href="#cite_note-606" id="mwFAc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFAg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFAk">[</span>599<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFAo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFAs"><b id="mwFAw">1982:</b> A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CD-ROM" title="CD-ROM" id="mwFA0">CD-ROM</a> contains <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_data_storage" title="Computer data storage" id="mwFA4">data</a> accessible to, but not writable by, a computer for data storage and music playback. The 1985 <i id="mwFA8">Yellow Book</i> standard developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sony" title="Sony" id="mwFBA">Sony</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philips" title="Philips" id="mwFBE">Philips</a> adapted the format to hold any form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binary_file" title="Binary file" id="mwFBI">binary data</a>.<sup about="#mwt1723" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EP689208_607-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EP689208"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-EP689208-607"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EP689208-607" id="mwFBM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFBQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFBU">[</span>600<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFBY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFBc"><b id="mwFBg">1982:</b> Direct to home <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satellite_television" title="Satellite television" id="mwFBk">satellite television</a> transmission, with the launch of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_One" title="Sky One" id="mwFBo">Sky One</a> service.<sup about="#mwt1726" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-608" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-608"}}'><a href="#cite_note-608" id="mwFBs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFBw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFB0">[</span>601<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFB4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFB8"><b id="mwFCA">1982:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laptop" title="Laptop" id="mwFCE">laptop</a> computer is launched, the 8/16-bit <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epson_HX-20" title="Epson HX-20" id="mwFCI">Epson HX-20</a>.<sup about="#mwt1729" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ipsj_609-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ipsj"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ipsj-609"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ipsj-609" id="mwFCM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFCQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFCU">[</span>602<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFCY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFCc"><b id="mwFCg">1983:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stereolithography" title="Stereolithography" id="mwFCk">Stereolithography</a> is invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chuck_Hull" title="Chuck Hull" id="mwFCo">Chuck Hull</a>.<sup about="#mwt1732" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-610" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-610"}}'><a href="#cite_note-610" id="mwFCs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFCw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFC0">[</span>603<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFC4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFC8"><b id="mwFDA">1983:</b> Ameritech, now known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AT&amp;T" title="AT&amp;T" id="mwFDE">AT&amp;T</a>, commercialized the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_System" title="Bell System" id="mwFDI">Bell System</a> (its cellular network) in Chicago, Ill.<sup about="#mwt1735" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-611" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-611"}}'><a href="#cite_note-611" id="mwFDM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFDQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFDU">[</span>604<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFDY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1738" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-612" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-612"}}'><a href="#cite_note-612" id="mwFDc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFDg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFDk">[</span>605<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFDo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFDs"><b id="mwFDw">1984:</b> The first commercially available <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cell_phone" title="Cell phone" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFD0">cell phone</a> in the US, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motorola_DynaTAC" title="Motorola DynaTAC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFD4">DynaTAC</a> 8000X, is created by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motorola" title="Motorola" id="mwFD8">Motorola</a>.</li>
<li id="mwFEA"><b id="mwFEE">1984:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chuck_Hull" title="Chuck Hull" id="mwFEI">Chuck Hull</a> patents the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stereolithography" title="Stereolithography" id="mwFEM">stereolithography</a> (SLA) process, also known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3D_printing" title="3D printing" id="mwFEQ">3D printing</a><sup about="#mwt1741" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:8-573"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFEU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFEY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFEc">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFEg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1744" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:10-613"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFEk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFEo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFEs">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFEw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFE0"><b id="mwFE4">1984:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA_profiling" title="DNA profiling" id="mwFE8">DNA profiling</a> is pioneered by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alec_Jeffreys" title="Alec Jeffreys" id="mwFFA">Alec Jeffreys</a>.<sup about="#mwt1747" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-614" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-614"}}'><a href="#cite_note-614" id="mwFFE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFFI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFFM">[</span>607<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFFQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1750" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-615" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-615"}}'><a href="#cite_note-615" id="mwFFU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFFY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFFc">[</span>608<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFFg">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFFk"><b id="mwFFo">1986:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Technophone" title="Technophone" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFFs">Technophone</a>, a British mobile phone company, created the first pocket-sized cell phone, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excel_mobile_phones" title="Excel mobile phones" id="mwFFw">Excell PCT105</a>.<sup about="#mwt1751" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-616" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-616"}}'><a href="#cite_note-616" id="mwFF0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFF4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFF8">[</span>609<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFGA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1754" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-617" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-617"}}'><a href="#cite_note-617" id="mwFGE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFGI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFGM">[</span>610<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFGQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFGU"><b id="mwFGY">1989:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karlheinz_Brandenburg" title="Karlheinz Brandenburg" id="mwFGc">Karlheinz Brandenburg</a> would publish the audio compression algorithms that would be standardised as the: MPEG-1, layer 3 (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MP3" title="MP3" id="mwFGg">mp3</a>), and later the MPEG-2, layer 7 Advanced Audio Compression (AAC).<sup about="#mwt1757" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-618" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-618"}}'><a href="#cite_note-618" id="mwFGk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFGo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFGs">[</span>611<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFGw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFG0"><b id="mwFG4">1989:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wide_Web" title="World Wide Web" id="mwFG8">World Wide Web</a> is invented by computer scientist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Berners-Lee" title="Tim Berners-Lee" id="mwFHA">Tim Berners-Lee</a>.<sup about="#mwt1760" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AHT_619-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AHT"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AHT-619"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AHT-619" id="mwFHE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFHI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFHM">[</span>612<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFHQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1763" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-620" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-620"}}'><a href="#cite_note-620" id="mwFHU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFHY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFHc">[</span>613<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFHg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="58" id="mwFHk" aria-labelledby="1990s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1990s">1990s</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=58" title="Edit section: 1990s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwFHo"><li id="mwFHs"><b id="mwFHw">1990:</b> The first search engine, "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archie_(search_engine)" title="Archie (search engine)" id="mwFH0">Archie</a>", was created by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Emtage" title="Alan Emtage" id="mwFH4">Alan Emtage</a>, Bill Heelan, and Peter J. Deutsch at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McGill_University" title="McGill University" id="mwFH8">McGill University</a><sup about="#mwt1766" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-621" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-621"}}'><a href="#cite_note-621" id="mwFIA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFIE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFII">[</span>614<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFIM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1769" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-622" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-622"}}'><a href="#cite_note-622" id="mwFIQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFIU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFIY">[</span>615<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFIc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1772" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-623" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-623"}}'><a href="#cite_note-623" id="mwFIg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFIk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFIo">[</span>616<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFIs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFIw"><b id="mwFI0">1991:</b> The first commercial flash-based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solid-state_drive" title="Solid-state drive" id="mwFI4">solid-state drive</a> is launched by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SanDisk" title="SanDisk" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFI8">SunDisk</a>.<sup about="#mwt1775" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-624" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-624"}}'><a href="#cite_note-624" id="mwFJA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFJE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFJI">[</span>617<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFJM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFJQ"><b id="mwFJU">1991:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sim_card" title="Sim card" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFJY">sim card</a> is developed by Munich smart-card maker Giesecke &amp; Devrient<sup about="#mwt1778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-625" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-625"}}'><a href="#cite_note-625" id="mwFJc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFJg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFJk">[</span>618<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFJo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1781" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-626" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-626"}}'><a href="#cite_note-626" id="mwFJs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFJw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFJ0">[</span>619<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFJ4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFJ8"><b id="mwFKA">1994:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM_Simon" title="IBM Simon" id="mwFKE">IBM Simon</a>, the world's first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smartphone" title="Smartphone" id="mwFKI">smartphone</a>, is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM" title="IBM" id="mwFKM">IBM</a>. It had a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touchscreen" title="Touchscreen" id="mwFKQ">touchscreen</a> and the first built-in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_software" title="Application software" id="mwFKU">apps</a> for a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile_device" title="Mobile device" id="mwFKY">mobile device</a>.<sup about="#mwt1784" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-627" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-627"}}'><a href="#cite_note-627" id="mwFKc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFKg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFKk">[</span>620<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFKo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1787" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-628" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-628"}}'><a href="#cite_note-628" id="mwFKs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFKw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFK0">[</span>621<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFK4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFK8"><b id="mwFLA">1994:</b> First generation of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluetooth" title="Bluetooth" id="mwFLE">Bluetooth</a> is developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ericsson_Mobile" title="Ericsson Mobile" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFLI">Ericsson Mobile</a>. A form of data communication on short distances between electronic devices<sup about="#mwt1790" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-629" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-629"}}'><a href="#cite_note-629" id="mwFLM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFLU">[</span>622<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFLY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1793" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-630" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-630"}}'><a href="#cite_note-630" id="mwFLc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFLg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFLk">[</span>623<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFLo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFLs"><b id="mwFLw">1994:</b> A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tetris" title="Tetris" id="mwFL0">Tetris</a> variant on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hagenuk_MT-2000" title="Hagenuk MT-2000" id="mwFL4">Hagenuk MT-2000</a> device becomes the first mobile game<sup about="#mwt1796" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-631" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-631"}}'><a href="#cite_note-631" id="mwFL8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFMA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFME">[</span>624<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFMI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1799" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-632" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-632"}}'><a href="#cite_note-632" id="mwFMM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFMQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFMU">[</span>625<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFMY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFMc"><b id="mwFMg">1995:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DVD" title="DVD" id="mwFMk">DVD</a> is an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optical_disc" title="Optical disc" id="mwFMo">optical disc</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_storage_device" title="Data storage device" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFMs">storage</a> format, invented and developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philips" title="Philips" id="mwFMw">Philips</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sony" title="Sony" id="mwFM0">Sony</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toshiba" title="Toshiba" id="mwFM4">Toshiba</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panasonic" title="Panasonic" id="mwFM8">Panasonic</a>. DVDs offer higher storage capacity than <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compact_disc" title="Compact disc" id="mwFNA">compact discs</a> while having the same dimensions.<sup about="#mwt1802" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-633" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-633"}}'><a href="#cite_note-633" id="mwFNE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFNI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFNM">[</span>626<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFNQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1805" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-634" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-634"}}'><a href="#cite_note-634" id="mwFNU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFNY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFNc">[</span>627<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFNg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1808" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-635" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-635"}}'><a href="#cite_note-635" id="mwFNk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFNo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFNs">[</span>628<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFNw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFN0"><b id="mwFN4">1996:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ciena" title="Ciena" id="mwFN8">Ciena Corporation</a>, in partnership with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sprint_Corporation" title="Sprint Corporation" id="mwFOA">Sprint</a>, deployed the first commercial dense <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wavelength-division_multiplexing" title="Wavelength-division multiplexing" id="mwFOE">wavelength-division multiplexing system</a>, which created the massive capacity of the Internet.<sup about="#mwt1811" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-636" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-636"}}'><a href="#cite_note-636" id="mwFOI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFOM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFOQ">[</span>629<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFOU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1814" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-637" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-637"}}'><a href="#cite_note-637" id="mwFOY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFOc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFOg">[</span>630<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFOk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1817" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-638" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-638"}}'><a href="#cite_note-638" id="mwFOo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFOs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFOw">[</span>631<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFO0">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFO4"><b id="mwFO8">1996:</b> Mobile web was first commercially offered in Finland on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nokia_9000_Communicator" title="Nokia 9000 Communicator" id="mwFPA">Nokia 9000 Communicator</a> phone, and it was also the first phone with texting<sup about="#mwt1820" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-639" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-639"}}'><a href="#cite_note-639" id="mwFPE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFPI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFPM">[</span>632<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFPQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFPU"><b id="mwFPY">1996:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolt_(website)" title="Bolt (website)" id="mwFPc">Bolt</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SixDegrees.com" title="SixDegrees.com" id="mwFPg">Six Degrees</a> (1997) both become the first social media sites.<sup about="#mwt1823" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:9_640-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":9"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:9-640"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:9-640" id="mwFPk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFPo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFPs">[</span>633<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFPw">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFP0"><b id="mwFP4">1996:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myriad_Genetics" title="Myriad Genetics" id="mwFP8">Myriad Genetics</a> released the BRACAnalysis, the first commercial genetic test for assessing the risk of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer.<sup about="#mwt1824" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-641" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-641"}}'><a href="#cite_note-641" id="mwFQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQI">[</span>634<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1827" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-642" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-642"}}'><a href="#cite_note-642" id="mwFQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFQU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQY">[</span>635<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQc">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFQg"><b id="mwFQk">1999:</b>  The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capsule_endoscopy" title="Capsule endoscopy" id="mwFQo">capsule endoscopy</a> was performed, after being invented in the mid-1990s by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gavriel_Iddan" title="Gavriel Iddan" id="mwFQs">Gavriel Iddan</a><sup about="#mwt1828" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFQw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFQ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ4">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1829" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFRA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFRE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFRI">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFRM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFRQ"><b id="mwFRU">1999:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_video_recorder" title="Digital video recorder" id="mwFRY">digital video recorder</a> (DVR), the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TiVo" title="TiVo" id="mwFRc">TiVo</a>, is launched<sup about="#mwt1832" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-643" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-643"}}'><a href="#cite_note-643" id="mwFRg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFRk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFRo">[</span>636<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFRs">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFRw"><b id="mwFR0">1999:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NTT_Docomo" title="NTT Docomo" id="mwFR4">NTT DoCoMo</a> launches <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I-mode" title="I-mode" id="mwFR8">i-mode</a>, the first integrated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/App_store" title="App store" id="mwFSA">Online App store</a> for mobile phones<sup about="#mwt1833" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-644" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-644"}}'><a href="#cite_note-644" id="mwFSE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFSI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFSM">[</span>637<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFSQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="59" id="mwFSU" aria-labelledby="21st_century"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="21st_century">21st century</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=59" title="Edit section: 21st century"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="60" id="mwFSY" aria-labelledby="2000s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="2000s">2000s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=60" title="Edit section: 2000s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwFSc"><li id="mwFSg"><b id="mwFSk">2001:</b> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_and_Drug_Administration" title="Food and Drug Administration" id="mwFSo">Food and Drug Administration</a> approved the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contraceptive_patch" title="Contraceptive patch" id="mwFSs">contraceptive patch</a><sup about="#mwt1834" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFSw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFS0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFS4">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFS8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1835" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFTE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFTI">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFTM">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFTQ"><b id="mwFTU">2001:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia" title="Wikipedia" id="mwFTY">Wikipedia</a> is launched by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Wales" title="Jimmy Wales" id="mwFTc">Jimmy Wales</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Sanger" title="Larry Sanger" id="mwFTg">Larry Sanger</a> as a open-content online <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encyclopedia" title="Encyclopedia" id="mwFTk">encyclopedia</a><sup about="#mwt1839" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-645" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-645"}}'><a href="#cite_note-645" id="mwFTo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFTs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFTw">[</span>638<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFT0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1842" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-646" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-646"}}'><a href="#cite_note-646" id="mwFT4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFT8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFUA">[</span>639<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFUE">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFUI"><b id="mwFUM">2002:</b> Programmer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Abrams_(businessman)" title="Jonathan Abrams (businessman)" id="mwFUQ">Jonathon Abrams</a> launches <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friendster" title="Friendster" id="mwFUU">Friendster</a>, establishing the modern template for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web-based" title="Web-based" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFUY">web-based</a> social networking<sup about="#mwt1845" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-647" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-647"}}'><a href="#cite_note-647" id="mwFUc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFUk">[</span>640<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFUo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1848" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-648" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-648"}}'><a href="#cite_note-648" id="mwFUs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFUw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFU0">[</span>641<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFU4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFU8"><b id="mwFVA">2003:</b> Development of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Android_(operating_system)" title="Android (operating system)" id="mwFVE">Android operating system</a> for mobile devices<sup about="#mwt1849" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFVI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFVM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFVQ">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFVU">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFVY"><b id="mwFVc">2004:</b> First <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Podcast" title="Podcast" id="mwFVg">podcast</a>, invented by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Curry" title="Adam Curry" id="mwFVk">Adam Curry</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dave_Winer" title="Dave Winer" id="mwFVo">Dave Winer</a><sup about="#mwt1852" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-649" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-649"}}'><a href="#cite_note-649" id="mwFVs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFVw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFV0">[</span>642<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFV4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1855" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-650" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-650"}}'><a href="#cite_note-650" id="mwFV8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFWA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFWE">[</span>643<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFWI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1858" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-651" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-651"}}'><a href="#cite_note-651" id="mwFWM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFWQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFWU">[</span>644<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFWY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFWc"><b id="mwFWg">2005:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube" title="YouTube" id="mwFWk">YouTube</a>, the first popular video-streaming site, was founded by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jawed_Karim" title="Jawed Karim" id="mwFWo">Jawed Karim</a><sup about="#mwt1859" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:9_640-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:9-640" id="mwFWs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFW0">[</span>633<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFW4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFW8"><b id="mwFXA">2006:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)" title="Amazon (company)" id="mwFXE">Amazon</a> pioneered <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud_computing" title="Cloud computing" id="mwFXI">cloud computing</a><sup about="#mwt1860" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFXM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFXQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFXU">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFXY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFXc"><b id="mwFXg">2007:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Inc." title="Apple Inc." id="mwFXk">Apple Inc.</a> released the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPhone" title="IPhone" id="mwFXo">iPhone</a><sup about="#mwt1861" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:9_640-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:9-640" id="mwFXs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFX0">[</span>633<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFX4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFX8"><b id="mwFYA">2007:</b> First <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Kindle" title="Amazon Kindle" id="mwFYE">Kindle</a> e-reader introduced by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)" title="Amazon (company)" id="mwFYI">Amazon</a><sup about="#mwt1863" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-652" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-652"}}'><a href="#cite_note-652" id="mwFYM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFYQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFYU">[</span>645<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFYY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1864" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFYk">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFYo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFYs"><b id="mwFYw">2009:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Satoshi_Nakamoto" title="Satoshi Nakamoto" id="mwFY0">Satoshi Nakamoto</a> develops the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockchain" title="Blockchain" id="mwFY4">blockchain</a>.<sup about="#mwt1865" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:9_640-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:9-640" id="mwFY8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFZE">[</span>633<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFZI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1866" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFZM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFZU">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFZY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1867" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFZc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFZk">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFZo">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFZs"><b id="mwFZw">2009:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_machine" title="Quantum machine" id="mwFZ0">quantum machine</a> was created by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_D._O'Connell" title="Aaron D. O'Connell" id="mwFZ4">Aaron D. O'Connell</a><sup about="#mwt1870" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-653" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-653"}}'><a href="#cite_note-653" id="mwFZ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFaA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFaE">[</span>646<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFaI">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="61" id="mwFaM" aria-labelledby="2010s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="2010s">2010s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=61" title="Edit section: 2010s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwFaQ"><li id="mwFaU"><b id="mwFaY">2010:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthetic_biology" title="Synthetic biology" id="mwFac">synthetic organism</a>, <i id="mwFag"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mycoplasma_laboratorium" title="Mycoplasma laboratorium" id="mwFak">Mycoplasma laboratorium</a></i> is created by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._Craig_Venter_Institute" title="J. Craig Venter Institute" id="mwFao">J. Craig Venter Institute</a><sup about="#mwt1873" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-654" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-654"}}'><a href="#cite_note-654" id="mwFas"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFaw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFa0">[</span>647<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFa4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1876" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-655" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-655"}}'><a href="#cite_note-655" id="mwFa8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFbA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFbE">[</span>648<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFbI">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFbM"><b id="mwFbQ">2010:</b>  Solid-state <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lidar" title="Lidar" id="mwFbU">Lidar</a> technology was introduced, replacing mechanical scanning with electronic beam steering<sup about="#mwt1877" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFbY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFbc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFbg">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFbk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFbo"><b id="mwFbs">2014:</b> The first known "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NFT" title="NFT" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFbw">NFT</a>", <i id="mwFb0">Quantum</i>,<sup about="#mwt1880" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-656" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-656"}}'><a href="#cite_note-656" id="mwFb4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFb8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFcA">[</span>649<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFcE">]</span></span></a></sup> was created by Kevin McCoy and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anil_Dash" title="Anil Dash" id="mwFcI">Anil Dash</a> in May.<sup about="#mwt1883" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-657" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-657"}}'><a href="#cite_note-657" id="mwFcM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFcQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFcU">[</span>650<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFcY">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFcc"><b id="mwFcg">2014:</b> Introduction of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepper_(robot)" title="Pepper (robot)" id="mwFck">Pepper</a>, the first commercial  <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humanoid_robot" title="Humanoid robot" id="mwFco">humanoid robot</a><sup about="#mwt1884" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFcs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFcw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFc0">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFc4">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFc8"><b id="mwFdA">2015:</b>  Discovery of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CRISPR_gene_editing" title="CRISPR gene editing" id="mwFdE">CRISPR gene editing</a> method<sup about="#mwt1887" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-658" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-658"}}'><a href="#cite_note-658" id="mwFdI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFdM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFdQ">[</span>651<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFdU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1888" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFdY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFdc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFdg">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFdk">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFdo"><b id="mwFds">2016:</b> First commercially available <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_pancreas" title="Artificial pancreas" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFdw">artificial pancreas</a><sup about="#mwt1889" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFd0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFd4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFd8">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFeA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1890" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFeE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFeI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFeM">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFeQ">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFeU"><b id="mwFeY">2016</b>: First successful launch of a multi-use rocket by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SpaceX" title="SpaceX" id="mwFec">SpaceX</a><sup about="#mwt1891" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:8_573-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:8-573" id="mwFeg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFek"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFeo">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFes">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFew"><b id="mwFe0">2019:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM" title="IBM" id="mwFe4">IBM</a> launches <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM_Q_System_One" title="IBM Q System One" id="mwFe8">IBM Q System One</a>, its first integrated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantum_computing" title="Quantum computing" id="mwFfA">quantum computing</a> system for commercial use.<sup about="#mwt1892" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:10_613-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:10-613" id="mwFfE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFfI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFfM">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFfQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1893" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:9_640-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:9-640" id="mwFfU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFfY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFfc">[</span>633<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFfg">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="62" id="mwFfk" aria-labelledby="2020s"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="2020s">2020s</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=62" title="Edit section: 2020s"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwFfo"><li id="mwFfs"><b id="mwFfw">2020:</b> The first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MRNA_vaccine" title="MRNA vaccine" id="mwFf0">mRNA vaccine</a> to be approved by public health medicines regulators is co-developed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pfizer" title="Pfizer" id="mwFf4">Pfizer</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BioNTech" title="BioNTech" id="mwFf8">BioNTech</a> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19" title="COVID-19" id="mwFgA">COVID-19</a>, with the potential to treat other diseases and cancer<sup about="#mwt1896" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-659" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-659"}}'><a href="#cite_note-659" id="mwFgE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFgI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFgM">[</span>652<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFgQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1899" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-660" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-660"}}'><a href="#cite_note-660" id="mwFgU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFgY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFgc">[</span>653<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFgg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1902" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-661" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-661"}}'><a href="#cite_note-661" id="mwFgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFgs">[</span>654<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFgw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1905" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-662" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-662"}}'><a href="#cite_note-662" id="mwFg0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFg4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg8">[</span>655<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFhA">]</span></span></a></sup></li>
<li id="mwFhE"><b id="mwFhI">2022:</b> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI" title="OpenAI" id="mwFhM">OpenAI</a> demonstrated an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence" title="Artificial intelligence" id="mwFhQ">Artificial Intelligence</a> model called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GPT-3" title="GPT-3" id="mwFhU">GPT-3</a>. The program was created to generate human-like responses when given prompts.<sup about="#mwt1908" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-663" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-663"}}'><a href="#cite_note-663" id="mwFhY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFhc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFhg">[</span>656<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFhk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1911" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-664" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-664"}}'><a href="#cite_note-664" id="mwFho"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFhs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFhw">[</span>657<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFh0">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="63" id="mwFh4" aria-labelledby="See_also"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="See_also">See also</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Timeline_of_historic_inventions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=63" title="Edit section: See also"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwFh8"><li id="mwFiA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accelerating_change" title="Accelerating change" id="mwFiE">Accelerating change</a></li>
<li id="mwFiI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_emerging_technologies" title="List of emerging technologies" id="mwFiM">List of emerging technologies</a></li>
<li id="mwFiQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_inventors" title="List of inventors" id="mwFiU">List of inventors</a></li>
<li id="mwFiY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_years_in_science" title="List of years in science" id="mwFic">List of years in science</a></li>
<li id="mwFig"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_prehistoric_technology" title="Outline of prehistoric technology" id="mwFik">Outline of prehistoric technology</a></li>
<li id="mwFio"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_prehistory" title="Timeline of prehistory" id="mwFis">Timeline of prehistory</a></li></ul>

<dl id="mwFiw"><dt id="mwFi0">By type</dt></dl>
