identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGcg">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2018Sci...359..912H" class="external text" id="mwGck">2018Sci...359..912H</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGco">doi</a>:<span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwGcs"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1126%2Fscience.aap7778" class="external text" id="mwGcw">10.1126/science.aap7778</a></span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hdl_(identifier)" title="Hdl (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGc0">hdl</a>:<span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwGc4"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://hdl.handle.net/10498%2F21578" class="external text" id="mwGc8">10498/21578</a></span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)" title="PMID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGdA">PMID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwGdE"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29472483" class="external text" id="mwGdI">29472483</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Science&amp;rft.atitle=U-Th+dating+of+carbonate+crusts+reveals+Neandertal+origin+of+Iberian+cave+art&amp;rft.volume=359&amp;rft.issue=6378&amp;rft.pages=912-915&amp;rft.date=2018&amp;rft_id=info%3Ahdl%2F10498%2F21578&amp;rft_id=info%3Apmid%2F29472483&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1126%2Fscience.aap7778&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F2018Sci...359..912H&amp;rft.au=D.+L.+Hoffmann&amp;rft.au=C.+D.+Standish&amp;rft.au=M.+Garc%C3%ADa-Diez&amp;rft.au=P.+B.+Pettitt&amp;rft.au=J.+A.+Milton&amp;rft.au=J.+Zilh%C3%A3o&amp;rft.au=J.+J.+Alcolea-Gonz%C3%A1lez&amp;rft.au=P.+Cantalejo-Duarte&amp;rft.au=H.+Collado&amp;rft.au=R.+de+Balb%C3%ADn&amp;rft.au=M.+Lorblanchet&amp;rft.au=J.+Ramos-Mu%C3%B1oz&amp;rft.au=G.-Ch.+Weniger&amp;rft.au=A.+W.+G.+Pike&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdoi.org%2F10.1126%252Fscience.aap7778&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt176" id="mwGdM"></span> 
"we present dating results for three sites in Spain that show that cave art emerged in Iberia substantially earlier than previously thought. Uranium-thorium (U-Th) dates on carbonate crusts overlying paintings provide minimum
ages for a red linear motif in La Pasiega (Cantabria), a hand stencil in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_of_Maltravieso" title="Cave of Maltravieso" id="mwGdQ">Maltravieso (Extremadura)</a>, and red-painted speleothems in Ardales (Andalucía). Collectively, these results show that cave art in Iberia is older than 64.8 thousand years (ka). This cave art is the earliest dated so far and predates, by at least 20 ka, the arrival of modern humans in Europe, which implies Neandertal authorship."</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-58" id="cite_note-58" data-mw-footnote-number="57"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGdU"><a href="#cite_ref-58" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGdY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGdc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-58" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt179" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwGdg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Smith"},"first":{"wt":"Kiona N."},"date":{"wt":"2026-05-13"},"title":{"wt":"Neanderthals drilled cavities to treat a toothache 59,000 years ago"},"url":{"wt":"https://arstechnica.com/science/2026/05/neanderthals-drilled-cavities-to-treat-a-toothache-59000-years-ago/"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260514024222/https://arstechnica.com/science/2026/05/neanderthals-drilled-cavities-to-treat-a-toothache-59000-years-ago/"},"archive-date":{"wt":"2026-05-14"},"access-date":{"wt":"2026-06-05"},"work":{"wt":"[[Ars Technica]]"},"language":{"wt":"en-US"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFSmith2026" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt179">Smith, Kiona N. (13 May 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://arstechnica.com/science/2026/05/neanderthals-drilled-cavities-to-treat-a-toothache-59000-years-ago/" class="external text" id="mwGdk">"Neanderthals drilled cavities to treat a toothache 59,000 years ago"</a>. <i id="mwGdo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ars_Technica" title="Ars Technica" id="mwGds">Ars Technica</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260514024222/https://arstechnica.com/science/2026/05/neanderthals-drilled-cavities-to-treat-a-toothache-59000-years-ago/" class="external text" 