 and sequencing of ancient DNA [... suggest] that dogs were domesticated in Siberia by ~23,000 y ago, possibly while both people and wolves were isolated during the harsh climate of the Last Glacial Maximum.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Proceedings+of+the+National+Academy+of+Sciences&amp;rft.atitle=Dog+domestication+and+the+dual+dispersal+of+people+and+dogs+into+the+Americas&amp;rft.volume=118&amp;rft.issue=6&amp;rft.artnum=e2010083118&amp;rft.date=2021&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov%2Fpmc%2Farticles%2FPMC8017920%23id-name%3DPMC&amp;rft_id=info%3Apmid%2F33495362&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1073%2Fpnas.2010083118&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F2021PNAS..11810083P&amp;rft.aulast=Perri&amp;rft.aufirst=Angela+R.&amp;rft.au=Feuerborn%2C+Tatiana+R.&amp;rft.au=Frantz%2C+Laurent+A.+F.&amp;rft.au=Larson%2C+Greger&amp;rft.au=Malhi%2C+Ripan+S.&amp;rft.au=Meltzer%2C+David+J.&amp;rft.au=Witt%2C+Kelsey+E.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fora.ox.ac.uk%2Fobjects%2Fuuid%3Ae31cc7b2-7912-47ac-89f5-ebc883f31160&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt251" id="mwGyE"></span></span></li>
