<li about="#cite_note-Radner-167" id="cite_note-Radner-167" data-mw-footnote-number="165"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHzo"><a href="#cite_ref-Radner_167-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHzs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHzw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Radner-167" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt509" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwHz0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"author1":{"wt":"Karen Radner"},"url":{"wt":"https://archive.org/details/oxfordhandbookcu00radn"},"title":{"wt":"The Oxford Handbook of Cuneiform Culture"},"author2":{"wt":"Eleanor Robson"},"date":{"wt":"22 September 2011"},"publisher":{"wt":"Oxford University Press"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-19-955730-1"},"pages":{"wt":"[https://archive.org/details/oxfordhandbookcu00radn/page/n117 86]"},"url-access":{"wt":"limited"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFKaren_RadnerEleanor_Robson2011" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt509">Karen Radner; Eleanor Robson (22 September 2011). <span class="id-lock-limited" title="Free access subject to limited trial, subscription normally required" id="mwHz4"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://archive.org/details/oxfordhandbookcu00radn" class="external text" id="mwHz8"><i id="mwH0A">The Oxford Handbook of Cuneiform Culture</i></a></span>. Oxford University Press. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwH0E"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://archive.org/details/oxfordhandbookcu00radn/page/n117" class="external text" id="mwH0I">86</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwH0M">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwH0Q"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-19-955730-1" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-19-955730-1" id="mwH0U"><bdi id="mwH0Y">978-0-19-955730-1</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+Oxford+Handbook+of+Cuneiform+Culture&amp;rft.pages=86&amp;rft.pub=Oxford+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2011-09-22&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-19-955730-1&amp;rft.au=Karen+Radner&amp;rft.au=Eleanor+Robson&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.org%2Fdetails%2Foxfordhandbookcu00radn&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt509" id="mwH0c"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-168" id="cite_note-168" data-mw-footnote-number="166"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwH0g"><a href="#cite_ref-168" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwH0k"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwH0o">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-168" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">"The world's earliest known writing systems emerged at more or less the same time, around 3300 bc, in Egypt and Mesopotamia (today's Iraq)."<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt512" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwH0s" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Before the Pyramids: The Origins of Egyptian Civilization"},"last":{"wt":"Teeter"},"first":{"wt":"Emily"},"publisher":{"wt":"Oriental Institute of the University of Chicago"},"year":{"wt":"2011"},"page":{"wt":"99"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFTeeter2011" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt512">Teeter, Emily (2011). <i id="mwH0w">Before the Pyramids: The Origins of Egyptian Civilization</i>. Oriental Institute of the University of Chicago. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwH00"> </span>99.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Before+the+Pyramids%3A+The+Origins+of+Egyptian+Civilization&amp;rft.pages=99&amp;rft.pub=Oriental+Institute+of+the+University+of+Chicago&amp;rft.date=2011&amp;rft.aulast=Teeter&amp;rft.aufirst=Emily&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt512" id="mwH04"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-169" id="cite_note-169" data-mw-footnote-number="167"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwH08"><a href="#cite_ref-169" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwH1A"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwH1E">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-169" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">"Although it was once thought that the idea of writing came to Egypt from Mesopotamia, recent discoveries indicate that writing arose first in Egypt."<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt515" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwH1I" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Middle Egyptian: An Introduction to the Language and Culture of Hieroglyphs"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=lF78Max-h8MC&amp;q=recent+discoveries+indicate+writing"},"last":{"wt":"Allen"},"first":{"wt":"James P."},"publisher":{"wt":"Cambridge University Press"},"year":{"wt":"2010"},"page":{"wt":"2"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-1-139-48635-4"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFAllen2010" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt515">Allen, James P. (2010). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=lF78Max-h8MC&amp;q=recent+discoveries+indicate+writing" class="external text" id="mwH1M"><i id="mwH1Q">Middle Egyptian: An Introduction to the Language and Culture of Hieroglyphs</i></a>. Cambridge University Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwH1U"> </span>2. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwH1Y">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwH1c"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-139-48635-4" title="Special:BookSources/978-1-139-48635-4" id="mwH1g"><bdi id="mwH1k">978-1-139-48635-4</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Middle+Egyptian%3A+An+Introduction+to+the+Language+and+Culture+of+Hieroglyphs&amp;rft.pages=2&amp;rft.pub=Cambridge+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2010&amp;rft.isbn=978-1-139-48635-4&amp;rft.aulast=Allen&amp;rft.aufirst=James+P.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DlF78Max-h8MC%26q%3Drecent%2Bdiscoveries%2Bindicate%2Bwriting&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt515" id="mwH1o"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-170" id="cite_note-170" data-mw-footnote-number="168"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwH1s"><a href="#cite_ref-170" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwH1w"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwH10">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-170" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">"and examples of writing in Egypt have been found that very well may pre-date the earliest writing from Mesopotamia."<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt518" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwH14" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Boudreau"},"first1":{"wt":"Vincent"},"title":{"wt":"The First Writing: Script Invention as History and Process"},"date":{"wt":"2004"},"publisher":{"wt":"Cambridge University Press"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-521-83861-0"},"page":{"wt":"71"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=jsWL_XJt-dMC&amp;pg=PA71"},"language":{"wt":"en"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBoudreau2004" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt518">Boudreau, Vincent (2004). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=jsWL_XJt-dMC&amp;pg=PA71" class="external text" id="mwH18"><i id="mwH2A">The First Writing: Script Invention as History and Process</i></a>. Cambridge University Press. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwH2E"> </span>71. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwH2I">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwH2M"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-521-83861-0" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-521-83861-0" id="mwH2Q"><bdi id="mwH2U">978-0-521-83861-0</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+First+Writing%3A+Script+Invention+as+History+and+Process&amp;rft.pages=71&amp;rft.pub=Cambridge+University+Press&amp;rft.date=2004&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-521-83861-0&amp;rft.aulast=Boudreau&amp;rft.aufirst=Vincent&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DjsWL_XJt-dMC%26pg%3DPA71&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt518" id="mwH2Y"></span></span></li>
