<li about="#cite_note-217" id="cite_note-217" data-mw-footnote-number="213"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIUU"><a href="#cite_ref-217" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIUY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIUc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-217" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt684" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIUg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Rao"},"date":{"wt":"July 1992"},"title":{"wt":"A Navigational Instrument of the Harappan Sailors"},"url":{"wt":"http://drs.nio.org/drs/bitstream/handle/2264/3082/J_Mar_Archaeol_3_61.pdf?sequence=2"},"journal":{"wt":"Marine Archaeology"},"volume":{"wt":"3"},"pages":{"wt":"61–66"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRao1992" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt684">Rao (July 1992). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://drs.nio.org/drs/bitstream/handle/2264/3082/J_Mar_Archaeol_3_61.pdf?sequence=2" class="external text" id="mwIUk">"A Navigational Instrument of the Harappan Sailors"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwIUo">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwIUs">Marine Archaeology</i>. <b id="mwIUw">3</b>: <span class="nowrap" id="mwIU0">61–</span>66.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Marine+Archaeology&amp;rft.atitle=A+Navigational+Instrument+of+the+Harappan+Sailors&amp;rft.volume=3&amp;rft.pages=61-66&amp;rft.date=1992-07&amp;rft.au=Rao&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fdrs.nio.org%2Fdrs%2Fbitstream%2Fhandle%2F2264%2F3082%2FJ_Mar_Archaeol_3_61.pdf%3Fsequence%3D2&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt684" id="mwIU4"></span> Notes: protractor described as "compass" in article.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-218" id="cite_note-218" data-mw-footnote-number="214"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIU8"><a href="#cite_ref-218" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIVA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIVE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-218" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt687" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIVI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Pingree"},"first":{"wt":"David"},"author-link":{"wt":"David Pingree"},"editor":{"wt":"Stephanie Dalley"},"editor-link":{"wt":"Stephanie Dalley"},"title":{"wt":"The Legacy of Mesopotamia"},"year":{"wt":"1998"},"publisher":{"wt":"Oxford University Press"},"location":{"wt":"Oxford"},"isbn":{"wt":"0-19-814946-8"},"pages":{"wt":"125–126"},"chapter":{"wt":"Legacies in Astronomy and Celestial Omens"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFPingree1998" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt687"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Pingree" title="David Pingree" id="mwIVM">Pingree, David</a> (1998). "Legacies in Astronomy and Celestial Omens". In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephanie_Dalley" title="Stephanie Dalley" id="mwIVQ">Stephanie Dalley</a> (ed.). <i id="mwIVU">The Legacy of Mesopotamia</i>. Oxford: Oxford University Press. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwIVY"> </span><span class="nowrap" id="mwIVc">125–</span>126. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwIVg">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwIVk"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-19-814946-8" title="Special:BookSources/0-19-814946-8" id="mwIVo"><bdi id="mwIVs">0-19-814946-8</bdi></a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=Legacies+in+Astronomy+and+Celestial+Omens&amp;rft.btitle=The+Legacy+of+Mesopotamia&amp;rft.place=Oxford&amp;rft.pages=125-126&amp;rft.pub=Oxford+University+Press&amp;rft.date=1998&amp;rft.isbn=0-19-814946-8&amp;rft.aulast=Pingree&amp;rft.aufirst=David&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt687" id="mwIVw"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-219" id="cite_note-219" data-mw-footnote-number="215"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIV0"><a href="#cite_ref-219" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIV4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIV8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-219" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt690" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIWA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"first":{"wt":"N. Kameswara"},"last":{"wt":"Rao"},"date":{"wt":"December 2005"},"title":{"wt":"Aspects of prehistoric astronomy in India"},"journal":{"wt":"Bulletin of the Astronomical Society of India"},"volume":{"wt":"33"},"issue":{"wt":"4"},"pages":{"wt":"499–511"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.ncra.tifr.res.in/~basi/05December/3305499-511.pdf"},"access-date":{"wt":"11 May 2007"},"quote":{"wt":"It appears that two artifacts from Mohenjadaro and Harappa might correspond to these two instruments. Joshi and Parpola (1987) lists a few pots tapered at the bottom and having a hole on the side from the excavations at Mohenjadaro (Figure 3). A pot with a small hole to drain the water is very similar to clepsydras described by Ohashi to measure the time (similar to the utensil used over the lingum in Shiva temple for abhishekam)."},"bibcode":{"wt":"2005BASI...33..499R"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRao2005" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt690">Rao, N. Kameswara (December 2005). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.ncra.tifr.res.in/~basi/05December/3305499-511.pdf" class="external text" id="mwIWE">"Aspects of prehistoric astronomy in India"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwIWI">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwIWM">Bulletin of the Astronomical Society of India</i>. <b id="mwIWQ">33</b> (4): <span class="nowrap" id="mwIWU">499–</span>511. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)" title="Bibcode (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwIWY">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2005BASI...33..499R" class="external text" id="mwIWc">2005BASI...33..499R</a><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIWg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIWk">11 May</span> 2007</span>. <q id="mwIWo">It appears that two artifacts from Mohenjadaro and Harappa might correspond to these two instruments. Joshi and Parpola (1987) lists a few pots tapered at the bottom and having a hole on the side from the excavations at Mohenjadaro (Figure 3). A pot with a small hole to drain the water is very similar to clepsydras described by Ohashi to measure the time (similar to the utensil used over the lingum in Shiva temple for abhishekam).</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Bulletin+of+the+Astronomical+Society+of+India&amp;rft.atitle=Aspects+of+prehistoric+astronomy+in+India&amp;rft.volume=33&amp;rft.issue=4&amp;rft.pages=499-511&amp;rft.date=2005-12&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F2005BASI...33..499R&amp;rft.aulast=Rao&amp;rft.aufirst=N.+Kameswara&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ncra.tifr.res.in%2F~basi%2F05December%2F3305499-511.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt690" id="mwIWs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-220" id="cite_note-220" data-mw-footnote-number="216"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIWw"><a href="#cite_ref-220" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIW0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIW4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-220" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">David S. Anthony, <i id="mwIW8">The Horse, The Wheel and Language: How bronze age riders from the Eurasian steppes shaped the modern world</i> (2007), pp. 397-405.</span></li>
