/span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)" title="S2CID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLm4">S2CID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLm8"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:25341056" class="external text" id="mwLnA">25341056</a>. <q id="mwLnE">The first packet-switching network was implemented at the National Physical Laboratories in the United Kingdom. It was quickly followed by the ARPANET in 1969.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Communications+of+the+ACM&amp;rft.atitle=Notable+computer+networks&amp;rft.volume=29&amp;rft.issue=10&amp;rft.pages=932-971&amp;rft.date=1986&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1145%2F6617.6618&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A25341056%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft.aulast=John+S&amp;rft.aufirst=Quarterman&amp;rft.au=Josiah+C%2C+Hoskins&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdoi.org%2F10.1145%252F6617.6618&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1635" id="mwLnI"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-577" id="cite_note-577" data-mw-footnote-number="570"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLnM"><a href="#cite_ref-577" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLnQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLnU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-577" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1638" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLnY" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite AV media ","href":"./Template:Cite_AV_media"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.inc.com/computerfreaks"},"title":{"wt":"Computer Freaks"},"date":{"wt":"June 22, 2023"},"last":{"wt":"Haughney Dare-Bryan"},"first":{"wt":"Christine"},"type":{"wt":"Podcast"},"publisher":{"wt":"Inc. Magazine"},"series":{"wt":"Chapter Two: In the Air"},"minutes":{"wt":"35:55"},"quote":{"wt":"Leonard Kleinrock: Donald Davies ... did make a single node packet switch before ARPA did"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFHaughney_Dare-Bryan2023" class="citation audio-visual cs1" about="#mwt1638">Haughney Dare-Bryan, Christine (22 June 2023). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.inc.com/computerfreaks" class="external text" id="mwLnc"><i id="mwLng">Computer Freaks</i></a> (Podcast). Chapter Two: In the Air. Inc. Magazine.  35:55 minutes in. <q id="mwLnk">Leonard Kleinrock: Donald Davies ... did make a single node packet switch before ARPA did</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Computer+Freaks&amp;rft.series=Chapter+Two%3A+In+the+Air&amp;rft.pub=Inc.+Magazine&amp;rft.date=2023-06-22&amp;rft.aulast=Haughney+Dare-Bryan&amp;rft.aufirst=Christine&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.inc.com%2Fcomputerfreaks&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" clas