<li about="#cite_note-Abbate20002-578" id="cite_note-Abbate20002-578" data-mw-footnote-number="571"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLns"><a href="#cite_ref-Abbate20002_578-0" id="mwLnw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLn0">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Abbate20002_578-1" id="mwLn4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLn8">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Abbate20002-578" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1641" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLoA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite book ","href":"./Template:Cite_book"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Abbate"},"first1":{"wt":"Jane"},"author-link":{"wt":"Janet Abbate"},"url":{"wt":"https://books.google.com/books?id=E2BdY6WQo4AC&amp;q=packet+switching&amp;pg=PA125"},"title":{"wt":"Inventing the Internet"},"date":{"wt":"2000"},"publisher":{"wt":"MIT Press"},"isbn":{"wt":"978-0-262-26133-3"},"pages":{"wt":"37–8, 58–9"},"quote":{"wt":"The NPL group influenced a number of American computer scientists in favor of the new technique, and they adopted Davies&apos;s term \"packet switching\" to refer to this type of network. Roberts also adopted some specific aspects of the NPL design."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFAbbate2000" class="citation book cs1" about="#mwt1641"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janet_Abbate" title="Janet Abbate" id="mwLoE">Abbate, Jane</a> (2000). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://books.google.com/books?id=E2BdY6WQo4AC&amp;q=packet+switching&amp;pg=PA125" class="external text" id="mwLoI"><i id="mwLoM">Inventing the Internet</i></a>. MIT Press. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLoQ"> </span><span class="nowrap" id="mwLoU">37–</span>8, <span class="nowrap" id="mwLoY">58–</span>9. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)" title="ISBN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLoc">ISBN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLog"> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-262-26133-3" title="Special:BookSources/978-0-262-26133-3" id="mwLok"><bdi id="mwLoo">978-0-262-26133-3</bdi></a>. <q id="mwLos">The NPL group influenced a number of American computer scientists in favor of the new technique, and they adopted Davies's term "packet switching" to refer to this type of network. Roberts also adopted some specific aspects of the NPL design.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Inventing+the+Internet&amp;rft.pages=37-8%2C+58-9&amp;rft.pub=MIT+Press&amp;rft.date=2000&amp;rft.isbn=978-0-262-26133-3&amp;rft.aulast=Abbate&amp;rft.aufirst=Jane&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbooks.google.com%2Fbooks%3Fid%3DE2BdY6WQo4AC%26q%3Dpacket%2Bswitching%26pg%3DPA125&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1641" id="mwLow"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:2-579" id="cite_note-:2-579" data-mw-footnote-number="572"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLo0"><a href="#cite_ref-:2_579-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLo4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLo8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:2-579" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1644" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLpA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Roberts"},"first1":{"wt":"Dr. Lawrence G."},"date":{"wt":"November 1978"},"title":{"wt":"The Evolution of Packet Switching"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.ismlab.usf.edu/dcom/Ch10_Roberts_EvolutionPacketSwitching_IEEE_1978.pdf"},"journal":{"wt":"Proceedings of the IEEE"},"volume":{"wt":"66"},"issue":{"wt":"11"},"page":{"wt":"1307"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1109/PROC.1978.11141"},"bibcode":{"wt":"1978IEEEP..66.1307R"},"access-date":{"wt":"10 September 2017"},"quote":{"wt":"In nearly all respects, Davies&apos; original proposal, developed in late 1965, was similar to the actual networks being built today."},"archive-date":{"wt":"31 December 2018"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20181231092936/http://www.ismlab.usf.edu/dcom/Ch10_Roberts_EvolutionPacketSwitching_IEEE_1978.pdf"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRoberts1978" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt1644">Roberts, Dr. Lawrence G. (November 1978). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20181231092936/http://www.ismlab.usf.edu/dcom/Ch10_Roberts_EvolutionPacketSwitching_IEEE_1978.pdf" class="external text" id="mwLpE">"The Evolution of Packet Switching"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwLpI">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwLpM">Proceedings of the IEEE</i>. <b id="mwLpQ">66</b> (11): 1307. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)" title="Bibcode (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLpU">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1978IEEEP..66.1307R" class="external text" id="mwLpY">1978IEEEP..66.1307R</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLpc">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1109%2FPROC.1978.11141" class="external text" id="mwLpg">10.1109/PROC.1978.11141</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.ismlab.usf.edu/dcom/Ch10_Roberts_EvolutionPacketSwitching_IEEE_1978.pdf" class="external text" id="mwLpk">the original</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwLpo">(PDF)</span> on 31 December 2018<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLps">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLpw">10 September</span> 2017</span>. <q id="mwLp0">In nearly all respects, Davies' original proposal, developed in late 1965, was similar to the actual networks being built today.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Proceedings+of+the+IEEE&amp;rft.atitle=The+Evolution+of+Packet+Switching&amp;rft.volume=66&amp;rft.issue=11&amp;rft.pages=1307&amp;rft.date=1978-11&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1109%2FPROC.1978.11141&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F1978IEEEP..66.1307R&amp;rft.aulast=Roberts&amp;rft.aufirst=Dr.+Lawrence+G.&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ismlab.usf.edu%2Fdcom%2FCh10_Roberts_EvolutionPacketSwitching_IEEE_1978.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1644" id="mwLp4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-580" id="cite_note-580" data-mw-footnote-number="573"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLp8"><a href="#cite_ref-580" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLqA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLqE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-580" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1647" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLqI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Computer Pioneers - Donald W. Davies"},"url":{"wt":"https://history.computer.org/pioneers/davies.html"},"access-date":{"wt":"2020-02-20"},"website":{"wt":"IEEE Computer Society"},"quote":{"wt":"The design of the ARPA network (ArpaNet) was entirely changed to adopt this technique."},"postscript":{"wt":"none"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1647" id="mwLqM"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://history.computer.org/pioneers/davies.html" class="external text" id="mwLqQ">"Computer Pioneers - Donald W. Davies"</a>. <i id="mwLqU">IEEE Computer Society</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLqY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLqc">20 February</span> 2020</span>. <q id="mwLqg">The design of the ARPA network (ArpaNet) was entirely changed to adopt this technique.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=IEEE+Computer+Society&amp;rft.atitle=Computer+Pioneers+-+Donald+W.+Davies&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fhistory.computer.org%2Fpioneers%2Fdavies.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1647" id="mwLqk"></span>; <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1649" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLqo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Donald Davies"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.internethalloffame.org/inductees/donald-davies"},"access-date":{"wt":"20 April 2022"},"website":{"wt":"www.internethalloffame.org"},"quote":{"wt":"the ARPANET received his network design enthusiastically and the NPL local network became the first two computer networks in the world using the technique."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1649" id="mwLqs"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.internethalloffame.org/inductees/donald-davies" class="external text" id="mwLqw">"Donald Davies"</a>. <i id="mwLq0">www.internethalloffame.org</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLq4">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLq8">20 April</span> 2022</span>. <q id="mwLrA">the ARPANET received his network design enthusiastically and the NPL local network became the first two computer networks in the world using the technique.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=www.internethalloffame.org&amp;rft.atitle=Donald+Davies&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.internethalloffame.org%2Finductees%2Fdonald-davies&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1649" id="mwLrE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:5-581" id="cite_note-:5-581" data-mw-footnote-number="574"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLrI"><a href="#cite_ref-:5_581-0" id="mwLrM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLrQ">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-:5_581-1" id="mwLrU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLrY">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:5-581" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1652" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLrc" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"The real story of how the Internet became so vulnerable"},"language":{"wt":"en-US"},"newspaper":{"wt":"Washington Post"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.washingtonpost.com/sf/business/2015/05/30/net-of-insecurity-part-1/"},"access-date":{"wt":"18 February 2020"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20150530231409/http://www.washingtonpost.com/sf/business/2015/05/30/net-of-insecurity-part-1/"},"archive-date":{"wt":"30 May 2015"},"quote":{"wt":"Historians credit seminal insights to Welsh scientist Donald W. Davies and American engineer Paul Baran"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1652" id="mwLrg"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20150530231409/http://www.washingtonpost.com/sf/business/2015/05/30/net-of-insecurity-part-1/" class="external text" id="mwLrk">"The real story of how the Internet became so vulnerable"</a>. <i id="mwLro">Washington Post</i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.washingtonpost.com/sf/business/2015/05/30/net-of-insecurity-part-1/" class="external text" id="mwLrs">the original</a> on 30 May 2015<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLrw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLr0">18 February</span> 2020</span>. <q id="mwLr4">Historians credit seminal insights to Welsh scientist Donald W. Davies and American engineer Paul Baran</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Washington+Post&amp;rft.atitle=The+real+story+of+how+the+Internet+became+so+vulnerable&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonpost.com%2Fsf%2Fbusiness%2F2015%2F05%2F30%2Fnet-of-insecurity-part-1%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1652" id="mwLr8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-582" id="cite_note-582" data-mw-footnote-number="575"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLsA"><a href="#cite_ref-582" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLsE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLsI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-582" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1657" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLsM" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.computerhistory.org/siliconengine/microprocessor-integrates-cpu-function-onto-a-single-chip/"},"title":{"wt":"1971: Microprocessor Integrates CPU Function onto a Single Chip &amp;#124; the Silicon Engine &amp;#124; Computer History Museum"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1657" id="mwLsQ"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.computerhistory.org/siliconengine/microprocessor-integrates-cpu-function-onto-a-single-chip/" class="external text" id="mwLsU">"1971: Microprocessor Integrates CPU Function onto a Single Chip <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLsY">|</span> the Silicon Engine <span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLsc">|</span> Computer History Museum"</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=1971%3A+Microprocessor+Integrates+CPU+Function+onto+a+Single+Chip+%26%23124%3B+the+Silicon+Engine+%26%23124%3B+Computer+History+Museum&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.computerhistory.org%2Fsiliconengine%2Fmicroprocessor-integrates-cpu-function-onto-a-single-chip%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1657" id="mwLsg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-computerhistory.org-583" id="cite_note-computerhistory.org-583" data-mw-footnote-number="576"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLsk"><a href="#cite_ref-computerhistory.org_583-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLso"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLss">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-computerhistory.org-583" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1660" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLsw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"http://www.computerhistory.org/revolution/memory-storage/8/261"},"title":{"wt":"Floppy Disks - CHM Revolution"},"website":{"wt":"www.computerhistory.org"},"access-date":{"wt":"October 6, 2017"},"archive-date":{"wt":"2017-01-03"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20170103071537/http://www.computerhistory.org/revolution/memory-storage/8/261"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1660" id="mwLs0"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.computerhistory.org/revolution/memory-storage/8/261" class="external text" id="mwLs4">"Floppy Disks - CHM Revolution"</a>. <i id="mwLs8">www.computerhistory.org</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20170103071537/http://www.computerhistory.org/revolution/memory-storage/8/261" class="external text" id="mwLtA">Archived</a> from the original on 3 January 2017<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLtE">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLtI">6 October</span> 2017</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=www.computerhistory.org&amp;rft.atitle=Floppy+Disks+-+CHM+Revolution&amp;rft_id=http%