<li about="#cite_note-HilbertLopez2011-584" id="cite_note-HilbertLopez2011-584" data-mw-footnote-number="577"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLtQ"><a href="#cite_ref-HilbertLopez2011_584-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLtU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLtY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-HilbertLopez2011-584" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.1200970" class="external text" id="mwLtc">"The World's Technological Capacity to Store, Communicate, and Compute Information"</a>, Martin Hilbert and Priscila López (2011), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_(journal)" title="Science (journal)" id="mwLtg">Science</a>, 332(6025), 60-65; free access to the article through here martinhilbert.net/WorldInfoCapacity.html</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-585" id="cite_note-585" data-mw-footnote-number="578"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLtk"><a href="#cite_ref-585" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLto"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLts">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-585" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">Nick Taylor. Laser: The Inventor, the Nobel Laureate, and the Thirty-Year Patent War. Simon &amp; Schuster. 2000</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-586" id="cite_note-586" data-mw-footnote-number="579"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLtw"><a href="#cite_ref-586" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLt0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLt4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-586" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1666" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLt8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Cerf"},"first1":{"wt":"V."},"last2":{"wt":"Kahn"},"first2":{"wt":"R."},"date":{"wt":"1974"},"title":{"wt":"A Protocol for Packet Network Intercommunication"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/fall06/cos561/papers/cerf74.pdf"},"journal":{"wt":"IEEE Transactions on Communications"},"volume":{"wt":"22"},"issue":{"wt":"5"},"pages":{"wt":"637–648"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1109/TCOM.1974.1092259"},"bibcode":{"wt":"1974ITCom..22..637C"},"issn":{"wt":"1558-0857"},"quote":{"wt":"The authors wish to thank a number of colleagues for helpful comments during early discussions of international network protocols, especially R. Metcalfe, R. Scantlebury, D. Walden, and H. Zimmerman; D. Davies and L. Pouzin who constructively commented on the fragmentation and accounting issues; and S. Crocker who commented on the creation and destruction of associations."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCerfKahn1974" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt1666">Cerf, V.; Kahn, R. (1974). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/fall06/cos561/papers/cerf74.pdf" class="external text" id="mwLuA">"A Protocol for Packet Network Intercommunication"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwLuE">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwLuI">IEEE Transactions on Communications</i>. <b id="mwLuM">22</b> (5): <span class="nowrap" id="mwLuQ">637–</span>648. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)" title="Bibcode (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLuU">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1974ITCom..22..637C" class="external text" id="mwLuY">1974ITCom..22..637C</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLuc">doi</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1109%2FTCOM.1974.1092259" class="external text" id="mwLug">10.1109/TCOM.1974.1092259</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLuk">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLuo"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/1558-0857" class="external text" id="mwLus">1558-0857</a>. <q id="mwLuw">The authors wish to thank a number of colleagues for helpful comments during early discussions of international network protocols, especially R. Metcalfe, R. Scantlebury, D. Walden, and H. Zimmerman; D. Davies and L. Pouzin who constructively commented on the fragmentation and accounting issues; and S. Crocker who commented on the creation and destruction of associations.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=IEEE+Transactions+on+Communications&amp;rft.atitle=A+Protocol+for+Packet+Network+Intercommunication&amp;rft.volume=22&amp;rft.issue=5&amp;rft.pages=637-648&amp;rft.date=1974&amp;rft.issn=1558-0857&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1109%2FTCOM.1974.1092259&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F1974ITCom..22..637C&amp;rft.aulast=Cerf&amp;rft.aufirst=V.&amp;rft.au=Kahn%2C+R.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cs.princeton.edu%2Fcourses%2Farchive%2Ffall06%2Fcos561%2Fpapers%2Fcerf74.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1666" id="mwLu0"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-:7-587" id="cite_note-:7-587" data-mw-footnote-number="580"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLu4"><a href="#cite_ref-:7_587-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLu8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLvA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-:7-587" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1669" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLvE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"30 November 2013"},"title":{"wt":"The internet&apos;s fifth man"},"newspaper":{"wt":"The Economist"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its"},"access-date":{"wt":"22 April 2020"},"issn":{"wt":"0013-0613"},"quote":{"wt":"In the early 1970s Mr Pouzin created an innovative data network that linked locations in France, Italy and Britain. Its simplicity and efficiency pointed the way to a network that could connect not just dozens of machines, but millions of them. It captured the imagination of Dr Cerf and Dr Kahn, who included aspects of its design in the protocols that now power the internet."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1669" id="mwLvI"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/news/technology-quarterly/21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its" class="external text" id="mwLvM">"The internet's fifth man"</a>. <i id="mwLvQ">The Economist</i>. 30 November 2013. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwLvU">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwLvY"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0013-0613" class="external text" id="mwLvc">0013-0613</a><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLvg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLvk">22 April</span> 2020</span>. <q id="mwLvo">In the early 1970s Mr Pouzin created an innovative data network that linked locations in France, Italy and Britain. Its simplicity and efficiency pointed the way to a network that could connect not just dozens of machines, but millions of them. It captured the imagination of Dr Cerf and Dr Kahn, who included aspects of its design in the protocols that now power the internet.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=The+internet%27s+fifth+man&amp;rft.date=2013-11-30&amp;rft.issn=0013-0613&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fnews%2Ftechnology-quarterly%2F21590765-louis-pouzin-helped-create-internet-now-he-campaigning-ensure-its&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1669" id="mwLvs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-588" id="cite_note-588" data-mw-footnote-number="581"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLvw"><a href="#cite_ref-588" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLv0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLv4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-588" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1672" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLv8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.ieee.org/about/awards/bios/environmental-safety-recipients.html"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20190325040102/https://www.ieee.org/about/awards/bios/environmental-safety-recipients.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"25 March 2019"},"title":{"wt":"IEEE Medal for Environmental and Safety Technologies Recipients"},"website":{"wt":"[[Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers]] (IEEE)"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1672" id="mwLwA"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20190325040102/https://www.ieee.org/about/awards/bios/environmental-safety-recipients.html" class="external text" id="mwLwE">"IEEE Medal for Environmental and Safety Technologies Recipients"</a>. <i id="mwLwI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Institute_of_Electrical_and_Electronics_Engineers" title="Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers" id="mwLwM">Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers</a> (IEEE)</i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.ieee.org/about/awards/bios/environmental-safety-recipients.html" class="external text" id="mwLwQ">the original</a> on 25 March 2019.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Institute+of+Electrical+and+Electronics+Engineers+%28IEEE%29&amp;rft.atitle=IEEE+Medal+for+Environmental+and+Safety+Technologies+Recipients&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ieee.org%2Fabout%2Fawards%2Fbios%2Fenvironmental-safety-recipients.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1672" id="mwLwU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-castel-589" id="cite_note-castel-589" data-mw-footnote-number="582"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLwY"><a href="#cite_ref-castel_589-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLwc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLwg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-castel-589" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1675" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLwk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"de Castella"},"first":{"wt":"Tom"},"date":{"wt":"28 April 2014"},"title":{"wt":"The people who are still addicted to the Rubik&apos;s Cube"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-27186297"},"access-date":{"wt":"28 April 2014"},"work":{"wt":"BBC News Magazine"},"publisher":{"wt":"BBC"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFde_Castella2014" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1675">de Castella, Tom (28 April 2014). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.bbc.com/news/magazine-27186297" class="external text" id="mwLwo">"The people who are still addicted to the Rubik's Cube"</a>. <i id="mwLws">BBC News Magazine</i>. BBC<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLww">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLw0">28 April</span> 2014</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=BBC+News+Magazine&amp;rft.atitle=The+people+who+are+still+addicted+to+the+Rubik%27s+Cube&amp;rft.date=2014-04-28&amp;rft.aulast=de+Castella&amp;rft.aufirst=Tom&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.com%2Fnews%2Fmagazine-27186297&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ATimeline+of+historic+inventions" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1675" id="mwLw4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-590" id="cite_note-590" data-mw-footnote-number="583"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLw8"><a href="#cite_ref-590" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLxA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLxE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-590" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1678" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwLxI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Rye"},"first":{"wt":"Dave"},"date":{"wt":"October 1999"},"title":{"wt":"My Life at X10"},"url":{"wt":"http://hometoys.com/emagazine.php?url=/htinews/oct99/articles/rye/rye.htm"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20140930080338/http://hometoys.com/emagazine.php?url=%2Fhtinews%2Foct99%2Farticles%2Frye%2Frye.htm"},"archive-date":{"wt":"September 30, 2014"},"access-date":{"wt":"October 8, 2014"},"website":{"wt":"AV and Automation Industry eMagazine"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFRye1999" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1678">Rye, Dave (October 1999). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20140930080338/http://hometoys.com/emagazine.php?url=%2Fhtinews%2Foct99%2Farticles%2Frye%2Frye.htm" class="external text" id="mwLxM">"My Life at X10"</a>. <i id="mwLxQ">AV and Automation Industry eMagazine</i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://hometoys.com/emagazine.php?url=/htinews/oct99/articles/rye/rye.htm" class="external text" id="mwLxU">the original</a> on 30 September 2014<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLxY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLxc">8 October</span> 2014</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=AV+and+Automatio